 (473,473,'Unknown','JAMES','ANDERSON','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'3rd Regt.',1119,'1917-04-09','Killed in action, during first day of the Battle of Arras. The 3rd S.A.I. was on the right of the South African Infantry Brigade in the attack of Black Line and Blue Line (North of St Laurent-Blangy). The 3rd S.A.I. sustained 53 killed and 226 wounded','Son of William and Catharine Anderson, of 8 Halkett Road, Kimberley, Cape Province. His brother also died in service','France',27,'ROCLINCOURT VALLEY CEMETERY',2179,'50.33322','2.80449 ','IV. G. 13.',NULL,'J','7794','','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
