 (478,478,'Unknown','NEIL','ANDERSON','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'232 Sqdn.',769,'1942-03-06','Died of injuries, received March 4th in Batavia, Java, as a POW. Ten Hurricanes were ordered to attack Kalidjati airfield on 4/3/42. Anderson was one of 4 detailed to remain as top cover whilst 6 attacked the airfield. Eventually the 4 went down to add to the attack they were themselves attacked by Japanese fighters but pulled out and, as instructed, continued to Andir as their new base. Anderson didn&#39;t appear. He was taken prisoner but died in captivity 2 days later','Son of William and Nellie Anderson, of Hillview, P.O. Brooklyn, Pretoria. Born Johannesburg','Singapore',70,'SINGAPORE MEMORIAL',2302,'1.41847','103.75813 ','Column 424.',NULL,'N','103705V','21','',0,'',0,''),
