 (617,617,'Unknown','WILLIAM','APRIL','Fireman and Trimmer',245,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Henri Mory (Swansea)',2947,'1941-04-26','Killed in action. At 01.30 hours on 27 Apr, 1941, the Henri Mory (Master Joseph Havard) was hit by one torpedo from U-110 and sank about 330 miles west-northwest of Blaskets Islands, Ireland. The ship had been dispersed from convoy SL-68 on 21 March, went to Bermuda and then continued unescorted.','Born Cape Town. Coloured man. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1939-45','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 56.',NULL,'W','','46','London',1,'',0,''),
