 (739,739,'Unknown','LEVI','ATHINDWA','Native Scout Private',376,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'2nd Bn.',900,'1916-05-30','Killed in action. He was the only one of 300 troops of 2RR killed during an assault on the so-called German Bridge over the Pangani River, north west of Buiko.','Levi was definitely attached to 2RR, but no record has been found which gives the Battalion as the one that he was actually a member of. Capell&#39;s very accurate nominal roll only lists white soldiers, which may also suggest that the Battalion did not have any non-white members. ref. The 2nd Rhodesia Regiment in East Africa. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918.','Kenya',41,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'L','10','','Unknown',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',0,''),
