 (784,784,'Unknown','CECIL NOEL','AURET','Private',429,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1942-06-05','Killed in action, at Point 204. This little-known clash occurred in the Alem Hamza area of the Gazala Line. The single company involved suffered heavy casualties in a clash with Italian troops, six were killed.','Son of Henry Hugo Auret and Martha Elizabeth Auret (nee Marais). Husband of Mrs. A. G. Auret, all of Jones Avenue, Brakpan, Transvaal. Born Shamva, Southern Rhodesia. Employed as a Reduction Worker. Educated Rand Collieries School; General Botha Cadet Draft 1930-1. Cecil Noel Auret joined the Hogarth Line in 1932. On Mossel Bay War Memorial, Western Cape.','Libya',45,'KNIGHTSBRIDGE WAR CEMETERY, ACROMA',1344,'32.09586','23.71913 ','5. E. 11.',NULL,'C N','26160','26','',0,'',0,''),
