 (822,822,'Unknown','JACOBUS ADRIAAN JOHANNES','BAARD','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'Unknown',0,'1943-10-18','Died in Aircraft Accident, Magister I R1844, crashed near Woodborough, 3 miles northwest of Upavon . The crash was attributed to a stable yawing dive to which Magisters were prone when elevators are blanked by rudder when recovering from a stall or spin','Son of Jacobus Adriaan Johannes Baard and of Huibrecht Gertruida Christina Baard (nee Dippenaar), of Cape Town, South Africa. Born Moorreesburg. Educated Moorreesburg High School; Cadet Draft 1936-7. Jacobus Adriaan Johannes Baard became an apprentice with the Runciman Shipping Company after completing his course on General Botha, obtaining his Second Mate&#39;s certificate in 1941. He then joined the RAF and received his training in the USA, Canada and England, obtaining his wings in September 1943','United Kingdom',90,'UPAVON CHURCH CEMETERY',2573,NULL,NULL,'Row A. Grave 4.',NULL,'J A J','150369','22','Wiltshire',1,'',0,''),
 (823,823,'Unknown','JAMES IVAN','BAARS','Trooper',581,'Special Service Battalion, S.A. Forces',901,'Unknown',0,'1944-06-10','Killed in action, by Anti-Tank fire and shelling in the Viterbo Area. When the Regiment advanced at 0900 hours, they encountered the enemy in prepared positions. He was killed during the advance','Son of Ivan and Freda Baars, of 118A Sinoia Street, Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia. Born in Salisbury. An apprentice Panel Beater. He was unmarried.','Italy',39,'BOLSENA WAR CEMETERY',298,'42.58562','11.99863 ','II, C, 6.',NULL,'J I','SR/597879V','22','',0,'',0,''),
