 (899,899,'Unknown','ROY','BAILEY','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'31 (S.A.A.F.) Sqdn.',1002,'1944-10-12','Killed in action, Liberator B.VI KG999, 8 crew (1 RAF and 5 RAFVR), took off from Celone, Italy, for Partisan supply drop in Northern Italy, north of Turin at night in poor weather. The weather conditions were very poor with 10/10 cloud cover and the aircraft crashed into the mountains above Ala di Stura. At the time of the crash there was no reported flak or air opposition','ref. South African Roll of Honour 1939-45','Italy',39,'MILAN WAR CEMETERY',1672,'45.48499','9.10346 ','Coll. grave V. C. 1-8.',NULL,'R','1899465','','',0,'',0,''),
 (900,900,'Unknown','ROYAL HUBERT SILAS','BAILEY','Second Lieutenant',475,'Royal Marine Light Infantry',675,'1st R.M. Bn. R.N. Div.',554,'1918-01-05','Killed in action','Son of George H. and Mary Bailey. Husband of Ethel Bailey, of 28, St. Michael&#39;s Park, Bristol. Formerly 1838 & 165791 Corporal Roy Bailey, North Somerset Yeomanry. Served with Umvoti Mounted Rifles in German South West Africa; ex-No.21 Officer Cadet Bn. ; Commissioned Temporary 2nd Lieutenant RM 27/6/17 ; Draft for BEF 18/12/17, joined 1st RM Bn. 1/1/18-5/1/18 DD. 1st RM Bn. War Diary records 3/1/18:- "Temporary 2nd Lieutenant Bailey to 2/RMLI to be attached." & 5/1/18:- "Temporary 2nd Lieutenant Bailey missing, killed." & 19/1/18 near Villers Plouich:- "Body of Temporary 2nd Lieutenant Bailey recovered & interred at 57c.R.15.c.85.92. (or 50.0774, 3.1563)" ; b.12/1/1887 ; Married Ethel Jones 5/12/1915.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 1 A.',NULL,'R H S','','30','Somme',1,'',0,''),
