 (1000,1000,'Unknown','ALBERT','BALLOCH','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'44 Sqdn.',1207,'1945-02-03','Killed in action, Lancaster I SW251, Took off 1948 3 Feb 1945 from Spilsby on way to Karlsruhe','Son of Robert Howie Balloch and May Balloch, of Broken Hill, Northern Rhodesia. Entered Grey House in January, 1936. After passing his Junior Certificate examination in December, 1937, he left to take up employment in Northern Rhodesia. He attested in July, 1943, received preliminary training in Rhodesia, and proceeded overseas in December, 1943. On Plumtree School Roll of Honour.','Germany',29,'DURNBACH WAR CEMETERY',737,'47.77834','11.73354 ','Joint grave 1. D. 22-23.',NULL,'A','710349','22','Bad Tolz, Bayern',1,'',0,''),
