 (1010,1010,'Unknown','JOHN WALTON','BAMBER','Lieutenant',334,'King&#39;s Own Yorkshire Light Infantry',423,'10th Bn.',198,'1916-07-01','Killed in action, north west of Fricourt','Son of William and Bessie Bamber, of 128, Pietermaritz St., Pietermaritzburg, Natal, South Africa. Born Ladysmith, Natal. Present during the Siege of Ladysmith during Boer War. Was in Canterbury, England studying to be a priest when war broke out. On Maritzburg College cenotaph.','France',27,'GORDON DUMP CEMETERY, OVILLERS-LA BOISSELLE',965,'50.02056','2.70735 ','Sp. Mem. B. 12.',NULL,'J W','','29','Somme',1,'',0,''),
