 (1016,1016,'Unknown','FREDERICK MICHAEL BAMPFIELD','DUGGAN','Sergeant',492,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'Unknown',0,'1944-06-21','Killed in action, during shelling in the vicinity of Cetona, Italy. WR/DLR and RNC had moved up and through the town, expecting an enemy counter attack. Casualties were from heavy shelling by Artillery and enemy tanks situated near Sarteano.','Son of Capt. Frederick John Duggan, R.F.A., and Edith E. Richards (formerly Duggan), of Summerhill House, Mooi River, Natal. Born in Woolwich, England. A clerk.','Italy',39,'BOLSENA WAR CEMETERY',298,'42.58562','11.99863 ','II, B, 20.',NULL,'F M B','242188V','33','',0,'LG Sup 13 January 1944 pg. 275',0,''),
