 (1491,1491,'Unknown','BELEZA','MYENGWA','Private',429,'South African Native Labour Corps',830,'1st Coy.',538,'1916-11-27','Died of pneumonia, at No. 2 SA Native General Hospital, Le Havre.','Son of Beleza, of Tsolo, Eeastern Cape. ***Formerly buried in Bleville Communal Cemetery, Seine-Maritime, his remains were re-interred at the South African National Memorial at Delville Wood on 6 July 2014. He was the first black South African to die in France.','France',27,'THE SOUTH AFRICA DELVILLE WOOD COMMEMORATIVE MUSEUM',2841,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'B','3009','','Somme',1,'',0,''),
