 (1535,1535,'Unknown','ERNEST AUBREY BRISTER','BELT','Captain',115,'1st Reserve Brigade, S.A. Forces',52,'Unknown',0,'1943-07-01','Died of carcinoma of lung','Son of William Brister and Mary Elizabeth Belt, of Port Elizabeth.','South Africa',72,'PORT ELIZABETH (SOUTH END) CEMETERY',2014,'-33.97419','25.62525 ','Sec.B. C. of E. (Old). Grave 33C.',NULL,'E A B','179729','53','Eastern Cape',1,'MC with Coldstream Guards EG Sup 25 April 1918 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty when in charge of a sub-section of machine guns attached to an assaulting battalion. When the infantry were held up by a strong point he brought his guns within close range and effectively assisted in the &#64257;nal assault. Later, he was largely instrumental in the repulse of a counter-attack. He was instrumental in getting into action a captured enemy machine gun, which was used with great effect against the enemy"',0,''),
