 (1576,1576,'Unknown','HARLAND TREVOR','BENN','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'South African Air Force',775,'34 Sqdn.',1033,'1945-03-02','Killed in action, 8 crew (2 RAFVR), disappeared without trace while on a bombing raid on the marshalling yards at Porta Vescovo, in Verona East, in Liberator B24J Mk VI #EW207. MRES searched the area south of Verona after the war, without success. The presumed grave is stated as "Lake Comacchio" in the SAAF death register.','Son of Max and Sadie Benn, of Port Elizabeth, Cape Province, South Africa. ***Jewish','Malta',51,'MALTA MEMORIAL',1588,'35.8947','14.50783 ','Panel 19, Column 2.',NULL,'H T','542859V','20','',0,'',0,''),
 (1577,1577,'Unknown','LOUIS HENRY','BENN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Henry William and the late Maria Benn, of Calitzdorp, Cape Province. Nephew of Alfred Benn, of Draai Street, Oudtshoorn, Cape Province','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'L H','2535','20','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
 (1578,1578,'Unknown','PERCY LESLIE','BENN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Millicent Ann Benn, of Lady Frere, Cape Province, and the late J. A. H. Benn.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'P L','6727','18','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
