 (1582,1582,'Unknown','ARTHUR JOHN','BENNETT','Private',429,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1942-07-27','Died of wounds, received in operation in the vicinity of El Alamein. The Regiment had been tasked to lift an enemy minefield to create a gap for 69 Bde and an Armoured Bde to pass through. Casualties were inflicted by severe MG fire and artillery bombardment. He died later the same day from his wounds','Son of Mrs. Elisabeth Ann Bennett, of Wimbledon Road, Brixton, Johannesburg. Born in Johannesburg. A train conductor.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','IV. A. 23.',NULL,'A J','84563','21','',0,'',0,''),
 (1583,1583,'Unknown','ARTHUR WILLIAM FERGUSON','BENNETT','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1918-03-24','Killed in action, in Battle of Marrieres Wood','Husband of Agnes Marie Bennett, of 120, Victoria Avenue, Brakpan, Transvaal. His brother John Henry Ferguson also died in service. ***May have died of wounds 25-April-1918 and buried 1km east of Ferme de l&#39;Hospital close to the western edge of the Bois Marrieres north and south of the path from the Ferme de l&#39;Hospital to Bouchavesnes','France',27,'POZIERES MEMORIAL',2045,'50.03448','2.71475 ','Panel 97.',NULL,'A W F','13231','27','Somme',1,'',0,''),
