 (1606,1606,'Unknown','HARRY RANDALL','BENNEWITH','Ordinary Seaman',389,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. Vindictive',2361,'1918-04-23','Killed in action, at Zeebrugge. During the operation, Harry belonged to the fore gun crew aboard HMS Vindictive. It was reported in the Johannesburg Star that Harry and the entire gun crew was blown to pieces by German shell fire. Harry was fatally wounded by this shellfire. (ref. Paul Kendall : The Zeebrugge Raid - 1918.)','Son of William James Bennewith, of Pretoria, South Africa, formerly of Stratford, London, England, and the late Ada Bennewith','United Kingdom',90,'DOVER (ST. JAMES&#39;S) CEMETERY',691,'51.13704','1.31198 ','P. W. 60A',NULL,'H R','J/51070','18','Kent',75,'',75,'28th Coy.'),
