 (1612,1612,'Unknown','HUGH','BENSON','Corporal',166,'Royal Durban Light Infantry, S.A. Forces',656,'1st Bn.',528,'1944-07-12','Died whilst a POW','Son of William C. Benson and Marion F. Benson; husband of Mary H. Benson, of Edinburgh. Served in Boer War with Lovat Scouts, in 1906 Rebellion with Natal Police, with Natal Carbineers in German South West Africa, later as a Captain in Royal Horse Artillery in WW1. Turned down for active service in WW2 because of his age he persisted and got through with 1st RDLI. Taken prisoner at Tobruk.','Germany',29,'BERLIN 1939-1945 WAR CEMETERY',231,NULL,NULL,'10. K. 3.',NULL,'H','1864','62','Berlin, Berlin',1,'MID LG Sup 23 December 1918 pg. 15030',0,''),
