 (1786,1786,'Unknown','THOMAS WYBURN','BIDDLECOMBE','Commander',152,'Royal Australian Navy',648,'H.M.S. "Q27"',2245,'1917-03-13','Killed in action, North Atlantic, west of Ireland - torpedoed once by German "U-38". Q-ship "Warner" ("Q-27", cargo ship, 1, 300grt, 1911) was on an eastward course as a tempting U-boat target. She was torpedoed around 09.00hrs, going down in five minutes. Some of her survivors were picked up by British submarine "D.3"','Son of William and Amelia Biddlecombe, of Swallowfield, Reading, England; husband of Gertrude Mary Biddlecombe, of 50, Leopold St., South Yarra, Victoria, Australia. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','23',NULL,'T W','','36','Devon',546,'',546,'on loan to Royal Navy'),
