 (1835,1835,'Unknown','FRANK','BIRT','Bombardier',97,'South African Heavy Artillery',804,'74th Siege Bty.',1576,'1916-11-21','Died of wounds. The Battery was at Colincamp since the 7th October 1916 in a position really untenable for a heavy battery, without cover and a favourite target for the German artillery. On the 20th November, the enemy kept up a severe bombardment all day, and four gunners were killed (the three men buried at Courcelles and Bombardier Frank Birt buried in Couin British Cemetery).','Son of Charles John and Eliza Louise Birt; husband of Florence E. Birt, of 2, Cato Rd., Clapham, London. On Cape Town "Company Gardens" Artillery Memorial','France',27,'COUIN BRITISH CEMETERY',581,'50.13949','2.53331 ','VI. B. 7.',NULL,'F','673','35','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
 (1836,1836,'Unknown','LASCELLES WILLIAM','BIRT','Captain',115,'Oxford and Bucks Light Infantry',551,'1st/4th Bn.',594,'1917-10-01','Died of wounds','Son of the late Raymond John and Constance Hogarth Birt; husband of Winifred Birt, of 22, St. Mark&#39;s Court, Abercorn Place, St. John&#39;s Wood, London. Served in Thornycroft&#39;s Mounted Infantry in the South African Campaign. Mentioned in Despatches. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','Belgium',10,'MENDINGHEM MILITARY CEMETERY',1647,'50.89751','2.64207 ','VI. C. II.',NULL,'L W','','49','Poperinge, West-Vlaanderen',1,'',0,''),
 (1837,1837,'Unknown','JOHN','BIRTWHISTLE','Fourth Officer',265,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Designer (Liverpool)',2911,'1941-07-09','Whilst operating with Convoy OB-341 was torpedoed and sunk by U-98. En route Ellesmere Port for Table Bay. When serving as Third Officer on the SS Designer, which carried cargo of mines and torpedoes for the Persian Gulf, he lost his life when she was torpedoed and sunk off Freetown, West Africa, on 9 July 1941, the only survivors being six Lascars who were landed at Cape Town but later died, and a naval gunner, who was landed at Oporto.','Son of Henry and Mary Elizabeth Birtwhistle, of Pretoria, Transvaal, South Africa. Born Middlesbrough, England. Educated Hamilton School, Pretoria; Cadet Draft 1936-7. After completing his course in General Botha John Birtwhistle joined the Harrison Line. He was a member of the Boys&#39; Naval Brigade.','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 35.',NULL,'J','','20','London',1,'',0,''),
