 (1925,1925,'Unknown','ROBERT HENRY PETTIPLACE','BLANDY','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'3 Group',971,'1941-03-15','Killed in action, in Wellington W5644, delivery flight to Malta, shot down by Oblt Muncheberg of 7/JG26 NW of Gozo. He saw the crew getting into a dinghy but they were never found, and were presumed drowned','Son of John Carne and Stella Blandy, of Warm Baths, Transvaal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 31.',NULL,'R H P','83740','33','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
