 (2183,2183,'Unknown','NOBLE','BOSTANDER','Gunner',278,'Cape Corps, S.A. Forces',252,'Unknown',0,'1944-08-27','Shot by Germans on the same day, a SS unit, in search of two allied airmen hidden in Andeville, shot 17 men of the village','Son of Saul and Lena Bostander; husband of Liza Bostander, of Strydenburg, Cape Province, South Africa.','France',27,'ANDEVILLE COMMUNAL CEMETERY',74,'49.26009','2.15984 ','Mil. Plot. Grave 1.',NULL,'N','C/305181','32','Oise',287,'',287,'attd. 2 A.A. Regt. South African Artillery'),
 (2184,2184,'Unknown','ROBERT SOUTHEY','BOSTOCK','Lieutenant',334,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. Ark Royal',2261,'1940-06-13','Killed in action, after attacking the Scharnhorst. He was in a Skua aircraft involved in a dogfight with a Heinkel over Grotli in Norway on 27/4/1940. the Heinkel was shot down, but the engine also failed on the Skua, and Robert and his captain landed in deep snow near Grotli. They were found next day by a Norwegian ski patrol and returned to the UK. Later on 13/6/1940 he was in one of 6 Skuas of 800 Squadron which attacked the Scharnhorst. There were 15 Skuas in all, 8 of which were shot down. Robert was killed when his Skua was shot down returning to the aircraft carrier near Trondheim, Norway.','Son of Robert V. and Janet Bostock; husband of Catherine Grace Bostock (nee Watson). On war memorial for King Edward VII School, Johannesburg. ***The character Robert Smith in the movie &#39;Into the White&#39; is based on him','United Kingdom',90,'LEE-ON-SOLENT MEMORIAL',1450,'50.80618','-1.20828 ','Bay 1, Panel 2.',NULL,'R S','','29','Hampshire',112,'',112,'800 Sqdn.'),
 (2185,2185,'Unknown','JAMES DONALDSON','BOSWALL','Captain',115,'Seaforth Highlanders',752,'10th Bn.',198,'1915-06-06','Killed in action','Son of the late Maj. Gen. Roper Boswall and his wife Eleanor Macdonald, daughter of the late Alexander Brodie, of Edinburgh; husband of Theresa, daughter of the late Hormuzd Rassam. He was a Writer to the Signet. Served in the South African War in the C.I.V&#39;S. Obtained permanent post of mounted orderly to Lord Kitchener. Inspector of Police in Pretoria at the conclusion of the South African War. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','Turkey',87,'HELLES MEMORIAL',1115,'40.04545','26.17927 ','Panel 177.',NULL,'J D','','45','',0,'',256,'attd. 1st Bn. Essex Regiment'),
