 (2752,2752,'Unknown','DOUGLAS BURN BUCHAN','BROWN','Lieutenant',334,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. "Indefatigable."',2239,'1916-05-31','This was the first of the three British battlecruisers to be sunk at Jutland. She was struck by at least two salvoes from Hipper&#39;s battlecruisers around 15.58 on 31st May 1916. HMS Indefatigable was seen to sink by the stern, rolling over to port. There were two survivors from a crew of 1,019.','b. 12-June-1887. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','10.',NULL,'D B B','','28','Devon',1,'',0,''),
