 (2755,2755,'Unknown','DUNCAN MENZIES','BROWN','Lieutenant',334,'Royal Naval Reserve',681,'H.M.S. Camito',2274,'1941-05-06','Put in command of captured Italian tanker which was struct by torpedo and sunk. Reported missing, believed killed','Son of George Aichison and Catherine Berry Brown, of De Hoek, Cape Province, South Africa. Born Kirkcaldy, Scotland, 19 February 1915; ed. Rondebosch Boys&#39; High School; General Botha Cadet Draft 1931-2 (Junior Cadet Captain). Joined Ellerman Lines 1933-38, transferred to Bank Line. WWII posted to RNR as Sub-Lieutenant. Survivor of Auxiliary cruiser Foylebank. Transferred to Auxiliary cruiser HMS Camito as Lieutenant.','United Kingdom',90,'PORTSMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',2031,'50.78242','-1.09599 ','Panel 60, Column 1.',NULL,'D M','','26','Hampshire',1,'',0,''),
