 (2759,2759,'Unknown','EDWIN','BROWN','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1917-04-09','Killed in action, at Battle of Arras','Brother of No. 1899 Sergeant Dan Brown, SAMR, of Office of Police Establishment 5th Regt. SAMR, Kuruman. Born Lymm, Cheshire, England, 5 November 1890. Former South African Policeman','France',27,'HIGHLAND CEMETERY, ROCLINCOURT',1147,'50.33129','2.79653 ','I. B. 47.',NULL,'E','508','26','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
 (2760,2760,'Unknown','ERIC GEORGE','BROWN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of Ernest Clement and Margaret Sarah Brown, of Raglan Farm, Waku Rail, Cathcart, Cape Province.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'E G','2129','27','Somme',19,'',19,'"D" Coy.'),
