 (2771,2771,'Unknown','HENRY','BROWN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-07-16','Killed in action, at Delville Wood. Brigadier-General Lukin was ordered to support the attack of the 11th Royal Scots [27th Brigade] on the orchard, situated in the northern sector of Longueval, between North Street and Flers Road. The Scots would attack along North Street while B and C Companies of the 1st SAI would attack northwards in the wood, parallel to the Royal Scots. The South African attack also failed. The enemy fire scythed down the advancing troops.','Friend of Henry Liddle, of Chester Street, Rondebosch, Cape Town','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'H','3856','','Somme',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
