 (2823,2823,'Unknown','SAMUEL','BROWN','Private',429,'Imperial Light Horse/Kimberley Regiment, S.A.Forces',393,'Unknown',0,'1944-08-02','Killed in action, during the advance on Impruneta. He was shot by a sniper at close range','Son of William Samuel and Kathleen Brown, of 14 Jackel Street, Kensington, Johannesburg. Born in Johannesburg. An assistant timekeeper. He was unmarried. Commemoration stone in Johannesburg (West Park) Cemetery.','Italy',39,'FLORENCE WAR CEMETERY',866,'43.77016','11.34284 ','III. D. 18.',NULL,'S','225743V','20','',0,'',0,''),
