 (2844,2844,'Unknown','ZANE','BROWN','Private',429,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'Unknown',0,'1944-11-08','Died of wounds, shell wound left shoulder and left upper chest. He was wounded on 10 October during a counter-attack on the RNC positions on Mount Stanco, Italy, by elements of the 16th SS Division. After being hospitalised, he appeared to be on the mend but relapsed on the 6 November and died 2 days later','Son of Frederick Raymond and Phoebe Annie Brown, of 17 Bonvista Mansions, Twist Street, Johannesburg. Born in Durban. Enlisted direct from school. He was unmarried.','Italy',39,'NAPLES WAR CEMETERY',1765,'40.88539','14.23985 ','IV.A. 14.',NULL,'Z','233077V','19','',0,'',0,''),
