 (2866,2866,'Unknown','ALEXANDER MORRISON','BRUCE','Stoker 2nd Class',540,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Dorsetshire',2284,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. DORSETSHIRE and her sister ship Cornwall were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of Robert Dalgety and Annie Isabella Bruce, of Mowbray, Cape Town, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'A M','67907','21','Devon',1,'',0,''),
