 (2941,2941,'Unknown','ALEXANDER ROSS','BUCKLE','Second Lieutenant',475,'Army Service Corps',184,'attd. YMCA Field Force Canteens',1931,'1920-04-23','Died of cancer of the tongue, at Kimberley','Husband of Mary Ann Buckle, of P.O. Box 48, Bloemhof, Transvaal. Served in GSWA in South African Army Service Corps. Joined CAHTC as Sergeant 16-May-1917, and posted to No. 7 Coy 18-May-1917. To Army Service Corps (BEF) 10-June-1918. Disembarked at Cape Town on HMT Ingoma 9-August-1919. Released from service 12-August-1919 at Maitland. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','South Africa',72,'KIMBERLEY (WEST END) CEMETERY',1296,'-28.73608','24.73764 ','Death certificate states buried in Kimberley (West End) Cemetery',NULL,'A R','','43','Northern Cape',1,'***Accepted by CWGC for War Grave Status & burial site under investigation',0,''),
