 (2999,2999,'Unknown','GEORGE WILLIAM','BUNN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'3rd Regt.',1119,'1916-08-01','Declared missing in action, on the 1st August 1916, fighting in Delville Wood','Only son of Police Superintendent John Bunn, of 39, North St., March, Cambs, England. Wounded and missing 16-7-16, died 1-8-16, age 32. Apprenticed to Chatteris Engineering Works and went with machinery from the factory to work for the owners of the New Premier Mine in South Africa. In South Africa 11 years when war declared and enlisted in army.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'G W','1645','32','Somme',6,'',6,'"A" Coy.'),
