 (3171,3171,'Unknown','GEORGE BARCLAY','BUXTON','Second Lieutenant',475,'Royal Flying Corps',661,'1st Sqdn.',572,'1917-07-28','Killed in action, Nieuport 17 # A6680, last seen being driven down with 4EA on tail','Son of Reverend Barclay Fowell Buxton and Margaret Maria Amelia Railton. b. 16 October 1892. Fought in British East Africa, Egypt and France.He gained the rank of 2nd Lieutenant in the service of the 5th Battalion, Norfolk Regiment. He gained the rank of 2nd Lieutenant in the service of the Royal Flying Corps. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','France',27,'ARRAS FLYING SERVICES MEMORIAL',95,'50.287','2.76039 ','',NULL,'G B','','24','Pas de Calais',146,'',146,'and 5th Bn. Norfolk Regiment'),
