 (3349,3349,'Unknown','STANLEY HALL ELPHINSTONE','CAPSTICK-DALE','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Air Force',775,'Unknown',0,'1944-07-24','Died in Aircraft Accident, Typhoon JP847, spun in whilst with 3 Tactical Exercise Unit','Son of Lieut.-Comdr. E. J. (James Ernest) Capstick-Dale, and of (Ellen Marguerit) Marjorie Capstick-Dale; stepson of Mr. D. Stant, of Chingola, Northern Rhodesia. Born Sydney, New South Wales, Australia. Educated Marist Bros. College Observatory, Johannesburg. General Botha Cadet Draft 1938-9. Joined the RN at the outbreak of war as a Midshipman and served in HMS Carnarvon Castle and HMS Shropshire. In January 1942 he joined th SAAF as a pupil pilot, receiving his &#39;wings&#39; in July 1943.','United Kingdom',90,'OXFORD (BOTLEY) CEMETERY',1898,'51.7519','-1.29295 ','Plot I/2. Grave 247.',NULL,'S H E','328461','22','Oxfordshire',1,'',0,''),
