 (3401,3401,'Unknown','DOUGLAS GRAHAM','CARNEGIE','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 2nd SAI, who went in 400 strong, lost 16 officers and 285 men.','Son of Jemima Camegie, of Groutville, North Coast, Natal, South Africa, and the late David Piper Carnegie. His two brothers also died on service. Commemoration stone in Durban (West Street) Cemetery. Born at Durban.','France',27,'BROWN&#39;S COPSE CEMETERY, ROEUX',371,'50.30288','2.88379 ','II. B. 12.',NULL,'D G','9391','26','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
 (3402,3402,'Unknown','ROBERT GRAHAM GORDON','CARNEGIE','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Missing in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of Jemima Carnegie, of Groutville, North Coast, Natal, South Africa, and the late David Piper Carnegie. His two brothers also died on service. Commemoration stone in Durban (West Street) Cemetery. Born at Durban.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'R G G','8022','18','Somme',19,'',19,'"D" Coy.'),
 (3403,3403,'Unknown','THEODORE ARTHUR','CARNEGIE','Lieutenant',334,'King&#39;s Royal Rifle Corps',424,'12th Bn.',307,'1917-08-16','Killed in action, gallantly leading his company when hit by a machine gun bullet','Son of the Revd. David and Mary Margaret (nee Sykes) Carnegie, of Bulawayo, Rhodesia. Born Hope, Orange Free State. Was a Beit Bursary holder and a Rhodes&#39; scholar. A Rhodes Scholar University College 1915. On Milton High School Bulawayo war memorial. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','Belgium',10,'TYNE COT MEMORIAL',2552,'50.88745','3.00051 ','Panel 115 to 119 and 162A and 163A.',NULL,'T A','','21','Zonnebeke, West-Vlaanderen',1,'',0,''),
