 (3464,3464,'Unknown','ALFRED SAMUEL','CARTER','Sub-Lieutenant',552,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M. Submarine Triton',2210,'1942-11-28','Reported missing, presumed killed, in the loss of the Greek submarine Triton.','Son of Victor Charles and Rosina Letitia Carter (nee Dicks). Husband of M. Carter, of Durban, Natal, South Africa. Born Ladysmith, Natal, 22 March 1920; ed. Mansfield Road School, Durban; General Botha Cadet Draft 1934-5. In 1936 Alfred Samuel Carter joined the Bank Line, and in 1941 became a Sub-Lieutenant in the Seaward Defence Force, where he remained for a year. He then joined the RNR, was afterwards transferred to the SANFVR.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 1.',NULL,'A S','330689','22','Devon',1,'',0,''),
