 (3483,3483,'Unknown','RICHARD ROTHWELL','CARTER','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 4th SAI lost 6 officers and 200 men.','Son of Anna Margaret Carter, of Corner of Inglis and Ludlaw St., Seatoun, Wellington, New Zealand, and the late Richard Carter.','France',27,'ARRAS MEMORIAL',96,'50.28697','2.76065 ','Bay 10.',NULL,'R R','3742','39','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
