 (3926,3926,'Unknown','DESMOND DE VILLIERS','CLARKE','Flying Officer',259,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'Unknown',0,'1944-09-08','Died in Aircraft Accident, Wellington BK552, training flight, cross country navigation exercise. Severe icing took place during the sortie, possibly rendering one engine unserviceable. The pilot lost control and the aircraft ploughed into the ground at 1343.','Of South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'CHESTER (BLACON) CEMETERY',520,'53.20537','-2.90908 ','Sec. A. Grave 103.',NULL,'D D V','160076','','Cheshire',1,'',0,''),
