 (3969,3969,'Unknown','FREDERICK HOWARD','CLAYTON','Engine Room Artificer 4th Class',219,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Hermes',2305,'1942-04-09','Attacked by carrier-borne aircraft from a Japanese force of three battleships and five carriers which had entered the Bay of Bengal a week before. Around seventy bombers were sent to dispatch the Hermes which sank within ten minutes.','Son of Alfred Howard and Jessie Clayton, of Durban, Natal, South Africa; husband of Beryl Wilfred Freda Clayton, of Durban.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'F H','68102','29','Devon',1,'',0,''),
