 (4461,4461,'Unknown','JOSEPH JOHN','COOPER','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force',635,'106 Sqdn.',177,'1942-07-27','Killed in action, Lancaster R5748, took off on 26 July 1942 at 2330, a bombing raid over the city of Hamburg in Germany. The aircraft was shot down over Friesland by the German night fighter Lt. Lothar Linke, 11./NJG1, after that it crashed in Opeinde at 0205. In the crash, four crew members got killed','Son of Alfred John and Ann Frances Cooper, of Claremont, Cape Town, South Africa.','Netherlands',57,'SMALLINGERLAND (OPEINDE) PROTESTANT CEMETERY',2306,'53.13353','6.07461 ','Grave 3.',NULL,'J J','778188','21','',0,'',0,''),
