 (4798,4798,'Unknown','ARTHUR','CUMMINGS','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1917-10-16','Killed in action, probably near Bazentin le Grand','Guardian Mr. David Ballantyne of Hammonia, Orange Free State. Wounded at Delville Wood. Born in State of Washington, U.S.A.','Belgium',10,'TYNE COT CEMETERY',2551,'50.88699','2.99771 ','XXVIII. D. 24.',NULL,'A','4503','','Zonnebeke, West-Vlaanderen',1,'LG Sup 14 January 1918 - From original documents "Sir With reference to the recent action of 20th (September 1917) inst, I herewith beg to bring to your notice 4503 Sergeant Cummings, A. On taking control of B Company, I found that Sergt. Cummings had partly re-organised the Company, and was directing operations in a cool and excellent manner, B Coy left flank then being in the air. This N.C.O. took charge of the Company when all the Officers were incapacitated, and is consider deserving of some recognition. - Victor S. Dickerson 2/Lt"',0,''),
