 (5092,5092,'Unknown','ARTHUR WILLIAM BOWEN','DAVIES','Flight Lieutenant',253,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'123 Sqdn.',292,'1944-04-24','Killed in action, Hurricane IIC LB727, missing from sweep. Aircraft "Y". Rhubarb 1455-1645 Formation of three with F/O AT Grubb and FSgt K Jones. Second sortie of day for formation over Tulhial - Patharkandi and Manipur Road. Last seen RP1898 ref','Son of Stuart Gwyn Davies and Doreen Catherine Davies, of Belvedere, Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia. Entered Lloyd House in January 1936. After passing the Cambridge School Certificate examination in December 1939, he left Plumtree to take up employment with the Salisbury Municipality. He attested in April 1941, received preliminary training in Rhodesia, and proceeded to the Middle East in January 1942. On Plumtree School Roll of Honour.','Singapore',70,'SINGAPORE MEMORIAL',2302,'1.41847','103.75813 ','Column 431.',NULL,'A W B','80289','21','',0,'',0,''),
