 (5171,5171,'Unknown','ALEXANDER ANDREW MARSHALL','DAWBARN','Flight Lieutenant',253,'Royal Air Force',635,'312 (Czech) Sqdn.',1010,'1941-04-10','Killed in action, Hurricane I V7066, flying with Sgt Truhlar from 312 Sqn detachment at Penhros. The report claims they were intercepting a ME110 west of Bardsey Island','Son of Alex Proctor Dawbarn. Ed, Government High School, Standerton. Born Durban. Ex-Cadet of the South African Training Ship General Botha. Cadet Draft 1928-9. Alexander Dawbarn was employed as an electrician by Hubert Davies & Co. before the war and on the outbreak of hostilities joined the RAF and became a Pilot Officer. Shared a Ju-88 kill on March 14, 1941 with Sgt. Joseph Stehlik (both of 312 Sqn). Commemoration stone in Durban (Overport) (Old St. Thomas) Cemetery','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 29.',NULL,'A A M','40213','28','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
