 (5427,5427,'Unknown','LINDSAY','DE VILLIERS','Lieut-Commander',331,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. Hunter',2311,'1940-04-10','Killed in action, 1st Battle of Narvik, ship loss. During the first battle of Narvik, the destroyer HMS Hunter was hit by shellfire and set on fire, she was then torpedoed by the German destroyer Georg Thiele. Hunter was then rammed in the stern by HMS Hotspur and then sank, Hotspur was out of control after been hit by enemy shells','Son of James Henry and Marie Josephine de Villiers; husband of Pamela Margaret de Villiers, of Durban, Natal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 36, Column 1.',NULL,'L','','35','Devon',1,'',0,''),
