 (5965,5965,'Unknown','ROBERT GORDON','DOWNIE','Warrant Officer Class I',594,'East African Artillery',300,'56 Bty., 301 Field Regt.',1349,'1944-02-12','Lost in S.S. Khedive Ismail (London). Sailing on 6 February 1944 from Kilindini Harbour at Mombasa, Kenya to Colombo, Ceylon in Convoy KR-8, the SS Khedive Ismail was attacked by a B1 type Japanese submarine. The Khedive Ismail was hit by two torpedoes. 1297 perished','Son of the Hon. J. W. Downie and Clara Downie, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','Kenya',41,'EAST AFRICA MEMORIAL',741,'-1.30973','36.74866 ','Column 13.',NULL,'R G','X/45','25','',0,'',0,''),
