 (6022,6022,'Unknown','HARRY THACKWRAY','DRIVER','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 1st SAI lost 2 officers and 203 men.','Son of Charles Harry and Maria Boyes Driver; husband of Aurelia Alice Driver, of "Somerville," Main Rd., Rondebosch, Cape Province. Educated at St. Andrew&#39;s College, Grahamstown. On Rondebosch War Memorial in St. Paul&#39;s Anglican Churchyard. On Mossel Bay War Memorial, Western Cape','France',27,'BROWN&#39;S COPSE CEMETERY, ROEUX',371,'50.30288','2.88379 ','II. A. 8.',NULL,'H T','10054','35','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
