 (6224,6224,'Unknown','BEN IAN','DUFF','Lieutenant',334,'General List',338,'Unknown',0,'1944-03-02','Killed in action, in Burma','Son of Colin Eric and Elizabeth Shaw Duff, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia; husband of Jean Duff. He was born on January 2nd, 1918, and entered Lloyd House in January 1932. After leaving Plumtree in August 1936, he entered the Public Health Department of the Civil Service. He attested in September 1939, and almost immediately proceeded on commitment. On Plumtree School Roll of Honour.','Myanmar',55,'TAUKKYAN WAR CEMETERY',2474,'17.03567','96.13127 ','4. D. 21.',NULL,'B I','246163','26','',0,'',371,'attd. 4th Bn. Nigeria Regiment, R.W.A.F.F.'),
