 (6268,6268,'Unknown','JACK','DUNBAR','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'3rd Regt.',1119,'1916-10-19','Died of wounds, received in front the Butte de Warlencourt. In the night of the 12-13th October, the 3rd S.A.I. relieved the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. which had suffered heavily during the attack on Snag and Tail Trenches. A new trench (Pearse&#39;s Trench) was dug and a patrol was sent on reconnaissance on The Pimple in the hands of the Germans. On the 14th October, the B Coy took The Pimple and a considerable part of the German communication trench. The B Coy was relieved by the A Coy in the night of the 15-16th October. The casualties of the 3rd S.A.I. amounted to 38 men. During the night of the 18-19th October, a company of the 3rd S.A.I. moved forward to the front line in Pearse&#39;s Trench.','Sister of Miss A. Watson, of 9 Hay Street, Operton, Johannesburg','France',27,'DERNANCOURT COMMUNAL CEMETERY EXTENSION',649,'49.97684','2.62496 ','III. H. 6.',NULL,'J','2278','','Somme',1,'',0,''),
