 (6334,6334,'Unknown','CHARLES CECIL WILLIAM PETER','DUTTON','Stoker 2nd Class',540,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Cornwall',2279,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. CORNWALL and her sister ship Dorsetshire were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. C. L. L&#39;B. Dutton, of Hout Bay, Cape Province, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'C C W P','68949','29','Devon',2,'',0,''),
