 (6424,6424,'Unknown','NICHOLAS','EDDY','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'3rd Regt.',1119,'1916-10-15','Killed in action. On the 14th October, the B Coy took The Pimple and a considerable part of the German communication trench. The B Coy was relieved by the A Coy in the night of the 15-16th October. The casualties of the 3rd S.A.I. amounted to 38 men.','Son of Annie Eddy, of 43 Trelowarren, Camborne, Cornwall, England','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','VIII. G. 13.',NULL,'N','9153','','Pas de Calais',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
