 (6528,6528,'Unknown','CHARLES FREDERICK','ELGAR','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-16','Died of wounds, received in front the Butte de Warlencourt. On the 12th October, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Husband of Lily Elgar, of 25 Bridge Street, Port Elizabeth','France',27,'DERNANCOURT COMMUNAL CEMETERY EXTENSION',649,'49.97684','2.62496 ','III. G. 9.',NULL,'C F','7842','','Somme',1,'',0,''),
