 (6895,6895,'Unknown','JACK','FALKSON','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force',635,'263 Sqdn.',840,'1940-06-08','Lost in H.M.S. Glorious, Falkson took part in the successful evacuation of fighters from Narvik on 8 June 1940 when he and nine other pilots from 263 Squadron landed their Gladiators aboard HMS Glorious. However this successful evacuation was to no avail when the carrier was sunk by the German battlecruisers Scharnhorst and Gneisenau later in the day with the loss of almost all aboard','Son of Ahron and Elizabeth Falkson, of Durban North, Natal, South Africa. Born Durban. Credited with 1 shared biplane victory. ***Jewish','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 8.',NULL,'J','41688','26','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
