 (6953,6953,'Unknown','ROBERT JAMES','FAULL','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'South African Air Force',775,'34 Sqdn.',1033,'1945-03-02','Killed in action, 8 crew (2 RAFVR), disappeared without trace while on a bombing raid on the marshalling yards at Porta Vescovo, in Verona East, in Liberator B24J Mk VI #EW207. MRES searched the area south of Verona after the war, without success. The presumed grave is stated as "Lake Comacchio" in the SAAF death register.','Son of Charles Arthur and Annie Ruchellina Faull, of Newlands, Cape Town, South Africa.','Malta',51,'MALTA MEMORIAL',1588,'35.8947','14.50783 ','Panel 19, Column 2.',NULL,'R J','607376V','18','',0,'',0,''),
