 (7047,7047,'Unknown','WILLIAM','FERGUSON','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Missing in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Husband of Mary Ferguson, of 99 English Street, Dunfries, Scotland','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'W','8031','','Somme',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
