 (7054,7054,'Unknown','ROBERTSON MALCOLM','FERNIE','First Radio Officer',248,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Grelhead (London)',2940,'1941-12-02','At 0119, 2 miles of the Atlantic coast of Morocco, U-562 sinks British SS Grelhead carrying 6900 tons of iron ore (41 killed, 2 survivors make land). At 2033 just East of Gibraltar, U-557 sinks Norwegian SS Fjord carrying 5900 tons of iron ore (14 killed, 22 survivors reach the Spanish coast on 2 rafts)','Son of Lt.-Col. Ralph Fernie and Ursula Maude Fernie; stepson of Elizabeth Fernie, of Thorpe, Norwich. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1939-45','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 53.',NULL,'R M','','36','London',1,'',0,''),
