 (7226,7226,'Unknown','BASIL JOHN INGLEBY','FLACK','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of Mrs. Caroline Louisa Flack, of 213, Burger St., Pietermaritzburg, Natal, and the late P. Paterson Flack. Played rugby for Natal in 1911. His brother also died on service. Fought in Delville Wood in July 1916','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'B J I','','29','Somme',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (7227,7227,'Unknown','BRIAN RUSSELL','FLACK','Gunner',278,'South African Artillery',784,'2 Field Regt.',632,'1944-09-27','Killed in action. In the North Italian village of Carpane on 27 September 1944 the Germans executed 16 Allied soldiers captured fighting with Italian partisans in that area. He was captured in the Middle East on 20 June 1942. Escaped with other South Africans from a nearby POW camp and joined up with local partisans to carry on fighting the Germans. They became such a thorn in the flesh of the Germans that a special operation was mounted in the Monte Grappa region to capture them. They were eventually captured and murdered by the Germans. Every year on this day since the end of the war the villagers of Carpane have held a memorial service at this spot by the side of the road where they were killed. For many years the identity of the 16 was not known and the monument was simply inscribed to "16 unknown". It was only about 4 or 5 years ago that their identity was uncovered by Sonia Residori, an Italian academic researcher','Son of Brian Victor Hugh and Maude Eliza Flack, of 337 Alexander Road, Pietermaritzburg. Born Pietermaritzburg. A bus driver. He was unmarried. His brother also died on service','Italy',39,'PADUA WAR CEMETERY',1910,'45.42165','11.83996 ','Coll. grave I. B. 3-8.',NULL,'B R','144020V','32','',0,'',0,''),
