 (7439,7439,'Unknown','ADAM JOHANNES','FOURIE','Corporal',166,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1942-07-27','Killed in action, in an operation in the vicinity of El Alamein. The Regiment had been tasked to lift an enemy minefield to create a gap for 69 Bde and an Armoured Bde to pass through. Casualties were inflicted by severe MG fire and artillery bombardment','Son of Louis L. and Ida H. Fourie; husband of Sylvia M. Fourie, of Prince Alfred Street, Pietermaritzburg, Natal. Born in Boshoff, Orange Free State. A clerk for the South African Railways & Harbours. He had one child.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','IV. H. 24.',NULL,'A J','306','30','',0,'',0,''),
