 (7729,7729,'Unknown','JOHN SAMUEL','FRY','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1916-07-13','Killed in action, at Bernafay Wood, Somme','Son of Edward Henry and Getske Marke Petronella Fry, of 148, Esselen St., Pretoria, Transvaal. Educated at St. Andrew&#39;s College, Grahamstown. Born Pretoria, enlisted 7 September 1915, as a private, Commissioned 25 March 1916, sailed for France via Egypt January 1916, landed Marseilles 20-April-1916, posted to "B" Company. Medals on eBay July 2007 for 495 GBP','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'J S','','26','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
