 (7915,7915,'Unknown','HUGH JAMES','GATER','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'450 (R.A.A.F.) Sqdn.',3291,'1944-08-13','Killed in action, shot down, near Fano, Italy, during a bombing mission against German ack-ack. Gater probably tried to land with his plane shot. He had a wound on his head. Two days passed and finally the owner of that field (Mr. Castellani) buried Gater (Germans refused to do it).','Son of A. H. and Annie R. Gater, of Vereeniging, Transvaal, South Africa. ***Have war diary extract','Italy',39,'ANCONA WAR CEMETERY',71,'43.58699','13.52365 ','III. H. 16.',NULL,'H J','329000V','22','',0,'',0,''),
