 (7944,7944,'Unknown','JOHN HENRY','GAYNOR','Major',343,'South African Air Force',775,'2 Sqdn.',657,'1944-03-03','Killed in action, hit HT cables during ground attack mission near Carsoli, in Supermarine Spitfire Mk IX #MJ290','Son of John G. and Christianna M. Gaynor, of Johannesburg, Transvaal, South Africa.','Italy',39,'BEACH HEAD WAR CEMETERY, ANZIO',172,'41.48234','12.62499 ','XXII. G. 8.',NULL,'J H','205579V','27','',0,'DFC LG Sup 23 April 1943 pg. 1856 - "This officer is a fearless and resourceful fighter. He has led the squadron on many occasions, setting a most inspiring example. Captain Gaynor has destroyed at least four enemy aircraft, two of them on his first operational flight" MID LG Sup 1 January 1945 pg. 104',0,''),
