 (7971,7971,'Unknown','GEOFFREY CLIFFORD','GEERDTS','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'15 Sqdn.',378,'1943-10-28','Killed in action, missing from sweep over Aegean, in Martin Baltimore Mk III #FA659','Son of Clifford E. and Doris C. Geerdts, of Durban, Natal, South Africa.','Egypt',23,'ALAMEIN MEMORIAL',35,'30.83823','28.94696 ','Column 277.',NULL,'G C','102541V','21','',0,'',0,''),
 (7972,7972,'Unknown','CARL FREDERICK','GEERE','Major',343,'South African Air Force',775,'19 (R.A.F.) Sqdn.',492,'1944-10-30','Died in Aircraft Accident, crashed in mountainside near Isernia','Son of Lt.-Col. Petrus Geere and Martha Magdalena Geere, of Krugersdorp, Transvaal, South Africa; husband of Yvonne Reeves Geere, of Krugersdorp. Born Krugersdorp.','Italy',39,'CASSINO WAR CEMETERY',482,'41.47757','13.82728 ','II. B. 21.',NULL,'C F','102995V','27','',0,'OBE LG Sup 24 November 1944 pg. 5465 - "In August, 1944, Major Geere was giving dual instruction in an aircraft when it crashed, broke in two and burst into flames. Although injured, Major Geere was able to extricate himself from the wreckage but soon realised that his pupil had not got free. Despite exploding ammunition, and well knowing that the petrol tanks might blow up at any minute this officer re-entered the blazing fuselage, unfastened his companion&#39;s harness and took him to safety. In the process, Major Geere sustained burns on the face and arms but his prompt and courageous action saved the pupil&#39;s life"; DFC LG Sup 29 December 1944 pg. 5956 - "In recognition of gallantry and devotion to duty in the execution of air operations"',0,''),
 (7973,7973,'Unknown','SENDER','GEFFEN','Stoker 1st Class',539,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Dorsetshire',2284,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. DORSETSHIRE and her sister ship Cornwall were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of David and Etta Geffen, of Durban, Natal, South Africa. Attended Glenwood High School, Durban. ***Jewish','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'S','68035','27','Devon',1,'',0,''),
