 (8289,8289,'Unknown','REGINALD BULTITUDE','GODFREY','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 2nd SAI, who went in 400 strong, lost 16 officers and 285 men.','Son of Henry and Constance May Godfrey, of 26, Porter St., East London, South Africa. Born at Cape Town.','France',27,'POINT-DU-JOUR MILITARY CEMETERY, ATHIES',1993,'50.31377','2.83578 ','Sp. Mem. A. 1.',NULL,'R B','4605','','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
