 (8309,8309,'Unknown','PERCY CLARK','GOLD','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of David Dundas and Catherine Louisa Gold, of Franklin, East Griqualand, South Africa. Born "Glengarry", Umzimkulu District. Fought in Delville Wood in July 1916. On Mount Currie National Park Boy Scout War Memorial near Kokstad','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','Sp. Mem. 12.',NULL,'P C','3658','22','Pas de Calais',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
