 (8385,8385,'Unknown','JOHN DAVID','GOODSON','First Radio Officer',248,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Nancy Moller (London)',2983,'1944-03-18','Torpedoed and sunk by Japanese I-165. En route from Durban, South Africa to Colombo, Ceylon. I-165&#39;s commander LtCdr Shimizu ordered his crewmen to open fire on the MOLLER&#39;s survivors. Thirty-two are killed by machine-gun and pistol fire.','Son of John Augustus and Irene Goodson; husband of Vera Goodson, of Rosebank, Cape Town, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 71.',NULL,'J D','','25','London',2,'',0,''),
