 (8585,8585,'Unknown','TOM GORDON','GRANTHAM','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'65 Sqdn.',1469,'1942-04-27','Killed in action, "Circus 142" took place, the escort of eight Hurricane bombers who were attacking St. Omer aerodrome. Three sections &#39;Red&#39;, &#39;White&#39; and &#39;Blue&#39; made up 65 Squadron&#39;s section of the Wing, and consisted of both Rhodesian, Czech and British airmen. The Wing flew across the Channel at 15,000 ft, and when on approach to the target, they were attacked by 50-60 FW-190s. In the ensuing dogfight F/O. D. Davies, in Spitfire #W3461; P/O. Tom Grantham (s/n: 80281) flying Spitfire #BL442, and P/O. Frederick Haslett (s/n: 80143) in Spitfire #AB401, were all reported missing presumed dead. It was thought that both F/O. Davies and P/O. Grantham may have collided as they were together when they went down, P/O. Grantham was just 19 years of age.','Son of Tom and Ann Grantham, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','France',27,'LONGUENESSE (ST. OMER) SOUVENIR CEMETERY',1512,'50.73114','2.25023 ','Plot 8. Row A. Grave 21.',NULL,'T G','80281','19','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
