 (8610,8610,'Unknown','JAMES DE VILLIERS BROWSE','GRAY','Lieutenant',334,'Pretoria Regiment, S.A. Forces',566,'Unknown',0,'1944-06-30','Killed in action, near Chianciano, Italy. He, together with the B Squadron Commander and the Tech Advisor, were inspecting a broken down tank when a bomb fell near them, wounding Lt. Gray. A vehicle was fetched to transport him for medical attention but that too was was damaged by a bomb, killing Lt. Gray and wounding the B Squadron Commander, Major Buchanan','Son of Nicholas Browse and Johanna Jacoba Gray (nee de Villiers), of "Plaisir de Merle", Simondium, Paarl. Born Paarl. A Chartered Accountant. He was unmarried. Commemoration stone in Western Cape, Paarl District, Simondium, St. Georges Church Yard','Italy',39,'FOIANO DELLA CHIANA WAR CEMETERY',869,'43.2619','11.82189 ','I. L. 3.',NULL,'J D V B','15609V','32','',0,'',0,''),
