 (8613,8613,'Unknown','JAMES WILLIAM','GRAY','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'149 Sqdn.',366,'1942-08-29','Killed in action, Stirling N6081, Nuremburg. 159 aircraft despatched- incurred 23 losses. Low altitude attack. PFF used target indicators for the first time and were able to place them with great accuracy. Much damage in the Altstadt and the Nazi rally area in the south of the city, shot down by a night-fighter and crashed 34 km NE of Mannheim','Son of Alexander and Maria Magdalene Gray, of East London, Cape Province, South Africa. A Mining Engineer','Germany',29,'DURNBACH WAR CEMETERY',737,'47.77834','11.73354 ','2. D. 19.',NULL,'J W','922567','31','Bad Tolz, Bayern',1,'',0,''),
