 (8623,8623,'Unknown','WILLIAM JOHNSTON','GRAY','Captain',115,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-07-15','Killed in action, at Delville Wood','Son of the late Walter and Isabella J. Gray, of Helmsley, Highflats, Natal; husband of the late Irene Gray. Was survived by his only child, Jocelyn William Gladstone Gray. Also served in the South African Campaign (Anglo-Boer War) (Siege of Ladysmith), 1906 Natal Rebellion, German South West Africa, a Lieutenant with the 3rd Natal Mounted Rifles. Educated at Hilton College. ***Date of death might be 15-July-1916, Killed in action on the 15th July 1916 in Delville Wood. "Captain Gray of C Coy was killed, he was very much loved by his men, a great loss" (D. Brice-Bruce, quoted in Delville Wood of I. Uys).','France',27,'SUCRERIE MILITARY CEMETERY, COLINCAMPS',2429,'50.09567','2.62341 ','I. HH. 3.',NULL,'W J','','39','Somme',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
