 (8885,8885,'Unknown','ERNEST MELVILLE CHARLES','GUEST','Flight Lieutenant',253,'Royal Air Force',635,'53 Sqdn.',1333,'1943-10-04','Killed in action, Liberator GR.V BZ753, his aircraft and another aircraft were sent out on an anti-submarine patrol. They were attacked by six JU88s. The other aircraft sought the protection of the clouds but Melville decided to fight it out','Son of Colonel the Hon. Sir Ernest Lucas Guest, K.B.E., C.M.G., C.V.O., and Lady Edith May Guest, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia; husband of Kathrine Mary Guest, of Pannal, Yorkshire. On Ruzawi Preparatory School War Memorial, near Marandellas, Rhodesia. Remembered on Diocesan College Roll of Honour. He attended Diocesan College 1933-37. His uncle (WW1) and twin brother (WW2) also died in service','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 119.',NULL,'E M C','33501','23','Surrey',1,'LG 26 May 1942 pg. 2289 - "This officer has now completed over 1,000 hours operational flying. His qualities of endurance are phenomenal, his ability as a pilot is exceptional, and his devotion to duty is of the highest order. All his work has been done quietly and efficiently. He has set an excellent example to the younger pilots of the Squadron." MID LG 24 September 1941 pg. 5573, 2nd MID LG 11 June 1942 pg. 2519',0,''),
 (8886,8886,'Unknown','IVOR ARTHUR MELVILLE','GUEST','Lieutenant',334,'Cape Corps',251,'1st',515,'1917-11-06','Killed in action, at Mkungu (Lindi Area), while checking the advance of a vastly superior enemy force. His gun crew had become casualties and he was handling the gun himself when he was killed.','Son of H. N. and L. C. Guest; husband of Bertha Anne Guest, of Waterbury Rd., Plumstead, Cape Province, South Africa. Born at Klerksdorp, Transvaal, South Africa. His nephews both died in service in WW2','Tanzania',84,'DAR ES SALAAM WAR CEMETERY',619,'-6.77467','39.24463 ','6. F. 10.',NULL,'I A M','','','',0,'',0,''),
 (8887,8887,'Unknown','JOHN DESMOND THOMAS','GUEST','Second Lieutenant',475,'King&#39;s Royal Rifle Corps',424,'1st Bn.',528,'1941-11-21','Killed in action, enfilade fire from German anti-tank guns, while leading a platoon of "A" Company in a frontal assault across a landing-ground','Son of Colonel the Hon. Sir Ernest Lucas Guest, K.B.E., C.M.G., C.V.O., and Lady Edith May Guest, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia. Was granted a Rhodes Scholarship at Trinity College, Oxford. On Ruzawi Preparatory School War Memorial, near Marandellas, Rhodesia. Remembered on Diocesan College Roll of Honour. He attended Diocesan College 1933-37. His uncle (WW1) and twin brother (WW2) also died in service','Libya',45,'KNIGHTSBRIDGE WAR CEMETERY, ACROMA',1344,'32.09586','23.71913 ','10. G. 9.',NULL,'J D T','137267','21','',0,'',6,'"A" Coy.'),
