 (8961,8961,'Unknown','THOMAS GERALD','HACKNEY','Flying Officer',259,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'83 Sqdn.',1642,'1942-11-07','Killed in action, Lancaster 1 R5566, took off 2210 from Wyton. Believed to have crashed in the Mediterranean between Sore on the Italian mainland SSE of Genoa and Corsica','Son of Fred and Lilian Hackney, of Gwelo, Southern Rhodesia.','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 67.',NULL,'T G','80218','23','Surrey',1,'LG Sup 20 November 1942 pg. 5032 - "This officer has participated in numerous sorties, involving attacks on a wide range of enemy targets. He is a skilful pilot and a fine captain whose determined efforts have contributed in a large measure to the many successes obtained. In the recent attack on Genoa, Pilot Officer Hackney attacked his objective successfully and obtained a photograph."',0,''),
