 (8963,8963,'Unknown','DACRE LOVETT','HADDON','Lieutenant',334,'Pretoria Regiment, S.A. Forces',566,'Unknown',0,'1944-07-06','Killed in action, during enemy shelling of the tank harbour positions near Villa a Sesta, Italy','Son of Hugh Evelyn and Isabel Annie Goddart (nee Lovett) Haddon, of "Fairseat", Alexandria Road, Kenilworth, Cape Town. Born Cape Town. A student. He was unmarried. Dacre Haddon from Diocesan College, Rondebosch region was named a Rhodes Scholar to Trinity College in 1941/2. Remembered on Diocesan College Roll of Honour. He attended Diocesan College 1930-39.','Italy',39,'FLORENCE WAR CEMETERY',866,'43.77016','11.34284 ','XI. G. 8.',NULL,'D L','110032V','22','',0,'',0,''),
