 (9158,9158,'Unknown','JOHN','HARBORD','Captain',115,'Norfolk Yeomanry',531,'Unknown',0,'1918-07-10','Died of wounds, received near Nieppe Forest, 6th July.','Son of Philip and Elinor Julia Harbord, of Northwold Lodge, Brandon, Norfolk. Native of Norfolk. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','France',27,'LES BARAQUES MILITARY CEMETERY, SANGATTE',1459,'50.96004','1.82406 ','IV. C. 7.',NULL,'J','','24','Pas de Calais',1,'LG Sup 26 July 1918 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty during an attack. He showed great courage and determination while leading his company, in face of heavy fire, over difficult country. He shot three of the enemy and took an officer and three men prisoners."',0,''),
