 (9350,9350,'Unknown','JOHN GERRARD (JEAN GERARD)','HARTER','Apprentice',66,'Merchant Navy',474,'M.V. Congella (London)',2544,'1943-10-24','Killed in action, as the result of gunfire from an enemy (Japanese) submarine.','Born in Durban on the 11th October, 1924, the son of Raoul Raymond Harter and Helene Marguerite, nee Reid. Educated at Marist Brothers, Durban. After Bothie, in 1942, joined Andrew Weir & Co. Ex-cadet of South African Training Ship General Botha. On St. Henry&#39;s College (Marist Brothers Durban) Roll of Honour. Commemoration stone in DURBAN, Stellawood, Cemetery','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 31.',NULL,'J G','','19','London',1,'',0,''),
