 (9416,9416,'Unknown','FREDERICK SPEED','HASLETT','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'65 Sqdn.',1469,'1942-04-27','Killed in action, "Circus 142" took place, the escort of eight Hurricane bombers who were attacking St. Omer aerodrome. Three sections &#39;Red&#39;, &#39;White&#39; and &#39;Blue&#39; made up 65 Squadron&#39;s section of the Wing, and consisted of both Rhodesian, Czech and British airmen. The Wing flew across the Channel at 15,000 ft, and when on approach to the target, they were attacked by 50-60 FW-190s. In the ensuing dogfight F/O. D. Davies, in Spitfire #W3461; P/O. Tom Grantham (s/n: 80281) flying Spitfire #BL442, and P/O. Frederick Haslett (s/n: 80143) in Spitfire #AB401, were all reported missing presumed dead.','Son of Francis Andrew and Ivy Gertrude Haslett, of Bulawayo, Southern Rhodesia; husband of Joan Mary Haslett. His brother also died on service','France',27,'DUNKIRK TOWN CEMETERY',714,'51.03063','2.38967 ','Plot 2 Row 3 Grave 8.',NULL,'F S','80143','30','Nord',1,'',0,''),
