 (9513,9513,'Unknown','JAMES','HAYES','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 1st SAI lost 2 officers and 203 men.','Brother of Mrs. S. J. Van der Spuy, of 3, Beyens Rd., Woodstock, Cape Province.','France',27,'BROWN&#39;S COPSE CEMETERY, ROEUX',371,'50.30288','2.88379 ','II. B. 29.',NULL,'J','1144','','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
