 (9515,9515,'Unknown','JOHN CAROLIN','HAYES','Lieutenant',334,'Coldstream Guards',270,'2nd Bn.',900,'1918-11-19','Died of pneumonia, following wounds','Son of John Carolin Hayes and Grace Hayes (nee Harte), of Dublin. Surveyor to the British South African Coy., Northern Rhodesia.','France',27,'STE. MARIE CEMETERY, LE HAVRE',2386,'49.50429','0.13028 ','Div. 62. IV. C. 1.',NULL,'J C','','35','Seine-Maritime',1,'LG Sup 18 July 1918 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He showed great ability and initiative in a critical situation, when the flank of the battalion became exposed. Later, he showed splendid coolness and disregard of danger in organising the defence under intense fire, and directed the destruction of several enemy counter-attacks."',0,''),
