 (9521,9521,'Unknown','RICHARD THOMAS','HAYES','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Barham',2265,'1941-11-25','Killed in action, while steaming to cover an attack on Italian convoys, HMS Barham was hit by three torpedoes from the German submarine U-331. As she rolled over to port, her after magazines exploded and the ship quickly sank with the loss of over two-thirds of her crew','Husband of I. M. Hayes, of Observatory, Cape Town, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 58, Column 3.',NULL,'R T','68499','','Devon',1,'',0,''),
