 (9556,9556,'Unknown','WILLIAM','HEALY','Corporal',166,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 1st SAI lost 2 officers and 203 men.','Son of Edward Healy, of 25 Kloof Street, Cape Town','France',27,'ATHIES COMMUNAL CEMETERY EXTENSION',111,'50.30399','2.83734 ','A. 7.',NULL,'W','1106','','Pas de Calais',1,'LG Sup 22 Sept 1916 - "For conspicuous gallantry in action. He stuck to his gun after all the rest of the team had become casualties, and, when it jammed, repaired the damage under heavy fire and carried on single-handed during the whole night."',0,''),
