 (9705,9705,'Unknown','HUGO','HENNEBERG','Electrician',214,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Nova Scotia (Liverpool)',2987,'1942-11-28','Lost at sea on S. S. Nova Scotia, torpedoed and sunk by U-177. En route from Aden to Durban, South Africa. Carrying 6 passengers, 11 military and naval personnel, 134 South African guards and 765 Italian civil internees','ref. South African Roll of Honour 1939-45','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 74.',NULL,'H','','','London',1,'',0,''),
