 (9709,9709,'Unknown','ALWYN PETRUS','HENNING','Private',429,'Imperial Light Horse, S.A. Forces',392,'1st',515,'1942-03-18','Died of injuries, fractured femur and skull fracture. Picked up off the roadside, in the Alexandria area, on 20 October 1941. Although the No. 8 General Hospital tried to save his leg, it was amputated on 18 March and he died later the day at 22:10 Hrs, according to the Hospital Record Card','Son of Anna M. Henning, of 55 Pan Road, La Rochelle, Johannesburg. Born in Johannesburg. An Office worker. He was unmarried.','Egypt',23,'ALEXANDRIA (HADRA) WAR MEMORIAL CEMETERY',49,'31.20378','29.92303 ','1. C. 24.',NULL,'A P','26405','21','',0,'',0,''),
