 (9719,9719,'Unknown','ALFRED BEECH','HENRY','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of John and Emma Teale Henry, of 341, Lordsnip Lane, Dulwich, London, England.','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','I. G. 20.',NULL,'A B','8495','35','Pas de Calais',15,'',15,'"C" Coy.'),
