 (9899,9899,'Unknown','RALPH GRENFELL','HILL','Lieutenant',334,'King&#39;s African Rifles',419,'1st',515,'1917-02-19','Killed in action','Son of Charles Pascoe Grenfell Hill and Elle Josephine Hill, of 61, Old Park Rd., Palmers Green, London, England. British South Africa Police Attested: October 1912. On All Saints School, Bloxham Roll of Honour. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','Tanzania',84,'IRINGA CEMETERY',1204,'-7.77931','35.69981 ','IX. B. 3.',NULL,'R G','','24','',0,'LG Sup 17 April 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty in carrying out dangerous reconnaissances. On one occasion, accompanied by another man, he penetrated the enemy&#39;s position and captured an outpost, obtaining most valuable information, which enabled a successful attack to be made." MID LG Sup 25 September 1917 pg. 9942 as 1634 R G Hill BSAP; MID LG Sup 7 March 1918 pg. 2888',0,''),
