 (9923,9923,'Unknown','JOHN CLARKE','HILSON','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Husband of Lucy Helena Hilson, of Renfrew Street, Cambridge, East London, Cape Province. On Cambridge Town war memorial for 1914-18','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','VI. G. 6.',NULL,'J C','2179','','Pas de Calais',19,'LG Sup 22 Sept 1916 - "For conspicuous gallantry in action. He displayed great coolness under heavy fire, and did fine work throughout the operations."',19,'"D" Coy.'),
