 (10197,10197,'Unknown','CHARLES RICHARD','HONEY','Private',429,'Cape Town Highlanders, S.A. Forces',260,'Unknown',0,'1942-10-14','Died in Accident, 11 perished in the accident. Whilst clearing mines and transporting them to 3 South African Field Coy. It appears that one of the land mines had not been defused correctly and exploded on the back of the truck detonating the other mines and killing the 9 on the back of the truck plus the driver and passenger in the cab','Son of Charles Richard and Sarah Jane Honey; husband of Gwendoleen Doreen Honey, of 87 Fairview Avenue, Woodstock, Cape Province. Born Concordia, Cape Province. A refrigeration mechanic. He had 2 children.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','Coll. grave III. B. 22.',NULL,'C R','17826','29','',0,'',0,''),
