 (10216,10216,'Unknown','AUBREY CLAUDE','HOOK','Able Seaman',25,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Neptune',2332,'1941-12-19','Ran into an uncharted minefield in the Mediterranean off Tripoli, and sank with the loss of 764 officers and men.','Son of Richard William and Mary S. Hook; husband of Enid Olive (nee Eedes) Hook, of Mowbray, Cape Town, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 58, Column 3.',NULL,'A C','67862','31','Devon',1,'',0,''),
