 (10246,10246,'Unknown','REGINALD JOHN','HOPKINS','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'25 O.T.U.',809,'1941-12-23','Died in Aircraft Accident, Wellington DV422, training took off from RAF Edgehill for general handling practice. While demonstrating stalling and recovery the aircraft went into a dive and at 14:20 crashed and burned near Wild Spring Farm, Little Tew, 5 miles east-north-east of Chipping Norton with the loss of 6 crew','Son of Walter Henry and Christine Maria Hopkins; husband of Barbara Dawn Hopkins, of Manor Park, Essex. Of South Africa. Born Waku, Cape Province. Educated Cambridge High School; General Botha Cadet Draft 1932-3. (Junior Cadet Captain). Reginald John Hopkins joined the Thesen Line in 1934 as an Apprentice.','United Kingdom',90,'BROOKWOOD MILITARY CEMETERY',369,'51.30022','-0.64212 ','24. A. 11.',NULL,'R J','111240','24','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
