 (10271,10271,'Unknown','CECIL EDMUND','HORNE','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 4th SAI lost 6 officers and 200 men.','Son of Antoinette Horne, of Wortley, Wetson Rd., Wynberg, Cape Province, and the late J. Templer Horne. Commemoration stone in Kimberley (West End) Cemetery','France',27,'ARRAS MEMORIAL',96,'50.28697','2.76065 ','Bay 10.',NULL,'C E','9865','37','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
