 (10296,10296,'Unknown','LEONARD ARTHUR','HORSFALL','Gunner',278,'South African Heavy Artillery',804,'71st Siege Bty.',1550,'1917-07-23','Killed in action, at Croisilles, he was serving ammunition at the gun, when a shell burst a few yards away, and a splinter killed him instantly','Brother of E. R. Horsfall, of Station Colliery, Witbank, Transvaal. Born at Melbourne, Australia. 20th July 1874. Enrolled Melbourne Law School 1890. Cambridge-Street State School, Collingwood, of which his father was Headmaster; Scotch College; Ormond College; BA, LL.B. Melbourne; LL.B. Cape University; maiden fours 1894. After admission to Victorian bar, went to South Africa during Boer War and became Crown Prosecutor, and ultimately a Resident Magistrate on the Rand. Was given leave to enlist in August 1916, and joined 71st Siege Battery South African Heavy Artillery as Gunner; promoted Corporal; to France 1 January 1917; evacuated to hospital 14 June 1917; rejoined battery 9 July 1917. Commemoration stone in Florida Cemetery, Gauteng see http://www.law.unimelb.edu.au/index.cfm?objectid=6AC6C9D0-5555-11E2-BC960050568D0140','France',27,'CROISILLES BRITISH CEMETERY',595,'50.19483','2.87739 ','I. E. 1.',NULL,'L A','1057','43','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
