 (10330,10330,'Unknown','ERIC FREDERICK','HOUSEMAN','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'1675 Heavy Conversion Unit',426,'1945-07-19','Died in Aircraft Accident, Liberator B.VI EV817. Aircraft climbed to a height of 500 ft. immediately after taking off. It then began to lose height, before climbing again. What followed was the aircraft then made a steep diving turn to port, from which it crashed and then destroyed by fire. The cause of the erratic flying was not positively determined but may have been a faulty artificial horizon or simply poor instrument flying','Attended Glenwood High School, Durban','Egypt',23,'MOASCAR WAR CEMETERY',1680,'30.60251','32.22209 ','2. E. 11.',NULL,'E F','581301V','20','',0,'',0,''),
 (10331,10331,'Unknown','FRANK PERCY','HOUSHOLD','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of Mr. D. T. and Mrs. Elizabeth A. Houshold, of 195, Boshoff St., Pietermaritzburg, Natal, South Africa. On Maritzburg College cenotaph.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'F P','8464','34','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
