 (10375,10375,'Unknown','HORACE GEORGE','HOWE','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Dorsetshire',2284,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. DORSETSHIRE and her sister ship Cornwall were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of Archibald J. and Charlotte S. Howe, of Port Elizabeth, Cape Province, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'H G','68680','22','Devon',2,'',0,''),
