 (10399,10399,'Unknown','ADRIAN MORRISON','HOWIE','Major',343,'South African Veterinary Corps',867,'Unknown',0,'1943-03-03','Drowned, on S. S. Nirpura. At 23.22 hours on 3 Mar, 1943, U-160 made her first attack on the convoy DN-21 about 40 miles south of Port St.Johns, South Africa, sank the Harvey W. Scott and Nirpura and damaged the Tibia. 38 men from the Nirpura (Master Thomas George Hodgkinson) were lost and 88 (including the master) were picked up by the SAAF crash launch R-8 and landed at Durban.','Son of Thomas J. and Mary M. Howie; husband of Agnes M. N. Howie, of Plumstead, Cape Town, South Africa. M.R.C.V.S. Howie&#39;s Military Medals, including his O.B.E., are housed in the Museum at the Castle in Cape Town','Myanmar',55,'RANGOON MEMORIAL',2108,'17.03621','96.13212 ','Face 19.',NULL,'A M','P/130639','53','',0,'LG Sup 7 February 1919',0,''),
