 (10558,10558,'Unknown','NEIL ANDERSON','HUNTER','Sergeant',492,'Imperial Light Horse/Kimberley Regiment, S.A.Forces',393,'"C" Coy.',18,'1944-09-17','Killed in action, when "C" Coy was ordered to carry out a left flanking attack on Monte Bagno. He was hit by Spandau fire while attacking a strong point. His body was only recovered on the 20th, due to heavy undergrowth and the tactical situation','Son of George A. and Florence M. McC. Hunter, of 156 Fordyce Road, Walmer, Port Elizabeth, Cape Province. Born in Koffiefontein, Orange Free State. An office clerk. He was unmarried. His brother also died on service.','Italy',39,'CASTIGLIONE SOUTH AFRICAN CEMETERY',483,'44.14397','11.16183 ','III, B, 1.',NULL,'N A','31400V','28','',0,'',0,''),
