 (10890,10890,'Unknown','JOHN REGINALD MAURICE','JACOBS','Captain',115,'Imperial Light Horse, S.A. Forces',392,'2nd Bn.',900,'1942-10-24','Killed in action, during attack of second battle of Alamein. The ILH advance continued behind a terrific barrage and the enemy wire was found already blown by shell-fire. Until the last 600 yds of their advance, the battalion met little opposition, but then after they had made their way through an anti-personnel minefield and Capt Jacobs&#39; company was consolidating, he and a small detachment went forward to reconnoitre. While under enemy mortar and anti-tank fire, Capt. Jacobs was shot and killed by rifle fire from a German anti-tank position not 20 yds away from him.','Son of Reginald Samuel and Irma Jacobs, of Denton Nurseries, Denton, Northamptonshire, England. An Insurance Agent for "Africa Life Insurance" in Johannesburg. He was unmarried. ***Jewish.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','III. C. 17.',NULL,'J R M','26794','30','',0,'',0,''),
