 (10960,10960,'Unknown','LESLIE JOHN','JAGGER','Lieutenant',334,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S.A.S. Parktown',2390,'1942-06-21','Ships were ordered to embark evacuation parties and leave Tobruk harbour when Axis forces started shelling the town on 20 June 1942. Under heavy fire and was the last Allied ship to leave Tobruk. Her decks were cramped with soldiers evacuated from Tobruk and outside the harbour she took a disabled tug in tow. Early the next morning she was attacked at close range by six Italian MAS boats. With her captain killed, nearly half her ship&#39;s company wounded and all ammunition expended, it was finally decided to abandon ship.','Son of Joseph and Maude Jagger, of Johannesburg, Transvaal, South Africa; husband of Grace Adelaide Jagger, of Johannesburg. *** On HMSAS Parktown Memorial in Pieter Roos Park, Parktown.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 1.',NULL,'L J','70016','32','Devon',1,'LG Sup 10 November 1942 pg. 4883',0,''),
 (10961,10961,'Unknown','CYRIL BLAKE','JAGO','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1917-04-09','Killed in action, at Battle of Arras','Son of E. and Susan Maynard Jago, of 9, Permere Terrace, Falmouth, Cornwall, England.','France',27,'CABARET-ROUGE BRITISH CEMETERY, SOUCHEZ',417,'50.38061','2.7416 ','XV. N. 6.',NULL,'C B','7475','27','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
 (10962,10962,'Unknown','REGINALD CECIL DUDLEY','JAGO','Private',429,'Imperial Light Horse/Kimberley Regiment, S.A.Forces',393,'"C" Coy.',18,'1944-09-13','Killed in action, when "C" Coy moved from Santomato to Castel Borroli. After encountering some enemy along the way, patrols reached the top of Castel Borrili and dug in. They were later subjected to heavy mortaring and shelling that resulted in casualties','Son of Isabel May Jefferies (formally Jago) of 24 Eaton Road, Durban. Husband of Norah Mary Jago (nee Williams), of 52 Main Road, Toll Gate, Durban. Born in Port Elizabeth. He had 1 son.','Italy',39,'CASTIGLIONE SOUTH AFRICAN CEMETERY',483,'44.14397','11.16183 ','III, B, 15.',NULL,'R C D','138390V','23','',0,'',0,''),
