 (11354,11354,'Unknown','PERCIVAL WILLIAM','JOHNSTON','Sergeant',492,'Q Service Corps, S.A. Forces',573,'1 Div. Supply Coy.',76,'1941-01-04','Died of self inflicted gun shot wound','Percival William Johnston was a draughtsman from Wynberg, Cape and served with the 3rd Supply Coy, "Q" service Corps from June 1937 - June 1940 prior to attesting for service in or outside South Africa. He served with the 1st Division Supply Coy in East Africa when he died from a self inflicted gunshot wound on 4 Jan 1941. Entitled to a 1939/45 Star; Africa Star; WM and ASM','Kenya',41,'NAIROBI WAR CEMETERY',1756,'-1.30902','36.74788 ','2. E. 8.',NULL,'P W','16816','','',0,'',0,''),
