 (11625,11625,'Unknown','KENNETH JOSEPH','JUBY','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Hollyhock',2308,'1942-04-09','Attacked by carrier-borne aircraft from a Japanese force of three battleships and five carriers which had entered the Bay of Bengal a week before. The fatal bomb hit near the funnel, probably exploding in her magazine, as she immediately blew up.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. H. W. B. Juby, of Germiston, Transvaal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'K J','69211','16','Devon',2,'',0,''),
 (11626,11626,'Unknown','LIONEL ORSMOND','JUBY','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Missing in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of Mrs. A. Juby, of Langlaagte, Transvaal.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'L O','6365','18','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
