 (11858,11858,'Unknown','GRAHAM HARFOLD','KAUFMANN','Captain',115,'South African Air Force',775,'182 Sqdn.',474,'1944-07-18','Killed in action, seen shot down in flames, during armed recce','Son of John E. and Florence. R. Kaufmann, of King William&#39;s Town, Cape Province, South Africa. The 182nd Squadron, a fighter-bomber squadron of the 2nd Tactical Air Force, was equipped with Hawker Typhoon','France',27,'BONNEBOSQ CHURCHYARD',301,'49.20542','0.07812 ','',NULL,'G H','242136V','25','Calvados',1,'DFC LG Sup 9 July 1943 pg. 3095 - "Over a period of 15 months Captain Kaufman has displayed continuous gallantry in the Western Desert and has to his credit at least three enemy aircraft destroyed. As a flight commander he has led the squadron most successfully. By his untiring efforts to fly at all times this officerâ€™s gallant conduct has set an excellent example, while his courage and fine fighting spirit have been of the highest order."; MID LG 1 January 1943 pg. 42',0,''),
