 (11862,11862,'Unknown','JOHN EUGENE CROUCH','KAVANAGH','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Helen Adelaide (aka Lily) and the late William Frederick Kavanagh, of 37 Albany Street, East London. Born Idutywa, Transkei.','France',27,'CABARET-ROUGE BRITISH CEMETERY, SOUCHEZ',417,'50.38061','2.7416 ','XXX. E. 19.',NULL,'J E C','6800','35','Pas de Calais',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
