 (11915,11915,'Unknown','DOUGLAS HAIG','KEEL','Corporal',166,'Technical Service Corps, S.A. Forces',922,'Unknown',0,'1944-11-11','Died on active service','Son of William J. and Mary J. Keel, of Northmead, Benoni, Transvaal.','Italy',39,'CASTIGLIONE SOUTH AFRICAN CEMETERY',483,'44.14397','11.16183 ','III, C, 9.',NULL,'D H','227539V','26','',0,'',0,''),
 (11916,11916,'Unknown','OSCAR ALAN','KEELER','Lieutenant',334,'London Regiment',441,'7th Bn.',1602,'1917-09-20','Killed in action','Son of Margaret and the late Alfred John Keeler, of 502, Moore Rd., Durban, Natal, South Africa. Commemoration stone in the Durban (West Street) Cemetery.','Belgium',10,'YPRES (MENIN GATE) MEMORIAL',2785,'50.8521','2.89138 ','Panels 52 to 54.',NULL,'O A','','28','Ieper, West-Vlaanderen',246,'LG 7 March 1916 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He held the line for three days before the attack under very difficult conditions and heavy shell fire. In the attack he prevented a threatened check by dashing forward and leading his company to the objective. He set a splendid example of determination and contempt of danger."',246,'attd. 17th Bn. King&#39;s Royal Rifle Corps'),
