 (11920,11920,'Unknown','PERCY NORMAN','KEELEY','Flight Sergeant',257,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'113 Sqdn.',241,'1942-01-24','Killed in air operations, in Burma. Z7582 MKIV FTR from a raid on Bangkok, Sgt P Keeley, Sgt Dingle, Sgt D Briggs KIA On 24 January a night raid was made on Bangkok, all serviceable aircraft participating. The Blenheims attacked singly at ten-minute intervals, bombing from 2000 feet with a war load of four 250 lb. bombs and four 25 lb. incendiaries. Large explosions and several fires resulted. An intense anti-aircraft barrage was again encountered over the target area, and two aircraft, including Z7582 piloted by Sergeant Keeley, failed to return.','Son of Edward and Eva Kelley, of Brakpan. Commemoration stone in Brakpan Cemetery','Thailand',85,'KANCHANABURI WAR CEMETERY',1240,'14.03195','99.52582 ','Coll. grave 10. M. 10-12.',NULL,'P N','785003','29','',0,'',0,''),
 (11921,11921,'Unknown','WILLIAM','KEELEY','Private',429,'Canadian Infantry (Nova Scotia Regiment)',240,'25th Bn.',830,'1916-06-18','Died of wounds, from a gun shot wound to the abdomen','Born at Pietermarizburg, South Africa Aug 16th, 1896. Next of kin in St. Anthony&#39;s Home, Sydney Co, Cape Breton, Nova Scotia, Canada. Previous service with the 94th Regiment.','Belgium',10,'LIJSSENTHOEK MILITARY CEMETERY',1477,'50.82839','2.7016 ','VIII. B. 3A.',NULL,'W','67153','19','Poperinge, West-Vlaanderen',1,'',0,''),
