 (11924,11924,'Unknown','FREDERICK WILLIAM','KEENEY','Able Seaman',25,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Hermes',2305,'1942-04-09','Attacked by carrier-borne aircraft from a Japanese force of three battleships and five carriers which had entered the Bay of Bengal a week before. Around seventy bombers were sent to dispatch the Hermes which sank within ten minutes.','Son of Fredrick W. and Wilhelmina A. Keeney.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'F W','67748','29','Devon',2,'',0,''),
