 (12040,12040,'Unknown','DENNIS CHARLES','KENNELLY','Ordinary Seaman',389,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. Hermes',2305,'1942-04-09','Attacked by carrier-borne aircraft from a Japanese force of three battleships and five carriers which had entered the Bay of Bengal a week before. Around seventy bombers were sent to dispatch the Hermes which sank within ten minutes.','He was born on October 1st, 1923, and entered Gaul House in January, 1936, leaving in December 1939. He played rugger and cricket for the School 2nd Teams, and was keen on boxing. On Plumtree School Roll of Honour','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 67, Column 2.',NULL,'D C','D/JX 283595','18','Devon',1,'',0,''),
