 (12214,12214,'Unknown','JOHN WILLIAM','KILLEEN','Warrant Officer Class I',594,'South African Veterinary Corps',867,'Unknown',0,'1943-03-03','Drowned, on S. S. Nirpura. At 23.22 hours on 3 Mar, 1943, U-160 made her first attack on the convoy DN-21 about 40 miles south of Port St.Johns, South Africa, sank the Harvey W. Scott and Nirpura and damaged the Tibia. 38 men from the Nirpura (Master Thomas George Hodgkinson) were lost and 88 (including the master) were picked up by the SAAF crash launch R-8 and landed at Durban.','Son of John and Kathleen Killeen; husband of Agnes Mary Killeen, of Pretoria, Transvaal, South Africa.','Myanmar',55,'RANGOON MEMORIAL',2108,'17.03621','96.13212 ','Face 19.',NULL,'J W','P/2068','50','',0,'',0,''),
