 (12221,12221,'Unknown','DENNIS CHARLES','KIMBLE','Electrical Artificer 4th Class',211,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Hermes',2305,'1942-04-09','Attacked by carrier-borne aircraft from a Japanese force of three battleships and five carriers which had entered the Bay of Bengal a week before. Around seventy bombers were sent to dispatch the Hermes which sank within ten minutes.','Son of Harold C. and Ellen K. Kimble, of Durban, Natal, South Africa. Attended Glenwood High School, Durban','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'D C','67766','23','Devon',1,'',0,''),
