 (12236,12236,'Unknown','DOUGLAS IVAN','KING','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1916-07-10','Killed in action, at Bernafay Wood, Somme','Son of Sarah Alice King, of "Lynedoch," Nottingham Rd., Natal, and the late James King. On Maritzburg College cenotaph. King&#39;s silver wound badge (No. SA 864), small 9ct gold locket containing small photograph and engraved: "D.I.K. Killed in Action 10/7/16, Pro Patria". On Kwazulu-Natal, LIONS RIVER district, Nottingham Road, St John&#39;s Gowrie Presbyterian Church, cemetery Great War Memorial','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'D I','5855','23','Somme',19,'',19,'"D" Coy.'),
