 (12253,12253,'Unknown','HENRY STUART','KING','Sub-Lieutenant',552,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. "Indefatigable."',2239,'1916-05-31','This was the first of the three British battlecruisers to be sunk at Jutland. She was struck by at least two salvoes from Hipper&#39;s battlecruisers around 15.58 on 31st May 1916. HMS Indefatigable was seen to sink by the stern, rolling over to port. There were two survivors from a crew of 1,019.','Son of Francis A. S. and Olivia E. King, of Cliftonville, Bray, Co. Wicklow. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','10.',NULL,'H S','','19','Devon',1,'',0,''),
