 (12570,12570,'Unknown','EINO','KORKOLAINAN','Able Seaman',25,'United States Merchant Marine',949,'Robin Goodfellow',2840,'1944-07-25','En route, Cape Town (16 Jul) - Bahia, Brazil - New York. At 02.12 hours on 25 Jul, 1944, the unescorted Robin Goodfellow (Master Bjarne Bjornsgaard) was torpedoed and sunk by U-862 in the South Atlantic. The British motor merchant Priam received a distress signal, but none of the eight officers, 33 crewmen and 27 armed guards (the ship was armed with one 4in, one 3in and five 20mm guns) survived.','Of Cape Town, South Africa. Might be last name KORKOLAIWAN','Lost at Sea',46,'DIED AT SEA',657,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'E','219569','','',0,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',0,''),
 (12571,12571,'Unknown','AARON','KORNA','Private',429,'Native Military Corps, S.A. Forces',513,'Unknown',0,'1943-03-03','Drowned, on S. S. Nirpura. At 23.22 hours on 3 Mar, 1943, U-160 made her first attack on the convoy DN-21 about 40 miles south of Port St.Johns, South Africa, sank the Harvey W. Scott and Nirpura and damaged the Tibia. 38 men from the Nirpura (Master Thomas George Hodgkinson) were lost and 88 (including the master) were picked up by the SAAF crash launch R-8 and landed at Durban.','Nephew of Fykkie Matthews, of Warrenton, Cape Province, South Africa.','Myanmar',55,'RANGOON MEMORIAL',2108,'17.03621','96.13212 ','Face 19.',NULL,'A','N/50824','25','',0,'',0,''),
 (12572,12572,'Unknown','ALEXANDER ARTHUR HOLMES','KORSTEN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Missing in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Jacques Richard Albert and Jessie Georgina Korsten, of 46, Cathcart Rd., Queenstown, Cape Province. A law student.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'A A H','8904','19','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
