 (12700,12700,'Unknown','DANIEL','KRYNAUW','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'60 Sqdn.',1426,'1944-08-26','Killed in action, Airborne 08:00 on 26 Aug 1944 from San Severo on a photo reconnaissance (PR) mission to several Messerschmitt aircraft factories and airfields at Regensburg. The aircraft was intercepted by a Me 262 (Ofw. Helmut Recker of Erprobungskommando 262) and crashed 10:19Z 3 km S of Breitenhill, 22 km N of Ingolstadt.','Son of Barend L. Krynauw and Maria E. Krynauw, of Cape Town, South Africa.','Germany',29,'DURNBACH WAR CEMETERY',737,'47.77834','11.73354 ','2. A. 21.',NULL,'D','328380V','20','Bad Tolz, Bayern',1,'',0,''),
