 (12898,12898,'Unknown','MAURICE RALPH PATON','LANDREY','Lieutenant',334,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1942-07-27','Died of wounds, received in action in an operation in the vicinity of El Alamein. The Regiment had been tasked to lift an enemy minefield to create a gap for 69 Bde and an Armoured Bde to pass through. Casualties were inflicted by severe MG fire and artillery bombardment. He suffered a traumatic injury to his left leg and died the same day','Son of Alfred Ernest Paton Landrey and Frances Harriet Landrey; husband of Frances Annetta Landrey, of Branksome Towers, Wanderers Street, Johannesburg. B.Sc., B.Sc. (Mining). Employed with the Dept of Mines. His brother also died in service in WW1','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','IV. A. 24.',NULL,'M R P','84559','29','',0,'',0,''),
