 (12905,12905,'Unknown','ARTHUR BLOOMFIELD','LANE','Captain',115,'Rifle Brigade',632,'10th Bn.',198,'1917-11-20','Killed in action','Son of Wilmot and Martha Lane, of 3, Eaton Gardens, Hove, Brighton. Formerly served in the King&#39;s Own Yorkshire Light Inf. Was managing a ranch in Rhodesia at outbreak of War, and accepted a Commission in the South African Forces, with whom he served in German West Africa, and France.','France',27,'CAMBRAI MEMORIAL, LOUVERVAL',433,'50.13666','3.01541 ','Panel 10 and 11.',NULL,'A B','','43','Nord',1,'',0,''),
