 (13156,13156,'Unknown','GEORGE RICHARD','LEACH','Sailor',468,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Blairatholl (Glasgow)',2892,'1942-11-27','Whilst operating with Convoy SC-98, had collision with John Bakke. Blairatholl sent an SOS. &#39;Foundering. Require Assistance. Taking to rafts. Boats carried away&#39;. Blairatholl foundered while proceeding to St.Johns NF. En route New York for Loch Ewe and Tyne.','Son of Catherine Johanna Leach, of Fort Beaufort, Cape Province, South Africa. Ex-cadet of the South African Training Ship General Botha','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 17.',NULL,'G R','','19','London',2,'',0,''),
