 (13192,13192,'Unknown','VICTOR EDWARD','LEDBURY','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-07-16','Killed in action, at Delville Wood','Son of Mr. Daniel and Mrs. E. Ledbury, of 1, Upper Union St., Gardens, Natal. Ledbury, a Clerk with the SA Railways & Harbours, was the son of Daniel J. Ledbury of 1, Upper Union Street, Gardens, Cape Town. He served with the 9th Infantry from 8 August 1914 to 13 August 1915 but as he did not leave the borders of the Union, he was not eligible for a 1914-15 Star. On 24 August 1915 he attested in the 1st SA Infantry Battalion and embarked at Cape Town on 20 September 1915.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'V E','2547','24','Somme',19,'',19,'"D" Coy.'),
