 (13206,13206,'Unknown','FREDERICK HENRY NORRIS','LEE','Lieutenant',334,'Irish Guards',409,'1st Bn.',528,'1916-07-04','Died of wounds','Son of the Rev. John Theodore Norris Lee and Mary Lee, of Hatfield Vicarage, Harlow, Essex. Born at Limerick. Joined the Tembuland Mounted Rifles, Sept., 1914, and fought against the rebels in the Orange Free State. Transf. 1915, to the Kalahari Horse and served in the German South West African Campaign.','France',27,'BOULOGNE EASTERN CEMETERY',319,'50.72483','1.62272 ','II. A. 42.',NULL,'F H N','','30','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
