 (13314,13314,'Unknown','HENDRIK JACOBUS PETRUS','LEMMER','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Air Force',775,'72 Operational Training Unit RAF',1556,'1942-07-23','Missing, Death Presumed, in Blenheim IV #7763, undergoing flying training in Kenya when their aircraft, a Blenheim bomber, did not return from a cross country navigational flying exercise. The wreck of the aircraft, and their mortal remains, were only discovered in 2002, and positively identified in 2003.','Son of Petrus Johannes and Marguerite Magdeline Lemmer, of Queenstown, Cape Province, South Africa. Commemoration stone in Queenstown Cemetery, Eastern Cape','Kenya',41,'NANYUKI WAR CEMETERY',1763,'-0.00053','37.10035 ','Special Memorial',NULL,'H J P','84626','23','',0,'',0,''),
