 (13319,13319,'Unknown','AARON','LEN','Private',429,'Imperial Light Horse/Kimberley Regiment, S.A.Forces',393,'Unknown',0,'1944-09-18','Killed in action, by enemy artillery barrage when "B" Coy was forming up to relieve "A" Coy in the vicinity of Monte Bagno at about 1545 on 18 September 1944','Son of Benzion and Sarah Len, of 162 Elston Avenue, Benoni, Transvaal. Born in Lithuania. A clerk. He was unmarried. ***Jewish.','Italy',39,'CASTIGLIONE SOUTH AFRICAN CEMETERY',483,'44.14397','11.16183 ','III, B, 4.',NULL,'A','79991V','25','',0,'',0,''),
