 (13329,13329,'Unknown','JOHN THOMAS','LENOURY','Private',429,'Essential Services Protection Corps, S.A. Forces',323,'Unknown',0,'1947-08-13','Died on active service','Son of John and Catherine Lenoury; husband of Sarah J. Lenoury, of Woodstock, Cape Town.','South Africa',72,'CAPE TOWN (MAITLAND) CEMETERY',452,'-33.91592','18.52805 ','Mil. Allotment. Grave 95728A.',NULL,'J T','700317','65','Western Cape',1,'',0,''),
 (13330,13330,'Unknown','ANTON','LENS','Captain',115,'South African Air Force',775,'183 Sqdn.',475,'1945-02-22','Killed in action, crashed in flames after being hit by flak. Would have been flying a Hawker Typhoon and based out of Gilze Rijen, Southern Netherlands at the time and flying in support of US offensive in the Ardennes.','Son of Wynand and Cornelia Lens, of Utrecht, Natal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 285.',NULL,'A','206321','23','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
 (13331,13331,'Unknown','JOHN WILFRED O&#39;NEILL','LENTAIGNE','Second Lieutenant',475,'Rifle Brigade',632,'1st Bn.',528,'1942-07-25','Died of wounds','Son of Lt.-Col. E. C. Lentaigne, D.S.O., formerly of the 4th Gurkha Rifles, and of C. M. Lentaigne (nee Bunbury), of Marandellas, Southern Rhodesia.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','XXI. E. 18.',NULL,'J W O','186295','20','',0,'LG Sup 13 August 1942 - "In recognition of gallant and distinguished services in the Middle East"',0,''),
 (13332,13332,'Unknown','ERNEST GERRET','LENTHALL','Aircraftman 1st Class',55,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'237 Sqdn.',775,'1941-12-11','Shortly after noon on 8th December, when many of the ground-staff and Headquarters personnel were congregated near the cookhouse, a sudden raid was made on the camp by a force of nearly a score of hostile aircraft, most of which were Messerschmitts 109 and 110. There was hardly time to reach the shelter of slit-trenches before the storm broke. The attack was short but severe. Thirty seconds of savage bombing and strafing from low level left the area a shambles of smoking debris. Four Rhodesians were killed - Corporal J. Smith, L/A/C.s A. G. Ednie and A. R. Meldrum, and AC.1 E. G. Lenthall','Son of Ernest Gilbert Lenthall, and of Aletta Johanna Frances Lenthall, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','XXXII. D. 7.',NULL,'E G','778196','19','',0,'',0,''),
 (13333,13333,'Unknown','KENNETH','LENTIN','Flight Sergeant',257,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'179 Sqdn.',459,'1944-07-07','Died in Aircraft Accident, Wellington XIV HF129, overshot runway and stalled, crashed on impact, at Chivenor','Son of Myer and Ida Lentin, of Kitwe, Northern Rhodesia. ***Jewish','United Kingdom',90,'BATH (HAYCOMBE) CEMETERY',166,'51.37033','-2.40131 ','Plot 51. Sec. H. Row S. Coll. grave 240.',NULL,'K','778686','','Somerset',1,'',0,''),
 (13334,13334,'Unknown','SIDNEY','LENTIN','Flight Sergeant',257,'South African Air Force',775,'24 Sqdn.',788,'1943-04-14','Killed in action, lost in St. Marie du Wit LG, in Douglas Boston Mk III #Z2195','Son of Max and Eva Lentin, of Windhoek, South-West Africa. ***Jewish','Tunisia',86,'SFAX WAR CEMETERY',2282,'34.72069','10.73326 ','XI. D. 23.',NULL,'S','206301','21','',0,'',0,''),
 (13335,13335,'Unknown','MISTER','LENTLE','Lance Corporal',311,'Native Military Corps, S.A. Forces',513,'Unknown',0,'1943-06-03','Died of cardiac failure','***Last name and first name may be reversed','South Africa',72,'PIET RETIEF (eTHANDAKUKHANYA) CEMETERY',1954,'-27.02518','30.78379 ','Grave 767.',NULL,'M','N/41917','','Mpumalanga',2,'',0,''),
 (13336,13336,'Unknown','RALPH PERCY','LENTON','Captain',115,'Royal Artillery',643,'Unknown',0,'1944-02-12','Lost in S.S. Khedive Ismail (London). Sailing on 6 February 1944 from Kilindini Harbour at Mombasa, Kenya to Colombo, Ceylon in Convoy KR-8, the SS Khedive Ismail was attacked by a B1 type Japanese submarine. The Khedive Ismail was hit by two torpedoes. 1297 perished','Son of Mr. and Mrs. A. H. Lenton, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia; husband of Barbara Lenton, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','Kenya',41,'EAST AFRICA MEMORIAL',741,'-1.30973','36.74866 ','Column 1.',NULL,'R P','214748','25','',0,'',345,'attd. 301 Field Regt. East African Artillery'),
