 (13363,13363,'Unknown','DOUGLAS BENJAMIN','LESAR','Private',429,'Youth Training Brigade, S.A. Forces',979,'Unknown',0,'1945-11-18','Died in explosion, at the Barracks of the Youth Training Brigade at Roberts Heights. 3 members were using a bayonet and a screwdriver in an attempt to dismantle a 2 inch mortar shell that they found in rubble from the explosion of the Grand Magazine, which was being used for earth works at Roberts Heights.','Son of Frederick B. and Susan Lesar, of Brentwood, Benoni.','South Africa',72,'BOKSBURG CEMETERY',295,'-26.21977','28.27423 ','Non-Conformist Sec. A. Grave 1633.',NULL,'D B','596587V','17','Gauteng',1,'',0,''),
