 (13507,13507,'Unknown','JOHN EDWARD JOSEPH','LEWIS','Lieutenant',334,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S.A.S. Southern Floe',2397,'1941-02-11','Lost after striking a mine while on patrol in Mediterranean near Tobruk, Libya','Son of George Herbert and Alden Rose Lewis, of Cape Town, South Africa; husband of Dulcie T. Lewis, of Gape Town. Born Wynberg, 28 November 1912. Educated Diocesan College, Rondebosch. Ex-cadet of the South African Training Ship General Botha. Cadet Draft 1927-8. John Edward Joseph Lewis joined the Blue Funnel Line as Midshipman, obtaining his Master&#39;s Certificate in 1936. During the war he served with the Seaward Defence Force. Was Commanding Officer of the HMSAS Southern Floe at the time. Winner of the King&#39;s Gold Medal. Joined the General Botha staff as Third Officer in 1937 before joining the navy in 1939.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 58, Column 3.',NULL,'J E J','70019','28','Devon',1,'',0,''),
