 (14038,14038,'Unknown','WILLIAM ALEXANDER','LUNDIE','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Infantry',807,'3rd Regt.',1119,'1916-07-06','Killed in action. On 5 July the 3rd SAI were in support of the front in the old British and German front-line trenches immediately to the north-west of Maricourt. The next day there was great shelling and the South African regiments suffered some twenty casualties.','Son of William E. and Pamela Lundie, of 25, Davies St., Pietermaritzburg, Natal. On Maritzburg College cenotaph.','France',27,'PERONNE ROAD CEMETERY, MARICOURT',1935,'49.97808','2.78206 ','I. A. 19.',NULL,'W A','4925','23','Somme',1,'',0,''),
