 (14109,14109,'Unknown','WILLIAM EDWARD','LYTTLE','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1944-07-29','Died of wounds, during the advance to Florence, in the vicinity of the river Greve. He received a shrapnel wound to the femur on the 28 July, but died the next day','Son of William Edward and Effie Lolotte Lyttle, of 413, Longmarket Street, Pietermaritzburg. Born Greytown, Natal. An accountant. He was unmarried. His brother also died on service','Italy',39,'FLORENCE WAR CEMETERY',866,'43.77016','11.34284 ','III. B. 3.',NULL,'W E','75071V','33','',0,'LG Sup 15 December 1942 pg. 5449',0,''),
