 (14208,14208,'Unknown','HECTOR OMDURMAN','MACDONALD','Captain',115,'South African Air Force',775,'26 Sqdn.',836,'1943-12-02','Died in Aircraft Accident, Vickers Wellington Mk XI #LN384, dived into sea off turn, blew up off Takoradi','Service in Royal Flying Corps and Royal Air Force in WW1 with 84 Squadron. Credited with 7 Victories. Born 29 June 1899 in Cape Town. He was commissioned on 20 July 1917 and posted to 84 Squadron on 03 February 1918. He was injured in a crash on 06 July 1918. Several months later, he returned to duty. After the war, he returned to South Africa and became a sugar grower. He was killed on 02 December 1943 in a crash while serving as an armaments officer in the South African Air Force. Husband of Kathleen Maud (nee Gould - born in Durban, died in 1960).','Ghana',30,'TAKORADI EUROPEAN PUBLIC CEMETERY',2462,'4.90585','-1.7744 ','Grave 55.',NULL,'H O','203267V','44','',0,'',0,''),
