 (14279,14279,'Unknown','ALEC DAVID AMBROSE','MacKENZIE','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Missing in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Alec and Jessie Evelyn MacKenzie, of "Epping," Palmyra Rd., Claremont, Cape Province.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'A D A','8911','20','Somme',1,'',0,''),
