 (14337,14337,'Unknown','BASIL GEORGE HOPELINEN','MACLEAR','Second Lieutenant',475,'Grenadier Guards',350,'4th Bn.',1259,'1916-07-26','Killed in action','Son of the late Rev. Canon G. F. Maclear, D.D. (Warden of St. Augustine&#39;s College, Canterbury, Kent). Left his farm in Cape Province, South Africa (where he had been since 1904), Aug., 1915 to serve. See http://www.hambo.org/kingscanterbury/view_man.php?id=195','Belgium',10,'ESSEX FARM CEMETERY',814,'50.87138','2.87247 ','II. Z. 19.',NULL,'B G H','','30','Ieper, West-Vlaanderen',1,'LG Sup 31 May 1916 - "For conspicuous gallantry and ability. When ordered to establish communication with another battalion, he did so over 250 yards of ground in the face of very heavy shell fire, establishing bombing posts as he proceeded."',0,''),
 (14338,14338,'Unknown','KENNETH','MACLEAR','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1917-10-14','Killed in action, during first battle of Passchendaele','Son of John Laing Maclear and Annie Louis Maclear, of Aberdeen, Cape Province. ***Full name may be Kenneth Louis Herschel Maclear','Belgium',10,'YPRES (MENIN GATE) MEMORIAL',2785,'50.8521','2.89138 ','Panel 15 - 16 and 16A.',NULL,'K','12501','24','Ieper, West-Vlaanderen',1,'',0,''),
