 (14348,14348,'Unknown','JOHN RODERICK','MacLEOD','Private',429,'London Regiment (London Scottish)',448,'1st/14th Bn.',581,'1918-08-29','Killed in action','Next of kin, A. MacLeod, Kincardine House, Ardgay, Scotland. Played for Durban Wanderers R.F.C. pre WW1. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','France',27,'VIS-EN-ARTOIS MEMORIAL',2637,'50.2469','2.95038 ','Panel 10.',NULL,'J R','511699','','Pas de Calais',1,'LG Sup 21 October 1918 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. For six months this man has performed continuous good work as a stretcher-bearer. He has at all times and especially during heavy fighting, rendered prompt assistance to the wounded and undoubtedly been the means of saving many lives."',0,''),
