 (14356,14356,'Unknown','ROBERT','MacNAE','Second Lieutenant',475,'The King&#39;s (Liverpool Regiment)',927,'10th Bn.',198,'1916-10-10','Killed in action','Son of the late Robert and Grace MacNae, of Maxwelltown, Dumfries. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','Belgium',10,'VLAMERTINGHE MILITARY CEMETERY',2640,'50.85564','2.81999 ','IV. G. 12.',NULL,'R','','','Ieper, West-Vlaanderen',1,'LG Sup 20 Oct 1916 pg 10187 - "For conspicuous gallantry in action. When all his senior officers had become casualties, he rallied his men and led them in two fresh attempts to capture the enemy&#39;s trench. Finally, he carried his company serjeant-major, who was severely wounded, back to safety. He set a fine example throughout the day."',0,''),
 (14357,14357,'Unknown','CARROLL CHARLES','MACNAMARA','Lieutenant Colonel',339,'Royal Irish Rifles',673,'1st Bn.',528,'1916-07-16','Died of wounds, received 1st July, commanding his regiment in the Somme','Son of the late N. C. Macnamara, F.R.C.S. Also served at Gallipoli. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','United Kingdom',90,'CHORLEY WOOD (CHRIST CHURCH) CHURCHYARD',538,'51.65868','-0.50388 ','South corner of church.',NULL,'C C','','41','Hertfordshire',1,'LG 25 July 1916 - "By His Highness the Sultan of Egypt in recognition of valuable services rendered"',0,''),
