 (14580,14580,'Unknown','JAMES','MAIN','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 1st SAI lost 2 officers and 203 men.','Brother of John Main, of Drummer Street, Hopeman, Elgin, Scotland. On Mansfield Road Boys School Roll of Honour','France',27,'BROWN&#39;S COPSE CEMETERY, ROEUX',371,'50.30288','2.88379 ','II. D. 38.',NULL,'J','8185','','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
