 (15420,15420,'Unknown','WILLIAM','MASON','Lance Corporal',311,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1942-07-27','Killed in action, in an operation in the vicinity of El Alamein. The Regiment had been tasked to lift an enemy minefield to create a gap for 69 Bde and an Armoured Bde to pass through. Casualties were inflicted by severe MG fire and artillery bombardment','Husband of Esther Mason, of Park Drive, Port Elizabeth. Born in Johannesburg. A clerk.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','XXIV. G. 7.',NULL,'W','353','41','',0,'',0,''),
