 (15907,15907,'Unknown','WILLIAM KENNETH','McDAVID','Stoker 2nd Class',540,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Cornwall',2279,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. CORNWALL and her sister ship Dorsetshire were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of Gilbert McArthur and Jean McDavid; husband of Madeline Olga Elizabeth McDavid, of Johannesburg, Transvaal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'W K','69138','34','Devon',1,'',0,''),
