 (16356,16356,'Unknown','ANDREW RALPH','MELDRUM','Leading Aircfraftman',317,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'237 Sqdn.',775,'1941-12-08','Shortly after noon on 8th December, when many of the ground-staff and Headquarters personnel were congregated near the cookhouse, a sudden raid was made on the camp by a force of nearly a score of hostile aircraft, most of which were Messerschmitts 109 and 110. There was hardly time to reach the shelter of slit-trenches before the storm broke. The attack was short but severe. Thirty seconds of savage bombing and strafing from low level left the area a shambles of smoking debris. Four Rhodesians were killed - Corporal J. Smith, L/A/C.s A. G. Ednie and A. R. Meldrum, and AC.1 E. G. Lenthall','RAF Number: Southern Rhodesians in Middle East','Egypt',23,'ALAMEIN MEMORIAL',35,'30.83823','28.94696 ','Column 244.',NULL,'A R','776371','','',0,'',0,''),
