 (16375,16375,'Unknown','MAXWELL ARTHUR','MELVILLE','Private',429,'Canadian Infantry (Manitoba Regiment)',239,'8th Bn.',1665,'1918-08-09','Killed in action, near Amiens','Son of Edward William and Mary Ann Melville, of Saskatoon, Saskatchewan. Born at Cape Town, South Africa. Came from Cape Town, South Africa, to homestead SW22-37-7-W3 northeast of Grandora. Maxwell was working as a boilermaker when he enlisted at Moose Jaw on Christmas Eve 1914.','France',27,'VRELY COMMUNAL CEMETERY EXTENSION',2656,'49.80084','2.68762 ','A. 20.',NULL,'M A','426140','35','Somme',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
