 (16769,16769,'Unknown','COLIN PATRICK','MITCHELL','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'44 (Rhodesia) Sqdn.',1203,'1943-01-18','Killed in action, in Lancaster I ED318, took off from Waddington at 17.09 hrs. Lost without a trace with all of its crew. 13 of the 187 bomber force were shot down over the North Sea, it is &#39;probable&#39; that ED318 was one of these','Son of Mr. and Mrs. E. C. Mitchell, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 159.',NULL,'C P','778210','22','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
