 (17351,17351,'Unknown','PETRUS LAVRAS','MOOLMAN','Corporal',166,'Imperial Light Horse, S.A. Forces',392,'1st',515,'1944-01-19','Died in hospital in Egypt, awaiting repatriation. He was reported missing in June 1942 and later confirmed as a POW. He was released in Italy in September 1943 and returned to Egypt where he was hospitalized in October 1943. He was classified as "D" for return to South Africa in January 1944 but died before this could happen','Son of Emma Melvina Moolman, of 51a High Street, Brixton, Johannesburg. Husband of Dorothea Barbara (nee Botha) Moolman, of 87 Putney Road, Brixton, Johannesburg. Born in Vrededorp, Transvaal. A clerk.','Egypt',23,'HELIOPOLIS WAR CEMETERY',1114,'30.07973','31.32963 ','4. G. 2.',NULL,'P L','26523','26','',0,'',0,''),
