 (17467,17467,'Unknown','CHRISTOPHER SEARLE HAMILTON','MORLEY','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'467 Sqdn.',1228,'1943-01-18','Killed in action, Lancaster W4378 took off from RAF Bottesford, Leicestershire, UK at 1705 hours on the night of 17/18th January 1943 to bomb Berlin. Nothing was heard from the aircraft after take off and it failed to return to base. Eight aircraft from the Squadron took part in the mission, and one of these W4378 failed to return.','RAF Number: Rhodesia for South Africans','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 159.',NULL,'C S H','711065','','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
