 (17488,17488,'Unknown','CHARLES','MORRIS','Private',429,'Highland Light Infantry',380,'12th Bn.',307,'1916-08-13','Killed in action','Husband of Frances Bean (formerly Morris), of 3, Durham Avenue, Salt River, Cape Province, South Africa.','France',27,'CATERPILLAR VALLEY CEMETERY, LONGUEVAL',489,'50.02619','2.792 ','V. G. 19.',NULL,'C','18034','22','Somme',1,'',0,''),
 (17489,17489,'Unknown','CYRIL DESMOND','MORRIS','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Barham',2265,'1941-11-25','Killed in action, while steaming to cover an attack on Italian convoys, HMS Barham was hit by three torpedoes from the German submarine U-331. As she rolled over to port, her after magazines exploded and the ship quickly sank with the loss of over two-thirds of her crew','Son of Thomas P. and Hilda Morris, of Durban, Natal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 58, Column 3.',NULL,'C D','68932','17','Devon',1,'',0,''),
