 (18047,18047,'Unknown','GRAHAME ALEXANDER','MUNRO','Cyclist',171,'South African Motor Cyclist Corps',824,'Unknown',0,'1916-12-18','Died of wounds, gun shot wound abdomen','Son of Alexander William and Ethel Munro, of Slaai Kraal, Grahamstown, Cape Province. Educated at St. Andrew&#39;s College, Grahamstown. Born 13/5/1896 At St Andrew&#39;s College 1911-1913. 1914 fought in Midland Horse in G.S.W.A., and in 1916 in Motor Cyclist Corps in G.E.A. where he died of wounds received in action.','Tanzania',84,'IRINGA CEMETERY',1204,'-7.77931','35.69981 ','IV. A. 1.',NULL,'G A','CM/51','20','',0,'',0,''),
