 (18893,18893,'Unknown','RONALD WYKEHAM','NOAKES','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Barham',2265,'1941-11-25','Killed in action, while steaming to cover an attack on Italian convoys, HMS Barham was hit by three torpedoes from the German submarine U-331. As she rolled over to port, her after magazines exploded and the ship quickly sank with the loss of over two-thirds of her crew','Son of Reginald William and Mary Louisa Noakes, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 58, Column 3.',NULL,'R W','68543','32','Devon',1,'',0,''),
