 (19111,19111,'Unknown','ALBERT DE WET','NUSSEY','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'150 (R.A.F.) Sqdn.',380,'1944-04-21','On the night of April 21, 1944 the Wellington LN385, belonging to 150 Squadron of the RAF base at Amendola in Puglia, on a bombing run to Porto Santo Stefano in Tuscany. On his return from the operation, near the coast of Salerno, the bomber had to undergo an air strike. At 23:23 the report states that a request was heard coming from the plane of MD-Q LN385. It was heard again weakly at 01:06 on April 22, after which radio contact was lost','Son of Brigadier-General A. H. M. Nussey and Bridget Nussey, of Potchefstroom, Transvaal, South Africa. See also http://www.aircrewremembrancesociety.com/raf1944/3/nusseyadw.html?hl=de&q=south+africa','Italy',39,'SALERNO WAR CEMETERY',2243,'40.62508','14.92202 ','I. E. 6.',NULL,'A D W','328728V','19','',0,'',0,''),
