 (19553,19553,'Unknown','DOUGLAS OSBORN','PACKER','Trooper',581,'Natal Mounted Rifles, S.A. Forces',504,'1st Bn.',528,'1944-07-17','Died of wounds, wounded on the 17th July, shrapnel wound to the head, during the advance of "A" Sqdn between Radda and Verline, Italy, but died later the same day and was temporarily buried along the roadside at Ossaia, Italy. He was later moved to the Assisi War Cemetery.','Son of Osborn and Florence Violet Packer, of Harding, Natal, South Africa. Born in Kokstad, East Griqualand. A blockman by profession','Italy',39,'ASSISI WAR CEMETERY',106,'43.04628','12.60942 ','V, B, 2.',NULL,'D O','6157','22','',0,'',8,'"A" Sqdn.'),
