 (19607,19607,'Unknown','RICHARD HENRY DAMPIER','PALMER','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'Unknown',0,'1941-12-18','Died in air crash, in Hudson V9032 at Quarry Farm, Ingleby Barwick, Middlesbrough. The crew of this aircraft were to undertake a training flight, the aircraft stalled soon after take off and then crashed into Quarry Farm, Ingleby Barwick. Along with the five airmen in the aircraft, four civilians in the house also were killed, two other children escaped with injuries.','On war memorial for King Edward VII School, Johannesburg. RAF Number: Enlistments in Rhodesia','United Kingdom',90,'ENFIELD (LAVENDER HILL) CEMETERY',789,'51.66598','-0.09438 ','Sec. C. Cons. Grave 6123.',NULL,'R H D','778436','','Middlesex',1,'',0,''),
