 (19641,19641,'Unknown','ROBIN FRASER','PARE','Captain',115,'South African Air Force',775,'1 Sqdn.',117,'1942-06-03','Killed in action, shot down on sweep, in Curtiss Tomahawk Mk IIB #AK384','Son of Henry Alfred and Lucy Pare, of "Belair", Constantia, Cape Province, South Africa. Commemoration stone in Cape Town (Constantia) Public Cemetery','Egypt',23,'ALAMEIN MEMORIAL',35,'30.83823','28.94696 ','Column 266.',NULL,'R F','202945V','23','',0,'LG 29 April 1941 pg. 2445 - "In February, 1941, Lieutenant Pare was detailed with six other aircraft to carry out an attack on the aerodrome at Massawa. On approaching the target, he observed an anti-aircraft gun post about to open fire on the leader of the formation. He attacked and silenced this post but in doing so his guns jammed. In spite of this he continued to dive down on other anti-aircraft posts thus minimising the fire directed against the rest of his formation. Lieutenant Pare also displayed great courage and determination in the battle of Keren, shooting down four enemy fighters in two air battles within three days."',143,'and 5 Sqdn.'),
