 (19648,19648,'Unknown','','PARK','Corporal',166,'General Service Corps, S.A. Forces',340,'1st S.A. Div. H.Q.',560,'1942-11-28','Lost at sea on S. S. Nova Scotia, torpedoed and sunk by U-177. En route from Aden to Durban, South Africa. Carrying 6 passengers, 11 military and naval personnel, 134 South African guards and 765 Italian civil internees','No additional information known at this time','Egypt',23,'ALAMEIN MEMORIAL',35,'30.83823','28.94696 ','Column 149.',NULL,'G','82166','','',0,'',0,''),
 (19649,19649,'Unknown','GEOFFREY ROGER','PARK','Wing Commander',606,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'272 Sqdn.',860,'1944-10-15','Killed in action, his Beaufighter was shot down by flak, whilst on a shipping strike over the Adriatic Sea','Son of Thomas and Kathleen Gertrude (nee Stephens) Park. Husband of Joan Mary Park, of Claremont, Cape Town, South Africa.','Malta',51,'MALTA MEMORIAL',1588,'35.8947','14.50783 ','Panel 12, Column 1.',NULL,'G R','78710','28','',0,'LG Sup 24 September 1943 pg. 4246 - "This officer has completed an extremely large number of hours flying on operations at night. One one occasion, in July 1943, he destroyed a Messerschmitt, while one night in August 1943, he destroyed two Dornier 217s. During the latter combat his own aircraft was badly damaged but displaying great skill and determination he flew it to an airfield near the coast. Wing Commander Park is a highly efficient squadron commander who has displayed rare keenness and devotion to duty"',0,''),
