 (19739,19739,'Unknown','GORDON RAYMOND','PATER','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of John Raymond Pater and Belinda Rosalie Pater, of "Toolanji," Eildon Rd., Kensington, Transvaal. Native of Melbourne, Australia. Attended Jeppe High School for Boys. Entered the School in 1908 and left in 1912. On Jeppe High School for Boys Roll of Honour','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','I. K. I.',NULL,'G R','7907','19','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
