 (19866,19866,'Unknown','HENRY GOOLD','PEARCE','Captain',115,'Royal Engineers',659,'171st Coy.',444,'1917-07-15','Killed in action','Son of Henry and Margaret Pearce; husband of Ina Pearce, of 77A, Nightingale Lane, Balham, London. Born Hurstpierpoint, Sussex June 1886; resided in Rhodesia prior to the outbreak of the Great War; served as a Corporal in the Northern Rhodesian Rifles, from 10.12.1914; discharged 30.4.1915 to return to the United Kingdom to take a commission in the Royal Engineers; served on the Western Front with the 171st Tunnelling Company, wounded 25.4.1917; the 171st Tunnelling Company were involved in the laying of 24 mines as part of the battle of Messine, from June 1917','Belgium',10,'POPERINGHE NEW MILITARY CEMETERY',2008,'50.84738','2.73305 ','II. B. 44.',NULL,'H G','','31','Poperinge, West-Vlaanderen',1,'LG Sup 1 January 1918 pg. 43',0,''),
