 (19881,19881,'Unknown','ALAN NEIL','PEARSE','Leading Aircraftman',318,'Royal Air Force',635,'Unknown',0,'1941-05-16','Died in Aircraft Accident, Oxford I P1881, while on a test flight the aircraft began to break up starting with the elevator detaching from the aircraft. This resulted in a loss of control and the aircraft hitting the ground. W Cdr. F K Damant and passenger LAC AN Pearse were both killed in the incident','Son of Colonel Stanley Arthur Coxon Pearse and Ivy Pearse, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','United Kingdom',90,'CRANWELL (ST. ANDREW) CHURCHYARD',591,'53.03683','-0.46122 ','Plot 2. Row B. Grave 18.',NULL,'A N','575535','18','Lincolnshire',1,'',0,''),
