 (20952,20952,'Unknown','WILLIAM RAMSAY','RAE','Lance Sergeant',313,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of M. Rae, of Alloa, Scotland, and the late A. Rae; husband of Jennie Rae, of Kimberley, Cape Province, South Africa.','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'W R','8228','34','Somme',19,'',19,'"D" Coy.'),
