 (21184,21184,'Unknown','FRANK','RAWLINS','Major',343,'Q Service Corps, S.A. Forces',573,'Unknown',0,'1942-12-19','Died in Aircraft Accident, in Lockheed Lodestar 18-08 #248. Crashed into the sea shortly after takeoff from Kisumu Airport (KIS). The airplane came down in Kavirondo Gulf, Lake Victoria. It appeared that the undercarriage could not be raised after takeoff because of an electrical failure in the under-carriage safety lock circuit. The Lodestar was returning to South Africa from Cairo, Egypt','Son of Frank and Edith A. Rawlins; husband of Sheila M. Rawlins, of Pietermaritzburg, Natal.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (OLD No.1) MILITARY CEMETERY',2491,'-25.80165','28.12721 ','L. 5.',NULL,'F','1009','31','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 23 June 1942 pg. 2745, 2nd MID LG Sup 24 June 1943 pg. 2867',0,''),
 (21185,21185,'Unknown','CLIVE FRANCIS METHLEY','RAWLINSON','Private',429,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'Unknown',0,'1943-06-04','Died of acute oedema and abscess larynx, whilst a POW, in Sardinia','Son of Francis Christopher Rawlinson, of Harlestone, Mooi River, Natal. He was captured on 20 June 1942 while part of the Regiment&#39;s Composite Coy, detached as part of the defensive line at Tobruk. Another POW reported that he had actually died in hospital at Carbonia, Sardinia and had been buried there. It is likely his grave was relocated after the war.','Italy',39,'CAGLIARI (ST. MICHELE) COMMUNAL CEMETERY',419,'39.24375','9.10118 ','I. B. 4.',NULL,'C F M','4275','23','',0,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
