 (21224,21224,'Unknown','ALAN GARDINER','REDFERN','Captain',115,'King&#39;s Royal Rifle Corps',424,'Unknown',0,'1943-11-12','Killed in action, at Leros. He was killed in action instantly by machine gun fire on Leros whilst leading a composite LRDG and SBS party in a close struggle with 500 German parachutists who had been dropped on the narrow strip between Gurna and Alinda bays.','Son of Arthur William and Margaret A. Redfern of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia; husband of Agnes Opal Redfern, of Salisbury.','Greece',31,'LEROS WAR CEMETERY',1458,'37.15978','26.83746 ','3. C. 9.',NULL,'A G','291976','37','',0,'LG Sup 1 January 1943 pg. 12 - "For running commando training courses in Gwelo, Southern Rhodesia"',162,'and Long Range Desert Group.'),
