 (21328,21328,'Unknown','WILLIAM MACDONALD','RENNIE','Corporal',166,'Special Service Battalion, S.A. Forces',901,'Unknown',0,'1944-06-12','Killed in action. The Regiment advanced up the road from Celleno to Bagnoregio and after having made contact with the anti-tank screen from the 26th Panzer Division, they withdrew and harboured for the night. Corporal Rennie was killed during heavy shelling of the harbour area','Son of John and Elizabeth Rennie, of Fort Victoria, Southern Rhodesia. Husband of Sarah Beatrice Dorothea Rennie, c/o The Standard Bank, Fort Victoria. Born in Fort Victoria. A farmer in the Mazoe area','Italy',39,'BOLSENA WAR CEMETERY',298,'42.58562','11.99863 ','II. A. 2.',NULL,'W M','SR/598384V','34','',0,'',0,''),
