 (21356,21356,'Unknown','FREDERICK HENRY','REYNARD','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Missing in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Charles and C. Fanny Reynard, of "Ozelor," Langlands, Ndonga, Lady Frere, Cape Province. His brother also died in service','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'F H','6781','34','Somme',6,'',6,'"A" Coy.'),
 (21357,21357,'Unknown','THOMAS JAMES','REYNARD','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Charles and C. Fanny Reynard, of "Ozelor," Langlands, Ndonga, Lady Frere, Cape Province. Native of Isle of Wight. His brother also died in service','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','I. G. 11.',NULL,'T J','6782','29','Pas de Calais',6,'',6,'"A" Coy.'),
