 (21656,21656,'Unknown','WILLIAM LEWIS THORTON','ROBERTSON','Third Officer',576,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. City of Pretoria (London)',2898,'1943-03-03','At 06.09 hours on 4 Mar, 1943, the unescorted City of Pretoria (Master Frank Deighton, OBE) was hit by two of three torpedoes from U-172 and sank after a heavy explosion about 320 miles northwest of the Azores. The ship was reported missing and presumed lost in approx. 41Â°45N/42Â°30W. The master, 108 crew members, 24 gunners, seven passengers (DBS) and 5 apprentices were lost.','Son of William and Annie Robertson. Ex-Cadet of the South African Training Ship General Botha','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 30.',NULL,'W L T','','22','London',1,'',0,''),
