 (21754,21754,'Unknown','NEVILLE JOHN','ROGERS','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'49 Sqdn.',1246,'1942-06-20','Died in Aircraft Accident, Manchester I L7387, crashed North Sea off the Frisian Islands. The squadron was asked to provide 4 Manchesters for a sea search. The previous evening, Bomber Command had attacked Emden and 9 aircraft had failed to return - a sea search was made in case any of these aircraft had ditched. It was an ironic tragedy, when a 49 Squadron crew, piloted by Sgt John O&#39;Brien RAAF and Sgt Charles Goldring (L7387) crashed into the sea themselves. Only two bodies were ever recovered','Son of Andrew Nicholson Rogers, and of Muriel Rogers, of Limbe, Nyasaland. RAF Number: Enlistments in Rhodesia','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 92.',NULL,'N J','778781','','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
