 (21807,21807,'Unknown','WILLIAM HENRY','ROOZA','Able Bodied Seaman',24,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Columbine',2905,'1944-06-16','On 16 June 1944, the unescorted Columbine (Master Andre Reidar Simensen) was torpedoed and sunk by U-198, 25 miles northwest of Cape Columbine, South Africa. The master, 19 crew members and six passengers were lost.','Brother of Leonard Alfred Rooza, of Cape Town. Born Cape Town. Coloured man. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1939-1945','Lost at Sea',46,'DIED AT SEA',657,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'W H','','26','',0,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',0,''),
 (21808,21808,'Unknown','ALFRED EDWARD','ROPER','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-13','Died of wounds, received in front the Butte de Warlencourt. On the 12th October, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range. The two battalions, which had suffered heavily, were relieved by the 3rd S.A.I. during the night of the 12th-13th October.','Son of Thomas Roper, of Quagga Hoek via Brandfort, Orange Free State','France',27,'DERNANCOURT COMMUNAL CEMETERY EXTENSION',649,'49.97684','2.62496 ','III. G. 46.',NULL,'A E','6824','','Somme',1,'',0,''),
