 (21865,21865,'Unknown','DAVID SCHALK ULUNDI','ROSS','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1918-03-25','Died of wounds, whilst a POW','Son of Mr. Colin George and Mrs. S. J. Ross, of Room 15, 218, Arcida Mansions, Johannesburg. At 14 years and 3 months, Pte. Ross is one of the youngest soldiers killed in the 1914-1918 war. Taken on strength 22 May 1917. Wounded in action (leg) 20 September 1917.','France',27,'HEUDICOURT COMMUNAL CEMETERY',1138,'50.02033','3.08071 ','3.',NULL,'D S U','11322','14','Somme',1,'',0,''),
