 (21867,21867,'Unknown','FINLAY GEORGE MACLEOD','ROSS','Captain',115,'Royal Army Medical Corps',640,'Unknown',0,'1917-06-04','Died of pneumonia, due to rigours of campaigning','Husband of Hazel Jessie Ross (nee Smith-Ridley). Son of Finlay M. Ross, commercial traveler; born Aberdeen, 31 October 1886; educated Aberdeen Grammar School; matriculated 1904; graduated M.B., 1909; Assistant, Murray&#39;s Asylum, Perth; later went to India as Medical Officer on S.S. "City of Paris". Subsequently, in 1911, following a period of ill-health, he went out to South Africa, where in a short space of time he developed an extensive private practice at Wolmaranstadt and filled many public positions of importance. Ross joined the R.A.M.C. at the outbreak of war and served in East Africa throughout the entire campaign there. Later he took over control of Klerksdorp Hospital to permit two resident medical men to serve in France. His health, affected by the rigours of campaigning, was indifferent and his duties as District Surgeon, Medical Officer of Health, and Physician to the staff of six mines overtaxed his strength, he died of pneumonia on 4 June 1917. His work on service was commended by those under whom he directed the medical organization entrusted to his particular care, and his personal popularity while at the University, in the Army and in private practice was a tribute to his winning personality.','South Africa',72,'WOLMARANSSTAD CEMETERY',2763,'-27.20422','25.97883 ','',NULL,'F G M','','30','North West Province',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',0,''),
 (21868,21868,'Unknown','FRANCIS MCWILLIAM','ROSS','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1918-09-12','Drowned at sea (from S.S. "Galway Castle"), as a result of an attack by an enemy submarine 160 miles S.W. and .5 S. of the Fastnet','Son of Arthur Peter and the late Emily Ross, of Aig, Boshoff St., Pietermaritzburg, Natal. Commemoration stone in Pietermaritzburg (Commercial Road) Cemetery','United Kingdom',90,'HOLLYBROOK MEMORIAL, SOUTHAMPTON',1156,'50.93384','-1.43114 ','Panel 49.',NULL,'F M','12786','22','Hampshire',1,'',0,''),
