 (22090,22090,'Unknown','GEORGE EDWARD','RUST','2nd Corporal',18,'South African Engineers',798,'Unknown',0,'1919-06-14','Died of alcoholism and pneumonia, at Johannesburg Hospital','Husband of Lucy Martha Rust, of 85 Frere Street, West Bank, East London. Born Komgha, Cape Province. Previous service in Queenstown Rifles, W. P. Mounted Rifles and South African Irish. One records states that he died of alcoholism and pneumonia, at Johannesburg Hospital, and another says he died of strychnine poisoning. Records indicate that he lost his left limb in service 29 March 1918, and that he was demobbed 28-May-1919, but entered hospital on 8 June 1919 due to the effects of malaria that he contracted on military service','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (BRAAMFONTEIN) CEMETERY',1219,'-26.19379','28.02763 ','Hospital Sec. Grave 22836. No headstone.',NULL,'G E','E/88','53','Gauteng',1,'***Accepted by CWGC for War Grave Status & burial site under investigation',0,''),
