 (22199,22199,'Unknown','LEONARD WILLIAM','SAMPSON','Lieutenant',334,'First City/Cape Town Highlanders, S.A. Forces',332,'Unknown',0,'1944-07-22','Died of wounds, near Greve, Tuscany. He was Platoon Commander, No 3 Pl, B Coy and during the advance toward Greve, the platoon came under heavy shellfire and withdrew to a nearby house. At approx 11 am the house received 3 direct hits from hostile shelling, wounding Lt Samson. He later died of his wounds','Husband of Mrs. E. L. Sampson, of Salisbury, Southern Rhodesia.','Italy',39,'FLORENCE WAR CEMETERY',866,'43.77016','11.34284 ','XI. A. 7.',NULL,'L W','SR/598322V','27','',0,'',0,''),
