 (22318,22318,'Unknown','ERIC','SAVILLE','Second Lieutenant',475,'Royal Berkshire Regiment',649,'1st Bn.',528,'1918-10-08','Killed in action','Son of Mr. W. Saville, of 193, North Ridge Rd., Durban, South Africa. Born at Amatikulu, Natal.','France',27,'FORENVILLE MILITARY CEMETERY',872,'50.13511','3.28076 ','A. 5.',NULL,'E','','21','Nord',1,'',0,''),
 (22319,22319,'Unknown','ERIC COWLEY','SAVILLE','Major',343,'South African Air Force',775,'260 (R.A.F.) Sqdn.',837,'1943-09-19','Killed in action, flying low into intense Breda fire','Son of William C. and Marjorie Saville, of Richmond, Natal, South Africa.','Italy',39,'NAPLES WAR CEMETERY',1765,'40.88539','14.23985 ','III. P. 11.',NULL,'E C','103255V','21','',0,'Bar to DFC LG Sup 8 December 1942 pg. 5337 - "One day in October, 1942, this officer led a formation of fighter aircraft on an interception patrol. A number of Messerschmitt 109s was observed and engaged after a short .pursuit. During the combat, Captain Saville destroyed 2 enemy aircraft. Subsequently, he skilfully led his formation to base where, in spite of .difficulties a perfect landing was effected. This officer has invariably displayed outstanding leadership, great courage and devotion to duty. Since being awarded the Distinguished Flying Cross he has destroyed at least 3 enemy aircraft."; DFC LG Sup 18 Sept 1942 pg. 4061 - "In recognition of gallantry displayed in flying operations against the enemy"; USA DFC LG Sup 16 June 1944 - "In recognition of valuable services rendered in connection with the war"',0,''),
