 (22322,22322,'Unknown','HARRY','SAVORY','Private',429,'4th Dragoon Guards (Royal Irish)',108,'Unknown',0,'1914-09-13','Killed in action','Third son of Thomas William and Ellen Savory, of Warham, Norfolk; husband of Edith Savory, of Sculthorpe, Fakenham, Norfolk. Was a settler in Rhodesia in 1896, and served throughout the whole of the Matabele War; served as Lt. in Imperial Light Horse, in the South African Campaign (Queen&#39;s Medal with 4 bars, King&#39;s Medal with 2 bars). Volunteered for active service at the outbreak of Great War.','France',27,'BOURG-ET-COMIN COMMUNAL CEMETERY',320,'49.3966','3.65535 ','7.',NULL,'H','GS/6692','','Aisne',1,'LG 27 Sept 1901 - No citation',0,''),
