 (22327,22327,'Unknown','CONRAD GORDON','SAXBY','Lieutenant Colonel',339,'New Zealand Maori (Pioneer) Battalion',523,'Unknown',0,'1918-11-27','Died of pneumonia and influenza','Son of Gordon H. and Katherine Saxby, of "Quamby," 23, Orakei Rd., Remuera, Auckland. Also served in South Africa, Egypt and Gallipoli. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','United Kingdom',90,'BROOKWOOD MILITARY CEMETERY',369,'51.30022','-0.64212 ','II. F. 1.',NULL,'C G','13/2150','38','Surrey',1,'DSO LG 1 January 1917 "For good work and devotion to duty during the period August 27th/October 2nd 1916. During this period Major Saxby commanded &#39;A&#39; Company N.Z. Pioneers, and his coolness under fire and he set a splendid example, were an inspiration to the men working under fire. His company work was always laid off with sound judgement and well carried out." MID LG 4 January 1917 "Mentioned in despatch from General Sir Douglas Haig, G.C.B., Commander-in-Chief of the British Armies in France, dated 13th November, 1916."',0,''),
