 (22335,22335,'Unknown','THOMAS EARLE GORDON','SCAIFE','Second Lieutenant',475,'Royal Flying Corps',661,'9th Sqdn.',1728,'1916-09-26','Killed in action, observer on BE2c, shot down by AA fire over Lesboeufs (Somme)','Son of Thomas Earle Scaife and Clara Scaife, of Burnholme, Robertson, Cape Province, South Africa. On Montague, Western Cape War Memorial','France',27,'ARRAS FLYING SERVICES MEMORIAL',95,'50.287','2.76039 ','',NULL,'T E G','','24','Pas de Calais',147,'LG 22 September 1916 - "For conspicuous gallantry and skill when on contact patrol work during active operations, often flying low under heavy fire. On one occasion, when flying at 1,000 feet, his petrol tanks were pierced by shell fire. He managed to stop the holes and enabled his pilot to bring the machine home."',147,'and 6th Dragoon Guards (Carabiniers)'),
