 (22500,22500,'Unknown','REGINALD OSCAR','SCHWARZ','Major',343,'King&#39;s Royal Rifle Corps',424,'6th Bn.',1493,'1918-11-18','Died of influenza','Son of Robert George Schwarz (merchant, of W. Kensington and of Bagshot, Surrey). B. May 4, 1875, at Lee, Kent. School, St Paul&#39;s, London. Matric. Michs. 1893. Football (rugby) &#39;blue,&#39; 1893; played for England, 1899, 1901. Played cricket for South Africa v. England, 1904, 1906, 1907, 1910, 1912; v. Australia, 1912. In a London office, 1895-7. Member of the London stock exchange, 1899-1902. On Staff of the South African Railways, Johannesburg, 1902-4. Member of Johannesburg stock exchange, 1904-11; of the London stock exchange from 1911. Served in the Great War, 1914-19 (Capt., S. African Infantry; Major, King&#39;s R.R.C.; D.A.Q.M.G.; Asst. Controller of salvage; wounded; M.C.; mentioned in despatches). South African Cricketer - played in twenty test matches.','France',27,'ETAPLES MILITARY CEMETERY',816,'50.53497','1.62468 ','XLV. A. 4.',NULL,'R O','','43','Pas de Calais',452,'LG Sup 1 January 1917 pg. 41',452,'attd. H.Q., 1st Echelon'),
