 (22797,22797,'Unknown','HARRY','SEVEL','Stoker 1st Class',539,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Dorsetshire',2284,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. DORSETSHIRE and her sister ship Cornwall were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of Simon and Rose Sevel, of Durban, Natal, South Africa. ***Jewish','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'H','68100','33','Devon',1,'',0,''),
