 (23139,23139,'Unknown','ALEXANDER','SIMMS','Captain',115,'Royal Engineers',659,'Unknown',0,'1918-09-12','Drowned at sea (from S.S. "Galway Castle"), as a result of an attack by an enemy submarine 160 miles S.W. and .5 S. of the Fastnet','ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','United Kingdom',90,'HOLLYBROOK MEMORIAL, SOUTHAMPTON',1156,'50.93384','-1.43114 ','Panel 48.',NULL,'A','','','Hampshire',1,'LG Sup 25 August 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty in carrying out surveys under continuous shell fire. By his disregard of danger he was able to furnish our guns with important data to enable them to keep up an accurate fire as they advanced. The use of delicate instruments under such conditions demands no ordinary nerve and steadiness." MID LG Sup 18 May 1917 pg. 4878',0,''),
