 (23856,23856,'Unknown','NOEL WILLIAM','SPENCE','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Cornwall',2279,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. CORNWALL and her sister ship Dorsetshire were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of David S. and Isabel G. Spence, of Glenwood, Durban, Natal, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'N W','68732','19','Devon',2,'',0,''),
