 (23858,23858,'Unknown','WILLIAM JOHN HECTOR','SPENCE','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1916-10-12','Killed in action. On the 12th October 1916, the 2nd and 4th S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The assault died away because of machine guns nests, placed well back in prepared positions, which caught the attacking waves at long range.','Son of William Spence, of Lindley, Orange Free State. Born in Elgin, Scotland','France',27,'WARLENCOURT BRITISH CEMETERY',2680,'50.08079','2.79911 ','I. D. 32.',NULL,'W J H','8632','28','Pas de Calais',10,'',10,'"B" Coy.'),
