 (23932,23932,'Unknown','CHARLES LORAINE SCOTT','ST. LEGER','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'South African Infantry',807,'H.Q. 3rd Bde.',2405,'1941-12-14','Died of dysentery','Son of Charles L. St. Leger and Margaret S. St. Leger; husband of Florence B. St. Leger, of Durban, Natal, South Africa. One of Durban&#39;s most promising cricketing figures. He played for Durban Central and then went to Greyville to help that old club reestablish itself. In addition, he was a member of the Durban Cricket Union for years and served as a member of the Natal Selection Committee.','Egypt',23,'KANTARA WAR MEMORIAL CEMETERY',1243,'30.87194','32.33173 ','C. 141A.',NULL,'C L S','7956','45','',0,'',0,''),
 (23933,23933,'Unknown','FREDERICK ANTHONY','ST. LEGER','Lance Bombardier',310,'South African Artillery',784,'4 Field Regt.',1138,'1942-09-10','Died of bacilliform dysentery','Son of Dr. A. Y. St. Ledger, of Rondebosch and Mrs. E. St. Ledger, of Grahamstown. Husband of Sheila Courtenay St. Ledger, of "Lorraine", P.O. Grahamstown. Born Pretoria. A farmer. Educated at St. Andrew&#39;s College, Grahamstown. On Grahamstown Cathedral Parish Church memorial.','Libya',45,'BENGHAZI WAR CEMETERY',217,'32.07696','20.08936 ','6. B. 8.',NULL,'F A','8785','32','',0,'',0,''),
