 (23945,23945,'Unknown','ARTHUR REEVE','STAINBANK','Second Lieutenant',475,'Royal Field Artillery',660,'113th Bde.',242,'1917-07-20','Killed in action','Son of Ethel Stainbank, of Coedmore, Bellair, Natal, South Africa, and the late Dering Lee Warner Stainbank. Served in the German West African War; at the conclusion he came to England and was gazetted to R.F.A. His brother William Dering also fell, he is commemorated on his brother&#39;s headstone. Buried 100 yards east of Potyze-Zillebeke Road, Zillebeke. Played rugby for Natal 1912 to 1914','Belgium',10,'YPRES (MENIN GATE) MEMORIAL',2785,'50.8521','2.89138 ','Panel 5 and 9.',NULL,'A R','','23','Ieper, West-Vlaanderen',1,'',0,''),
