 (23982,23982,'Unknown','GEOFFREY GEORGE','STANNARD','Leading Telegraphist',327,'Royal Navy',685,'H.M.S. Dorsetshire',2284,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. DORSETSHIRE and her sister ship Cornwall were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of George and Maud Stannard; husband of Doreen Constance Stannard, of Wynberg, Cape Town, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PORTSMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',2031,'50.78242','-1.09599 ','Panel 66, Column 3.',NULL,'G G','P/JX 128470','31','Hampshire',2,'',0,''),
