 (24088,24088,'Unknown','ERIC BERKELEY','STEPHEN','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Cornwall',2279,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. CORNWALL and her sister ship Dorsetshire were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','Son of William Mitchell and Vera Hutchinson Clarke Stephen, of Green Point, Cape Town, South Africa.','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'E B','68861','21','Devon',1,'',0,''),
