 (24101,24101,'Unknown','LIONEL','STEPHENS','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'South African Air Force',775,'34 Sqdn.',1033,'1945-04-04','Killed in action, 8 crew (1 RAF), after returning froma bombing raid on the Brescia marshalling yards in Northern Italy, Liberator collided with an RAF Wellington bomber KL355 from 70 Sqdn while circling Celone airfield to land, in Liberator B24J Mk VI #KK302','Son of William Henry and Ida Millicent Stephens, of Kensington, Johannesburg. Born Kraal, Heidelberg District. A clerk with South African Railways by profession. His father also died in service in WW2','Italy',39,'BARI WAR CEMETERY',155,'41.06481','16.8947 ','XIII. B. 7.',NULL,'L','607248V','19','',0,'',0,''),
 (24102,24102,'Unknown','REGINALD CRAWFORD','STEPHENS','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of Annie Elizabeth and the late Michael Stephens, of Ardlin, Rosebank, Cape Province. On Rondebosch War Memorial in St. Paul&#39;s Anglican Churchyard','France',27,'THIEPVAL MEMORIAL',2498,'50.05081','2.68569 ','Pier and Face 4 C.',NULL,'R C','8122','37','Somme',6,'',6,'"A" Coy.'),
