 (24233,24233,'Unknown','EDWARD','STILES','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry',807,'1st Regt.',556,'1916-10-18','Killed in action. On the 18th October 1916, at 3.40 am, three companies of the 1st S.A.I. attacked Snag and Tail Trenches. The B Coy failed to realize that they had reached Snag Trench and continued beyond it. They had lost touch with their flanks and only some men succeeded to come back. Only a block was established at 50 metres of The Pimple. The D Company launched an attack at 5.45 pm and Snag Trench was occupied but the machine-gun fire from the Butte de Warlencourt took a heavy toll, leaving a small group in the trench.','Son of James and Mary Stiles, of 118 Long Street, Cape Town. Husband of Violet Maud Mabel Stiles. Born Dulu, London. A station master. His brother also died in service','France',27,'OVILLERS MILITARY CEMETERY',1896,'50.02841','2.69196 ','XVII. Y. 10.',NULL,'E','807','42','Somme',6,'',6,'"A" Coy.'),
