 (24806,24806,'Unknown','CHARLES LIVINGSTONE','TAYLOR','Captain',115,'East Lancashire Regiment',314,'8th Bn.',1665,'1918-03-24','Killed in action','Son of Mr. and Mrs. C. J. Taylor, of Melrose, Johannesburg, Transvaal.','France',27,'POZIERES MEMORIAL',2045,'50.03448','2.71475 ','Panel 42 and 43.',NULL,'C L','','34','Somme',313,'LG Sup 16 August 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He rendered most valuable service as intelligence officer during the assault. On his own initiative he made several daring reconnaissances and obtained information which was of the utmost value."',313,'attd. 2nd Bn.'),
