 (24813,24813,'Unknown','EWERT ARTHUR','TAYLOR','Flying Officer',259,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'12 Sqdn.',284,'1943-12-02','Killed in action, target Berlin','Nicknamed "Ding". Entered Lloyd House in January 1934. He left Plumtree in December 1939, and before attesting in the R.A.F. he was working at the Magistrate&#39;s Court, Bulawayo. School Record: House Prefect, 1938-1939; Rugger 1st XV, 19&#39;38-1939 (Colours 1938-1939); Cricket, Under 13 and Under 14 School team; Sergeant in Cadets; active member of Debating Society; Matriculated in December 1939. On Plumtree School Roll of Honour','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 129.',NULL,'E A','80477','22','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
