 (24834,24834,'Unknown','IVOR NORMAN LAWRENCE','TAYLOR','Captain',115,'South African Air Force',775,'40 Sqdn.',1162,'1944-06-13','Killed in action, shot down by flak near Orvieto, in Supermarine Spitfire Mk VC #EF738','Son of Leslie and Constance Taylor, of Selukwe, Southern Rhodesia.','Italy',39,'BOLSENA WAR CEMETERY',298,'42.58562','11.99863 ','II, C, 2.',NULL,'I N L','205516V','24','',0,'LG Sup 2 November 1943 pg. 4814 - "In September 1943, this officer located a large enemy camp, with its lines of armoured cars, some 25 miles from one of our forward airfields. In the face of intense anti-aircraft fire, Captain Taylor flew over the encampment at a height of only 50 feet to complete the reconnaissance. He returned to base and afterwards led a bomber force to the target which was attacked with great success. Captain Taylor displayed outstanding gallantry and devotion to duty and his example was worthy of the highest praise."',0,''),
