 (25368,25368,'Unknown','REGINALD CAMPBELL','TOMLINSON','Major',343,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'Unknown',0,'1944-10-24','Died of wounds, received in action in the vicinity of Salvaro, near Monte Pezza, Italy. He received severe shrapnel wounds to his legs, requiring a double amputation. He did not survive the operation','Son of Major Reginald and Ellen Tomlinson, of P.O. Box 271, Pietermaritzburg. Born Pietermaritzburg. A farmer near Rosetta, Natal. His brother also died in service.','Italy',39,'CASTIGLIONE SOUTH AFRICAN CEMETERY',483,'44.14397','11.16183 ','I, A, 25.',NULL,'R C','215V','30','',0,'MC LG Sup 16 April 1942 pg. 1694, MID LG Sup 15 September 1942 pg. 5448',10,'"B" Coy.'),
 (25369,25369,'Unknown','ROBERT DUNCAN CAMPBELL','TOMLINSON','Flight Sergeant',257,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'Unknown',0,'1942-03-18','Killed in action, operations over Norway. PRU-Spitfire R7035 failed to return after take off from Wick. When he reached Britain on his return the cloud was so thick he did not know where he was. An aircraft was heard overhead at the airfield he was supposed to land at, and at the time he was expected to arrive. His aircraft was never found, so it was assumed he ran out of fuel somewhere over the sea.','Son of (Major) Reginald and Ellen Tomlinson, of Pietermaritzburg, Natal, South Africa. His brother also died in service','United Kingdom',90,'RUNNYMEDE MEMORIAL',2216,'51.43804','-0.56503 ','Panel 76.',NULL,'R D C','905231','30','Surrey',1,'',0,''),
