 (25456,25456,'Unknown','JOHN FREDERICK ALFRED','TREHEARN','Sergeant',492,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'102 Sqdn.',164,'1943-07-30','Killed in action, Halifax W7883, on the night of 29/30 July 1943 on their first operational sortie. They were part of a force of 777 aircraft - 340 Lancasters, 244 Halifaxes, 119 Stirlings, 70 Wellingtons, 4 Mosquitos being dispatched to Hamburg. The intention was to approach Hamburg from almost due north and bomb those northern and north-eastern districts which had so far not been bombed. At 22.39 they were airborne from Pockington, shot down at 00:57 by a night- fighter (Lt Gotthard Sachsenberg, 11./NJG3 flying a Dornier 217) from 18,000 feet, crashing at Todesfelde, 6 miles of Bad Segeberg killing all the seven man crew','Son of John Griffiths Trehearn and Marion Alice Trehearn, of Durban, Natal, South Africa.','Germany',29,'HAMBURG CEMETERY',1048,'53.61975','10.03544 ','4A. A. 3.',NULL,'J F A','1267812','','Hamburg, Hamburg',1,'',0,''),
