 (26281,26281,'Unknown','UNKNOWN SOLDIER','UNKNOWN SOLDIER','Rank Unknown',443,'South African Infantry',807,'4th Regt.',1270,'1917-09-20','Killed in action, during attack on Borry Farm','Buried July 9th, 2013. The remains of the three soldiers were found near a brick factory in Zonnebeke at the end of 2011. Indications are that these soldiers were never formally buried, but that their graves were covered during battle by mortar/artillery fire. Based on objects recovered, including unit insignia, as well as the location of the find, the remains were accepted as that of three unknown South African Soldiers that formed part of the 4th Regiment South African Infantry.','Belgium',10,'TYNE COT CEMETERY',2551,'50.88699','2.99771 ','XXXII. E. 13',NULL,'','','','Zonnebeke, West-Vlaanderen',1,'',0,''),
