 (26439,26439,'Unknown','OWEN PATRICK','UNSWORTH','Ordinary Seaman',389,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Barham',2265,'1941-11-25','Killed in action, while steaming to cover an attack on Italian convoys, HMS Barham was hit by three torpedoes from the German submarine U-331. As she rolled over to port, her after magazines exploded and the ship quickly sank with the loss of over two-thirds of her crew','Son of Henry and Mary C. Unsworth, of Liverpool. (Served as JEVON, R.K.)','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 58, Column 3.',NULL,'O P','69089','22','Devon',1,'',0,''),
 (26440,26440,'Unknown','ARTHUR EDWARD','UPTON','Private',429,'South African Infantry',807,'2nd Regt.',925,'1917-04-12','Killed in action, in the improvised and disastrous attack of the 9th (Scottish) Division on the German positions in the East of Fampoux. The 2nd SAI, who went in 400 strong, lost 16 officers and 285 men.','Son of James Upton. Born at Islington, London, England.','France',27,'BROWN&#39;S COPSE CEMETERY, ROEUX',371,'50.30288','2.88379 ','I. E. 12.',NULL,'A E','8051','41','Pas de Calais',1,'',0,''),
 (26441,26441,'Unknown','FRANCIS CLIVE RAMSDEN','UPTON','Second Lieutenant',475,'Canterbury Regiment, N.Z.E.F.',246,'Unknown',0,'1916-10-02','Killed in action','Son of Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Evererd Upton, of Ashburton, Canterbury. Previously wounded at Gallipoli. He was well known as an amateur boxer, and played football with the Christchurch 1st fifteen." (Chronicles of the N.Z.E.F. December 27 1916 p. 209). ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918.','France',27,'CATERPILLAR VALLEY (NEW ZEALAND) MEMORIAL',488,'50.02563','2.79247 ','',NULL,'F C R','6/854','25','Somme',1,'LG 25 November 1916, p11551: "For conspicuous gallantry in action. He led his platoon with great courage and initiative, and organised a bombing party to repel an enemy attack. Later, he carried out most valuable reconnaissance."',0,''),
