 (27936,27936,'Unknown','EDWARD LYNDEN','WEBBER','Lieutenant',334,'Lincolnshire Regiment',437,'6th Bn.',1493,'1915-08-07','Killed in action','Son of Benjamin M. and Millicent A. Webber, of Bedford, Cape Province, South Africa. born 1/12/1883. Of Rhodesia. Educated at St. Andrew&#39;s College, Grahamstown. At St Andrew&#39;s from July 1894-1898. When war broke out he got a commission with the Lincolnshire regiment and was sent to the Dardanelles in 1915. He was killed on 7th August of that year. In a letter to this man&#39;s brother his adjutant writes that they were ordered to take hill 53. Webber and a Captain Buck reached the top of the hill first where Webber was killed by a wounded Turk who fired at him from the bottom of the trench. The adjutant buried Webber on the top of the hill, Yilghen Burnu, and placed a cross and inscription over him.','Turkey',87,'GREEN HILL CEMETERY',995,'40.29303','26.27983 ','II. B. 4.',NULL,'E L','','31','',0,'',0,''),
