 (27954,27954,'Unknown','DONALD GORDON','WEBSTER','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Air Force',775,'150 (R.A.F.) Sqdn.',380,'1944-04-21','On the night of April 21, 1944 the Wellington LN385, belonging to 150 Squadron of the RAF base at Amendola in Puglia, on a bombing run to Porto Santo Stefano in Tuscany. On his return from the operation, near the coast of Salerno, the bomber had to undergo an air strike. At 23:23 the report states that a request was heard coming from the plane of MD-Q LN385. It was heard again weakly at 01:06 on April 22, after which radio contact was lost','Son of Margaret T. Webster. Born East London. see also http://www.aircrewremembrancesociety.com/raf1944/3/nusseyadw.html?hl=de&q=south+africa','Italy',39,'SALERNO WAR CEMETERY',2243,'40.62508','14.92202 ','I. E. 2.',NULL,'D G','103442V','24','',0,'',0,''),
