 (28157,28157,'Unknown','GEORGE MASTERMAN','THOMPSON','Lieutenant',334,'Royal Scots',693,'1st Bn.',528,'1914-08-22','Killed in action, while attempting to storm the German trenches, on the enemy&#39;s left, at Chra Village','Son of Col. George William Thompson, (Commanding Royal Scots), and Mrs G. W. Thompson, of Beechwood, Burley, Hants. Born Eshowe, Zululand. The First British Officer killed in action in the war. A Special French Army Order was published on 20th October commending his gallantry and the fine example he gave to the French soldiers temporarily under his command. Commemorated on War Memorial in Burley, Hampshire','Togo',96,'WAHALA CEMETERY',2957,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'G M','','24','',0,'',159,'and General List'),
