 (28164,28164,'Unknown','WILLIAM JOHN','WHEELER','Major',343,'South African Air Force',775,'4 Sqdn.',1151,'1944-01-23','Killed in action, hit by flak near Pescara, in Supermarine Spitfire Mk VC #ES292. His wingman reported that the aircraft was trailing Glycol (engine coolant). To which he turned the aircraft back towards the coast and prepared to bale out. The aircraft went into a dive and after a short while was seen to exit, his parachute did not open properly and fell to his death. The Germans recovered his body and buried him in the local cemetery, which was later pointed out by locals to the searcher party','Son of John Roux and Elizabeth Catharina Johanna Wheeler, of Johannesburg, Transvaal, South Africa. Born Witbank. Worked as clerk with South African Railways and Harbours. Matriculated at Forest High School Johannesburg, Head prefect 1938, Volunteered for the SAAF and pilot training in 1940.','Italy',39,'MORO RIVER CANADIAN WAR CEMETERY',1714,'42.33623','14.41678 ','XII. D. 4.',NULL,'W J','103839V','24','',0,'LG Sup 2 June 1943 pg. 2460',0,''),
 (28165,28165,'Unknown','DORIEN DUDLEY','WHEELWRIGHT','Corporal',166,'Kaffrarian Rifles, S.A. Forces',415,'Unknown',0,'1944-09-27','Killed in action. In the North Italian village of Carpane on 27 September 1944 the Germans executed 16 Allied soldiers captured fighting with Italian partisans in that area. Escaped with other South Africans from a nearby POW camp and joined up with local partisans to carry on fighting the Germans. They became such a thorn in the flesh of the Germans that a special operation was mounted in the Monte Grappa region to capture them. They were eventually captured and murdered by the Germans. Every year on this day since the end of the war the villagers of Carpane have held a memorial service at this spot by the side of the road where they were killed. For many years the identity of the 16 was not known and the monument was simply inscribed to "16 unknown". It was only about 4 or 5 years ago that their identity was uncovered by Sonia Residori, an Italian academic researcher','Son of Guy Dudley and Maud Lilian Wheelwright; husband of Johanna Viola Pohl Wheelwright, of Lusikisiki, Cape Province, South Africa. On Jeppe High School for Boys Roll of Honour','Italy',39,'PADUA WAR CEMETERY',1910,'45.42165','11.83996 ','I. A. 9.',NULL,'D D','11607','41','',0,'',0,''),
