 (28187,28187,'Unknown','ARTHUR JAMES','WHITE','Third Officer',576,'Merchant Navy',474,'S.S. Derrynane (London)',2910,'1941-02-12','On February 12, 1941, SS Derrynane was in convoy SLS.64, with a cargo of iron ore from Lourenco Marques, when the convoy was attacked by the German heavy cruiser Admiral Hipper. The position was 37.12N, 21.20W (about 400 miles S.E. of the Azores). Derrynane was the second vessel to be hit by shellfire and blew up killing all those on board; the master (Earnest Joice), thirty four crew members and one DEMS gunner.','Son of Frederick James and Annie Mary White. Ex-Cadet of the South African Training Ship General Botha. Commemoration stone in King William&#39;s Town Cemetery','United Kingdom',90,'TOWER HILL MEMORIAL',2527,'51.50955','-0.07769 ','Panel 35.',NULL,'A J','','22','London',1,'',0,''),
