 (28231,28231,'Unknown','BARTLETT WALLACE','WHITECROSS','Private',429,'Royal Natal Carbineers, S.A. Forces',679,'1st',515,'1942-07-27','Killed in action, in an operation in the vicinity of El Alamein. The Regiment had been tasked to lift an enemy minefield to create a gap for 69 Bde and an Armoured Bde to pass through. Casualties were inflicted by severe MG fire and artillery bombardment','Son of Bartlett Bonniman Whitecross, of Fort Beaufort and Mabel Iris van der Vyver (formerly Whitecross), of Garcia Street, Cambridge, East London. Born in Pretoria. A baker.','Egypt',23,'EL ALAMEIN WAR CEMETERY',775,'30.83819','28.94707 ','IV. H. 27.',NULL,'B W','136642','21','',0,'',0,''),
