 (28542,28542,'Unknown','WALTER NOEL','WILLIAMSON','Able Seaman',25,'South African Naval Forces',831,'H.M.S. Dorsetshire',2284,'1942-04-05','Killed in action. DORSETSHIRE and her sister ship Cornwall were detached from the Fleet when they were sighted by Japanese aircraft. A little later they were overwhelmed by approximately 50 dive-bombers whose accurate attack sank both ships quickly; 190 of Cornwall&#39;s crew of 650 were lost.','No additional information known at this time','United Kingdom',90,'PLYMOUTH NAVAL MEMORIAL',1989,'50.36573','-4.14223 ','Panel 74, Column 2.',NULL,'W N','67803','','Devon',2,'',0,''),
