 (28548,28548,'Unknown','JAMES OWEN','WILLIS','Wing Commander',606,'Royal Air Force',635,'45 Sqdn.',1215,'1941-11-22','Killed in action, Blenheim IV Z6439, at Libya','Son of the late George Willis, of 57 Heathfield Avenue. Of Southern Rhodesia. His brother Francis also died in service.','Libya',45,'KNIGHTSBRIDGE WAR CEMETERY, ACROMA',1344,'32.09586','23.71913 ','2. B. 9.',NULL,'J O','32059','','',0,'LG 30 May 1941 pg. 3095 - "This officer has displayed the utmost determination in action against the enemy. In May, 1941, he led a force of fighter aircraft in an attack against a moving transport column of some 100 vehicles, the majority of which were either destroyed or damaged. His leadership has been of a high order."',0,''),
