 (28561,28561,'Unknown','EDWARD JOHN','WILLS','Corporal',166,'Auckland Regiment, N.Z.E.F.',191,'3rd Bn.',1097,'1917-10-05','Died of wounds','Son of Edward John and Kate Eliza Wills, of 662, Gloucester Street, East Christchurch, New Zealand. ref. South African Roll of Honour 1914-1918','Belgium',10,'NINE ELMS BRITISH CEMETERY',1814,'50.85095','2.69701 ','II. E. 2.',NULL,'E J','29119','21','Poperinge, West-Vlaanderen',1,'LG Sup 17 December 1917, pg. 13202 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty, at Gravenstafel on 4/10/1917. During the advance he led his section in the attack and just before reaching the objective had his arm blown off. With a splendid determination he refused all assistance, ordered his men to push on and by coolness and courage, he steadied them at a trying period. He has always shown a fine devotion to duty."',0,''),
