 (28856,28856,'Unknown','STEPHEN HUGH JAMES','WOULFE-FLANAGAN','Lieutenant Colonel',339,'Royal Indian Army Service Corps',668,'Unknown',0,'1942-12-19','Died on active service','Son of Stephen and Gertrude Woulfe-Flanagan; husband of Margaret Woulfe-Flanagan, of Cape Town, South Africa. Stephen Hugh James Woulfe-Flanagan was born on 9 February 1900. He was first commissioned Unatt. 2-Lt. 17/12/19. I.A. 2-Lt. 2/5/20. Lt. 17/12/20. Capt. 17/12/26. Maj. 17/12/37. Staff Capt. 25/2/37 to 31/7/39. Brig. Maj. 1/8/39. His India General Service 1908-35, 2 clasps, Waziristan 1919-21, North West Frontier 1930-31 (Lieut. S. H. J. Woulfe-Flanagan, 2-15 Sikhs), 2nd clasp loose was sold for 120 pounds at Dix Noonan and Webb on 21st September 2007','India',33,'MADRAS WAR CEMETERY, CHENNAI',1562,'13.01405','80.19393 ','6. A. 10.',NULL,'S H J','781/IA','42','',0,'LG 28 October 1942',0,''),
