 (28860,28860,'Unknown','ARTHUR LEONARD','WRENFORD','Lieutenant Colonel',339,'Worcestershire Regiment',975,'Unknown',0,'1918-03-21','Killed in action, at Hargicourt','Son of William Leonard Wrenford, Barrister-at-Law, and Emily Flora Mary Wrenford, of Upton Manor, Brixham, South Devon; husband of Mrs. A. L. Wrenford, of 8, South Parade, Southsea. Entered Army 1903. University (Cambridge) Commission. 4th on Sandhurst List. Served with Worcestershire Regt. in Ireland, South Africa, Ceylon, India. 3 times seconded to Northern Nigeria Regt., West Africa, where he served first months of war, 1914.','France',27,'CABARET-ROUGE BRITISH CEMETERY, SOUCHEZ',417,'50.38061','2.7416 ','XXX. F. 17.',NULL,'A L','','36','Pas de Calais',370,'',370,'attd. 4th Bn. East Lancashire Regiment'),
