 (29075,29076,'Unknown','HAROLD CHARLES','ZELM','Radio Officer',442,'United States Merchant Marine',949,'Robin Goodfellow',2840,'1944-07-25','En route, Cape Town (16 Jul) - Bahia, Brazil - New York. At 02.12 hours on 25 Jul, 1944, the unescorted Robin Goodfellow (Master Bjarne Bjornsgaard) was torpedoed and sunk by U-862 in the South Atlantic. The British motor merchant Priam received a distress signal, but none of the eight officers, 33 crewmen and 27 armed guards (the ship was armed with one 4in, one 3in and five 20mm guns) survived.','Of Cape Town, South Africa','Lost at Sea',46,'DIED AT SEA',657,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'H C','85141','33','',0,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',0,''),
