 (29176,29179,'Unknown','NAMBAHU','ABIATAL','Special Constable',517,'South West African Police',876,'South West Africa Police Counter-Insurgency Wing: Ops-K Division (KOEVOET)',3100,'1989-04-02','Killed in action, heavy fighting continued to rage throughout Northern Owamboland as large groups of heavily armed SWAPO/PLAN insurgents numbering 150+ continued with mass infiltrations into the area from Southern Angola and were constantly being engaged by Koevoet elements in the field. The Koevoet Casspirs bore the brunt of the attacks in the face of fusillades of Soviet RPG-7 anti-tank rockets, Czech RPG-75 anti-tank rockets, Yugoslavian M60 Anti-Tank rifle grenades and M60P HEAP Pencil STRIM rifle grenades. The SWAPO/PLAN insurgents paid dearly for their efforts but the South West Africa Police Counter-Insurgency Wing: Ops-K Division (Koevoet) Units suffered another ten members Killed in Action during these fierce contacts with many others being wounded','ref. "The Covert War" by Peter Stiff','South Africa',72,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Likely buried in Namibia - Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'N','','27','Unknown',1,'',0,''),
 (29177,29180,'Unknown','ELI','ABIRAM (ABRAMOWITZ)','Corporal (Rank raised to Sgt posthomously)',168,'Israeli Defence Forces',410,'Artillery (IDF site lists Medical)',1829,'1973-10-16','Killed in action, in the Yom Kippur war, in the defence of Israel','From Port Elizabeth. On Cape Town (Pinelands) Jewish Memorial. Son of Chaya and Jacob.','Israel',38,'RAMAT ZVI (MOSHAV) CEMETERY',2098,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,'E','410766','34','North',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor82.asp?t=95105',0,''),
 (29178,29181,'Unknown','ABRAHAM','ABOUD','Rifleman',462,'GROUP 34',363,'Virginia Commando',3189,'1983-01-06','Killed in action. Buffel Troop Carrier detonated a boosted anti-tank mine near the Okangwati Military Base, while on route to Sodeliet base. One of the mines used was an old British Mk 8 Anti-Tank Mine and the metal plug on top of this mine penetrated the V hull of the Buffel on the welded seam. This ignited the diesel tank and a box of white phosphorus grenades in the vehicle.','Husband of Mrs. J. E. Aboud','South Africa',72,'VIRGINIA CEMETERY',2635,'-28.11082','26.8493 ','A3',NULL,'A','76524644KT','22','Free State',1,'',0,''),
