 (29379,29382,'Unknown','KENNETH FRAMPTON','BEGHIN','Private',429,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'2 South African Infantry Battalion',654,'1973-08-07','Died in Military Vehicle Accident. While undergoing Driver and Maintenance training, he died when a Bedford struck an Eland on a narrow bridge on the Walvis Bay - Windhoek road','Son of Mr. Claude John Geoffrey and Mrs. Ruth Dawn Pascoe Beghin, of Maidstone, Hilton Road, Natal. Educated at Hilton College, Natal','South Africa',72,'HILTON (CHURCH OF THE ASCENSION) CEMETERY',2835,NULL,NULL,'Cremated and his ashes are buried at the Church of the Ascension, Hilton, Natal.',NULL,'K F','71537872N','18','Kwazulu Natal',1,'',0,''),
