 (29426,29429,'Unknown','CHRISTO FRANCOIS','BEZUIDENHOUT','Gunner',278,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'61 Mechanised Battalion Group',1442,'1983-03-06','Killed in action, on guard duty with Gnr. J. Bosse on a farm near Tsumeb, well below the danger line. A small band of terrorists sneaked up on the two and shot them at point blank range.','Western Transvaal colours in Cricket and Rugby. Grew up with Gnr. J. Boose as best friends, and had no family (having been brought up together in a childcare facility). N-O-K given as Mrs. M. L. Schultz','South Africa',72,'POTCHEFSTROOM CEMETERY',2039,'-26.71486','27.075 ','HA12',NULL,'C F','79576542BG','20','North West Province',1,'',0,''),
