 (29575,29578,'Unknown','DARYL QUINTIN','BRANDON','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'5 South African Infantry Battalion',1298,'1976-01-03','Died of wounds, during Ops Savannah while leading a patrol in a contact against a numerically superior enemy force in Central Angola approximately 30km North of Cela. On 2 January 1976 during the SADF&#39;s mop up and withdrawal from Angola, he was in command of a 5 SAI platoon approaching Cela from the north. He was advised that Cuban troops occupied the hillocks ahead of them so he led his patrol on foot in the direction of these hillocks, camping overnight in rainy weather. Early the following morning on 3 January 1976, he led a section on a reconnaissance patrol leaving Corporal Vincent Rawlings and the remainder of the platoon in their temporary base at the foot of the hill. After leading his section up a footpath to the crest of the hill, he went forward to observe the enemy positions but was immediately shot and severely wounded by enemy machine gun fire when the patrol was ambushed. At great personal risk, Corporal Rawlings moved forward and retrieved the severely wounded Officer under heavy enemy machine-gun fire, an act that earned him the Honoris Crux Silver. Unfortunately this brave young officer succumbed to his wounds and was pronounced dead on arrival at the Forward Army Surgical Hospital at Cela','Son of Mr. A. C. Brandon','South Africa',72,'DUNDEE CEMETERY',710,'-28.17535','30.22975 ','Grave 1021',NULL,'D Q','72416571BC','19','Kwazulu Natal',10,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=90271',10,'"B" Coy.'),
 (29576,29579,'Unknown','HEINRICH WILLIAM','BRAUCKMANN','Lieutenant',334,'4th Reconnaissance Regiment',111,'5 South African Infantry Battalion',1298,'1985-08-30','Died in Motor Vehicle Accident, at Langebaan.','Son of H. F. Brauckmann, of Wesselsbron.','South Africa',72,'WESSELSBRON CEMETERY',2706,NULL,NULL,'Grave 1021',NULL,'H W','78266616PE','23','Free State',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=90271',10,'"B" Coy.'),
 (29577,29580,'Unknown','SIMAO DOMINGOS','BRAZ','Staff Sergeant',531,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1980-06-04','Died of wounds, received south of Mutuanjamba (approx. 80km inside Angola) during first phase of Operation Sceptic, specifically area clearing and domination as well as establishment of tactical HQ at Mulemba.','Joao was badly wounded and Braz and Van Der Walt were killed when their patrol crossed a gravel road in the kill zone of a vehicle ambush. Large force of dug in SWAPO with mortars and machine guns were able to inflict casualties and pin the patrol down. Reinforcements dislodged the ambushing force, but were forced to secure the immediate area and attend to casualties rather than pursue the enemy. When 2Lt Van Der Walt was hit, Braz went to his aid and was hit multiple times by the same dug in PKM machine gun. Braz was alive when casevac arrived, but died moments later.','Namibia',56,'KIMBO CEMETERY, BUFFALO',1304,NULL,NULL,'OLD SEC 143',NULL,'S D','76928100SP','27','Caprivi',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=90271',10,'"B" Coy.'),
