 (29584,29587,'Unknown','PIET M','BREYTENBACH','Warrant Officer Class I',594,'South African Air Force',775,'83 Technical Supply Depot',1644,'2002-11-18','Died in Freak Accident, was busy with the identification of unexploded aircraft-mounted bombs and ammunition at the Roodewal bombing range outside Polokwane (Pietersburg) when a mortar exploded after he had picked it up. He was part of the clearing crew based at the range, which was used by the SAAF.','ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'P M','81309981BT','22','Gauteng',118,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=90271',118,'Air Force'),
