 (29621,29624,'Unknown','MARK ANDREW','BROWN','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'Kaffrarian Rifles',2488,'1965-12-02','Died of heat exhaustion, heat exhaustion during a training session at the Infantry School in Oudtshoorn. The heat was reported at over 37 Degrees C during the training session. As a direct result of the findings of Board of Enquiry held into his death, training procedures were modified and amended','Son of Mrs. K. M. Brown','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Panel 01',NULL,'M A','61089728N','21','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=90271',99,'452 Parachute Battalion'),
