 (29804,29807,'Unknown','JACQUES','COETZER','Major',343,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'1 South African Infantry Battalion',114,'1999-09-16','Lieutenant Sibusiso Madubela started shooting at white soldiers early in the day because of a salary problem, which he caused by himself for AWOL. He started at the Officer Commanding&#39;s office and worked his way through the unit. Some of the other soldiers started chasing him to try and stop him in his rampage. Eventually two soldiers got hold of guns and ammunition and a "mini war" broke out between them. They finally stopped him in his tracks after killing Sgt Nell when they shot and killed him. He wounded 4 others during the shooting rampage','Husband of Mrs. L. Coetzer','South Africa',72,'BLOEMFONTEIN (SOUTHPARK) CEMETERY',282,NULL,NULL,'Block 27 Grave No 593',NULL,'J','84478957PE','31','Free State',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3069 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (29805,29808,'Unknown','JOHAN ADAM','COETZER','Colonel',143,'South African Commandos',791,'Danie Theron Combat School',2071,'1982-07-14','Died in Aircraft Accident, Crashed following mid-air collision with Piper Pa-31 Navajo ZS-KTX over Swartkops., in Swearingen Merlin 4A #ZS-JLZ. The collision occurred when returning from Namibia and on final approach to Waterkloof Air Base and the Navajo was on final approach to Wonderboom Airport.','Husband of Mrs. J. A. Coetzer','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','Grave 1175',NULL,'J A','01166180PE','55','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3069 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
