 (29897,29900,'Unknown','GERALD PEREIRA','DA SILVA','Rifleman',462,'GROUP 34',363,'Sandriver Commando',3036,'1983-01-07','Died of burn wounds, at 1 Mil Hospital. Wounded in a landmine explosion on 6 January when their Buffel detonated a boosted anti-tank mine near the Okangwati Military Base, while on route to Sodeliet base. One of the mines used was an old British Mk 8 Anti-Tank Mine and the metal plug on top of this mine penetrated the V hull of the Buffel on the welded seam. This ignited the diesel tank and a box of white phosphorus grenades in the vehicle.','Husband of Mrs. F. Da Silva, of Riebeeckstad, Welkom.','South Africa',72,'WELKOM CEMETERY',2694,NULL,NULL,'A20',NULL,'G P','70256961KT','28','Free State',1,'OBE LG Sup 31 December 1976 - "New Years Honours", MC LG 15 December 1972 - "In recognition of distinguished service in Northern Ireland during the period 1 August 1971 to 31 October 1971", MID LG Sup 19 September 1978 - "In recognition of gallant and distinguished service in Northern Ireland"',179,'Army'),
