 (30228,30231,'Unknown','DANE F S','ELSON','Lance Corporal',311,'Welsh Guards',962,'1st Battalion',524,'2009-07-05','Killed in action, while on patrol in Babaji as part of Operation PANCHAI PALANG in Helmand province, Afghanistan','He was part of a Fire Support Group from the 1st Battalion Welsh Guards, attached to The Light Dragoons Battle Group. Born in Harare, Zimbabwe, He was part of a Fire Support Group from the 1st Battalion Welsh Guards, attached to The Light Dragoons Battle Group. He served in Iraq in 2004/05, and in Bosnia in 2006/07. He passed a promotion course and was promoted to Lance Corporal during the pre-deployment training for Afghanistan. Lance Corporal Elson was a keen rugby player and he lived for the mates he had around him in the Welsh Guards. He had a very bright future ahead of him, and stood out as a Guardsman destined for the higher ranks of the battalion.','United Kingdom',90,'PENCOED CEMETERY',1930,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'D F S','25176709','22','Glamorganshire',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=512204',179,'Army'),
 (30229,30232,'Unknown','DENNIS MICHAEL','ELWORTHY','Trooper',581,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'2 Special Service Battalion',655,'1978-08-23','Killed in action, during the early hours of the morning when the bungalow in which they were sleeping at Katima Mulilo received a direct hit from a Soviet GRAD-P 122mm High Explosive Katyusha Rocket. SWAPO/PLAN insurgents operating from Zambia fired 20 x 122mm GRAD-P Katyusha Rockets into the town. 18 rockets exploded harmlessly in the veld, one struck a school in the Katima Mulilo Township and the other demolished the Bungalow in which the soldiers were sleeping','Son of Mrs. S. Elsworthy. Of Florida.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'CREMATED - Ashes at Garden of Remembrance, St Gabriels Anglican Church, Florida, Johannesburg. Panel 06',NULL,'D M','73246241BG','20','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=512204',179,'Army'),
