 (30416,30419,'Unknown','BRIAN ROBERT','GIBBS','Sapper',469,'South African Corps of Engineers',793,'2 Field Engineer Regiment',624,'1982-04-11','Died of accidental injuries, rifle grenade explosion, at Olifantshoek','Son of Mr. and Mrs. R. A. Gibbs, of Ladysmith.','South Africa',72,'LADYSMITH CEMETERY',1417,'-28.55551','29.79635 ','Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'B R','79464954BG','18','Kwazulu Natal',634,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98001',634,'attd. Army Battle School'),
 (30417,30420,'Unknown','CRAIG NEIL','GIBSON','Civilian',137,'Marsh & McLennan Companies, Inc.',467,'2 Field Engineer Regiment',624,'2001-09-11','Died on 97th floor, of the World Trade Center, Tower 1 (North Tower)','Born in Springs, South Africa and lived in Brooklyn, New York. Craig Gibson had a number of keen interests, starting with soccer (he played for a Manhattan team called Barnestonworth, but rooted for Liverpool) and continuing with the movies. (He had to be the first to see a new release, and there had to be plenty of popcorn on hand.) And he loved his wife, Dannielle, with whom he immigrated from Australia last December. But beginning in August, he had a new focus Daisy, the boxer puppy he gave his wife for her birthday. "He was so obsessed with this dog,"" marveled Mrs. Gibson. At the office, where Mr. Gibson, 37, was a reinsurance broker for Marsh & McLennan, "instead of doing work he&#39;d be on the Internet, looking up pet stores and buying treats for her." Sometimes he would come home in the middle of the day to take Daisy for a walk. It was hardly a one-sided affair. "She used to sleep on his slippers every night, with her little nose tucked into one of them and her paws over the top," Mrs. Gibson said. "She was mad about him."','United States of America',91,'NATIONAL 9/11 MEMORIAL, NEW YORK',1767,NULL,NULL,'North Pool: Panel N-16',NULL,'C N','79464954BG','37','New York',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98001',634,'attd. Army Battle School'),
 (30418,30421,'Unknown','LENNOX STANLEY','GIBSON','Corporal',166,'Technical Service Corps, S.A. Forces',922,'2 Field Engineer Regiment',624,'1948-11-03','Died of carcinoma of bladder, at Wynberg Military Hospital','Husband of Nora Matilda Gibson, of P.O. Bulk River, District Uitenhage. ref. 1939-45 South African Roll of Honour','South Africa',72,'CAPE TOWN (PLUMSTEAD) CEMETERY',463,'-34.02633','18.4764 ','North Pool: Panel N-16',NULL,'L S','227468','51','Western Cape',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98001',634,'attd. Army Battle School'),
 (30419,30422,'Unknown','CORNELIUS HARRY','GIJSBERS','Captain',115,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'2 Field Engineer Regiment',624,'1975-08-09','Died of leukemia, at Pretoria','Husband of Mrs. E. J. Gijsbers, of Pretoria.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','Grave 839',NULL,'C H','67541466','27','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98001',634,'attd. Army Battle School'),
