 (30627,30630,'Unknown','DESMOND BRIAN','HARMSE','Colonel',143,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'Att to SWA Command',1842,'1975-10-29','Killed in aircraft accident, in Beechcraft Baron. He had been detached on special duties as he spoke Portugese. The plane, known as "Dinky Toy" was supplied by UNITA and had been checked out by SAAF personel at Rundu. It was busy with aerial observations','Husband of Mrs. C. J. Harmse, of Pretoria. ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','Grave 853',NULL,'D B','01217066PE','46','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',22,'"E" Coy.'),
