 (30637,30640,'Unknown','GAVIN JOHN','HARVEY','Rifleman',462,'1 Parachute Battalion',7,'"B" Coy.',13,'1981-06-02','Died of wounds, severely wounded in the chest and lungs by shrapnel from a Yugoslavian M60P Pencil STRIM rifle grenade during follow-up operations against SWAPO/PLAN insurgents in conjunction with Koevoet Units on 22 May 1981. He was evacuated to the Hospital in Grootfontein where he was stabilised before being evacuated by air to 1 Military Hospital in Pretoria the following day. He unfortunately succumbed to his wounds in 1 Military Hospital on 01 June 1981.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. E. B. Harvey','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'G J','76244718BG','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',22,'"E" Coy.'),
