 (30739,30742,'Unknown','LEON','HOLSCHER','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'2 South African Infantry Battalion',654,'1973-11-26','Died in Freak Accident, in Kunene River, attacked by crocodile','Son of Mr. J. Holscher','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered. Panel 03',NULL,'L','70299235N','19','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (30740,30743,'Unknown','JOHN OWEN','HOLTZHAUSEN','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'2 Sqdn.',657,'1952-04-10','Killed in action, in North American F-51 Mustang #372. Major Mouton led a three aircraft flight, comprising himself, Lt J.O. Holtzhausen in the No.2 position and Capt van der Merwe in the No.3 position. Their target was a railroad at YE5004, which they attacked from 7500 feet. Visibility over the target was poor, with low cloud and haze. Prior to his attack, Major Mouton noticed that both his No.2 and No.3 were in position, and after the attack he headed for the form up point and called his flight to check in. Only No.3 did so. On calling Lt Holtzhausen again, Major Mouton received a response, to the effect that Lt Holtzhausen was joining an American flight for the return home. However, he failed to arrive with any of the American flights involved in the attack, and was not heard of again.','Husband of Mrs. Sybil Dulcie Holtzhausen (born Eckstein on 20 May 1923 and married 10 December 1949), of Cape Town. ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Korea',73,'UNITED NATIONS PUSAN MEMORIAL',2571,NULL,NULL,'Panel 13',NULL,'J O','P1/38342','28','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
