 (30745,30748,'Unknown','JOHANNES GEORGE','HORN','Rifleman',462,'South African Training Corps',864,'South African Army Gymnasium',3085,'1959-10-14','Drowned, in the swimming pool, on active service','Born Cape Province. Resided at Landman Street, Dispatch, Uitenhage District, but he lived in the Army Gymnasium, Pretoria. He was unmarried.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Reportedly buried in Dispatch, Cape Province',NULL,'J G','L/16494','19','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (30746,30749,'Unknown','MARIUS','HORN','Staff Sergeant',531,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'5 South African Infantry Battalion',1298,'1988-08-04','Died in Military Vehicle Accident, while returning in a convoy from Eshowe. His Samil truck stopped near Eshowe for a water break. Marius was sitting in passenger seat and while troops were climbing off the back, the vehicle started sliding down the embankment and hit the fence. A fence post went through the vehicle door and impaled him to his seat, killing him instantly','Husband of Mrs. A. Horn','South Africa',72,'LADYSMITH CEMETERY',1417,'-28.55551','29.79635 ','Block 26, Row A, Grave 101',NULL,'M','79571923PE','27','Kwazulu Natal',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (30747,30750,'Unknown','FRANCIS','HORWELL','Second Lieutenant',475,'Imperial Light Horse',391,'5 South African Infantry Battalion',1298,'1922-03-12','Killed in action, at Ellis Park, during Rand Revolt','Went to St. Andrew&#39;s College, Grahamstown from October 1897 to December 1899. In 1901 he joined Cape Peninsular Regiment and after the Boer War entered Civil Service in the Transvaal. Later became a Public Prosecutor at Boksburg. In 1914 he served in Rebellion of 1914 with Enslin&#39;s Horse and the campaign of SWA, where he was a trooper with the ILH, and East Africa (Staff Sgt. 1st Mtd. Bde.). He subsequently obtained a commission as a 2nd Lieut. in the KAR.','South Africa',72,'PIETERMARITZBURG (COMMERCIAL ROAD) CEMETERY',1958,'-29.60699','30.38471 ','Block 26, Row A, Grave 101',NULL,'F','79571923PE','38','Kwazulu Natal',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (30748,30751,'Unknown','HERMAN','HOSEA','Special WO',520,'South West African Police',876,'South West Africa Police Counter-Insurgency Wing: Ops-K Division (KOEVOET)',3100,'1984-02-24','Killed in action, Counter-insurgency duty in South West Africa. Member of Koevoet','ref. "The Covert War" by Peter Stiff','South Africa',72,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Likely buried in Namibia - Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'H','79571923PE','38','Unknown',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (30749,30752,'Unknown','ZANDISILE JACKSON','HOSHO','Sergeant',492,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1999-08-16','Died of injuries, received on 6 August, in a Military Vehicle Accident','Husband of Mrs. N. G. Hosho','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'Z J','94812377PE','26','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',179,'Army'),
 (30750,30753,'Unknown','LEONARD PATRICK','HOUGH','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'3 South African Infantry Battalion',987,'1982-04-15','Killed in action, in contact with the enemy. Whilst on patrol the Lt sent out a section (1 Ratel) to follow a couple a tracks that the tracker had picked up. The Ratel hit an ambush just after 10am. By the time backup had formed up and went to their aid a group of soldiers had been killed.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. L. F. Hough, of Pietermaritzburg.','South Africa',72,'PIETERMARITZBURG (MOUNTAIN RISE) CEMETERY',1960,'-29.57947','30.39986 ','Cremated at PMB on 23 Apr 1982. Ashes at Block G, 105 at the Mountain Rise Cemetery.',NULL,'L P','77375863BG','20','Kwazulu Natal',626,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
