 (30752,30755,'Unknown','GEORGE MICHAEL','HOWARD','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Artillery Corps',785,'4th Artillery Regiment',1254,'1987-10-16','Died in Military Vehicle Accident, at Mariental, Buffel rolled while trying to avoid colliding with a delivery truck, resulting in him being crushed underneath.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. W. G. Howard','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Cremated - Ashes scattered in Magaliesberg Hills',NULL,'G M','83429985BG','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
