 (30769,30772,'Unknown','CHRISTOPHER MAUNDER','HUMPHREY','Flight Lieutenant',253,'Royal Air Force',635,'RAF Wildenrath',2779,'1972-01-12','Died in air crash, the pilot took off to demonstrate the handling characteristics of the Harrier to a party of Swiss officials. Immediately after take-off he entered cloud and presumably having decided to execute a wing over, he emerged from the cloud in a very steep dive. Although he ejected, the seat was carried into the side of a building and the pilot did not survive.','Of Chingola, Northern Rhodesia','United Kingdom',90,'OXFORD (WOLVERCOTE) CEMETERY',1899,'51.79137','-1.27205 ','Sec. L, Grave 84',NULL,'C M','608462','28','Oxfordshire',1,'LG Sup 7 June 1951 pg. 3097 - "King&#39;s birthday"',118,'Air Force'),
