 (30826,30829,'Unknown','LOURENS JOHANNES','JANSE VAN RENSBURG','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'7 South African Infantry Battalion',1529,'1983-12-18','Killed in action, Ops Askari, ten members that were part of an Anti-Aircraft team deployed near Caiundu in Southern Angola were killed during a fierce fire-fight when their position was attacked by a numerically superior enemy force of more than 200 FAPLA troops. Sergeant Hendrik Albertus Oosthuyse volunteered to remain behind armed with a MAG machine-gun and due to his heroic actions, he delayed the enemy advance sufficiently to allow the remainder of the team to successfully evade capture','Son of Mr. and Mrs. L. J. Janse Van Rensburg','South Africa',72,'NOORDVAAL CEMETERY (near Vanderbiljpark)',1822,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'L J','79364600BG','20','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor83.asp?t=516019',10,'"B" Coy.'),
