 (30857,30860,'Unknown','JAN ABRAHAM','JERLING','Warrant Officer II',597,'South African Air Force',775,'41 Sqdn.',1176,'2002-12-05','Died in Freak Accident, fell out of a landed Caravan aircraft and broke his neck. He died shortly after the accident on the runway in Alldays, Limpopo. He was part of a 4-man crew of 41 Squadron (AFB Waterkloof) that was on a night flying training flight.','Husband of Ilse Jerling, a Lt.Col. at SAAF HQ, and father of three children: Christo (12), Desire (9) and Jacques (2). His funeral was at the NGK Lyttelton-Noord in Monument Ave, Centurion.','South Africa',72,'CENTURION CEMETERY',499,NULL,NULL,'Block E, Grave H118',NULL,'J A','76913979SP','36','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 4 January 1917 pg. 245',179,'Army'),
