 (30861,30864,'Unknown','EVARISTO','JOAO','Lance Corporal',311,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1987-02-01','Killed in action, during a first light attack on a SWAPO camp in the Cassumbi area east of Cassinga (Operation Kakebeen)','A 82mm mortar exploded between him and his machine gun buddy Rfn Tolosi. Husband of Mrs. M. Cashika','Namibia',56,'KIMBO CEMETERY, BUFFALO',1304,NULL,NULL,'NEW SEC 123',NULL,'E','76906403SP','32','Caprivi',10,'LG Sup 4 January 1917 pg. 245',10,'"B" Coy.'),
 (30862,30865,'Unknown','JOSHUA','JOAO','Rifleman',462,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1980-06-04','Killed in action, south of Mutuanjamba (approximately 80km inside Angola) during first phase of Operation Sceptic, specifically area clearing and domination as well as establishment of tactical HQ at Mulemba','Joao was badly wounded and Braz and Van Der Walt were killed when their patrol crossed a gravel road in the kill zone of a vehicle ambush. Large force of dug in SWAPO with mortars and machine guns were able to inflict casualties and pin the patrol down. Reinforcements dislodged the ambushing force, but were forced to secure the immediate area and attend to casualties rather than pursue the enemy. Joao withdrew and attempted to return to nearby TB, but became lost and died of wounds (according to intercepts and evidence supported by his badly damaged equipment). Despite extensive efforts to find him, he was not recovered','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered',NULL,'J','79830626SP','24','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 4 January 1917 pg. 245',10,'"B" Coy.'),
