 (30880,30883,'Unknown','RALPH MARTIN','JOHNSON','Second Lieutenant',475,'Household Cavalry Regiment',387,'South West Africa Police Counter-Insurgency Wing: Ops-K Division (KOEVOET)',3100,'2006-08-01','Killed in action, in Afghanistan. Captain Alex Eida, 2nd Lieutenant Ralph Johnson and Lance Corporal Ross Nicholl were killed after a vehicle patrol was ambushed by militants in a northern district of Helmand province in southern Afghanistan on 1 August, they were ambushed with RPGs, AK-47s and a heavy machine gun','Of George, South Africa','South Africa',72,'GEORGE (ST. MARK&#39;S) CATHEDRAL',930,NULL,NULL,'Cremation Plaque',NULL,'R M','76','24','Western Cape',1,'LG Sup 4 January 1917 pg. 245',179,'Army'),
