 (31157,31160,'Unknown','GEORGE HUTTON','KROHN','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'2 Sqdn.',657,'1951-11-24','Killed in action, in North American F-51 Mustang #345. Lt G.H. Krohn was a member of a flight tasked with rail interdiction. On take off, Lt Krohn aborted due to a fault with his radiator, and was delayed 10 minutes, the rest of his flight continuing without him. After his radiator had been repaired, he took off alone, in an attempt to catch up with his flight. He was seen by two USAF flights, and Lt Krohn reported that he was making his attack with a USAF flight. They reported seeing his bombs explode, and the last American pilot off the target reported seeing a lone &#39;Cheetah&#39; Mustang heading south. He failed to return, and was not heard of again.','ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Korea',73,'UNITED NATIONS PUSAN MEMORIAL',2571,NULL,NULL,'Panel 13',NULL,'G H','328524','30','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor82.asp?t=516194',103,'54th Bn.'),
