 (31241,31244,'Unknown','RICHARD LLEWELLEN','LAVIS','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Air Force',775,'85 Combat Flying School',1651,'2011-03-08','Collapsed and died after completing a training flight in a Hawk jet trainer.','Son of Mrs. Lavis, of Vryburg.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'R L','2509634','24','Gauteng',1,'Awarded while serving with the South African Air Force in the Korean War',179,'Army'),
 (31242,31245,'Unknown','DEREK ROLLO','LAW','Flying Officer',259,'Royal Air Force',635,'RAF Wattisham',2778,'1966-01-05','Died in air crash, when the Lightning crashed on approach into Bentwaters. Suffered a double engine/reheat fire, had tried to eject but the canopy failed to release and attempted a forced landing into Bentwaters. Unfortunately he was unable to make the runway and the almost copybook landing into a ploughed field was enough to cause the canopy to detach and the ejection sequence to commence. Regrettably the seat required both height and forward speed to enable to parachute to deploy.','No additional information known at this time','United Kingdom',90,'RINGSHALL (ST. CATHERINE) CHURCHYARD',2162,'52.13627','0.98239 ','Row 2 Grave 10',NULL,'D R','5200008','24','Suffolk',118,'Awarded while serving with the South African Air Force in the Korean War',118,'Air Force'),
