 (31244,31247,'Unknown','ANTHONY DENNIS MICHAEL','LAWRENSON','Major',343,'South African Air Force',775,'Wklt Flt',3216,'1962-03-12','Died in Aircraft Accident, crashed near Belfast, in Dornier Do-27A #5431','Husband of Mrs. M. J. Lawrenson. A veteran of WW2 and Korea','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (OLD No.1) MILITARY CEMETERY',2491,'-25.80165','28.12721 ','Row 2 Grave 10',NULL,'A D M','P21813','43','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 1 January 1946 - "New Year&#39;s Honours" pg. 155',118,'Air Force'),
 (31245,31248,'Unknown','GEOFFREY ALLAN','LAWRIE','Lance Corporal',311,'1 Reconnaissance Regiment',9,'Wklt Flt',3216,'1977-01-01','Killed in action, contact with enemy forces North of Beacon 28, near Omunduangilo','Son of Mr. G. A. Lawrie, of Port Elizabeth','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Cremated - Ashes at St Mary',NULL,'G A','69360642PE','23','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 1 January 1946 - "New Year&#39;s Honours" pg. 155',118,'Air Force'),
 (31246,31249,'Unknown','GEORGE EDGAR BRUCE','LAWSON','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'Wklt Flt',3216,'1923-11-19','Died of injuries, head injuries, received in aircraft accident, Avro 504K #H9701, at Roberts Heights Military Hospital','Son of Mr. Lawson, of Johannesburg. WW1 Fighter ace, credited with 6 victories. ref. 85 years of SAAF.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (OLD No.1) MILITARY CEMETERY',2491,'-25.80165','28.12721 ','Grave 623, CoE Section',NULL,'G E B','69360642PE','24','Gauteng',1,'LG 8 February 1919 - "A pilot of courage and skill, bold in attack and gallant in action, who has accounted for five enemy aeroplanes. On 27th September he attacked fifteen Fokker biplanes that were harassing one of our bombing formations, driving down one in flames. He then engaged a second; in the combat the two machines collided, and the enemy aeroplane fell down completely out of control. Although his machine was badly damaged, Lieutenant Lawson successfully regained our lines."',118,'Air Force'),
 (31247,31250,'Unknown','DIEDRE','LUITINGH','Lieutenant',334,'South African Army',780,'Quartermaster General',3259,'1980-11-01','Committed suicide, suspected, from a bullet wound to the head, near Krugersdorp.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. D. J. Luitingh, of Krugersdorp.','South Africa',72,'KRUGERSDORP (STERKFONTEIN) CEMETERY',1379,'-26.06757','27.76241 ','Grave 623, CoE Section',NULL,'D','79697900','18','Gauteng',525,'LG 8 February 1919 - "A pilot of courage and skill, bold in attack and gallant in action, who has accounted for five enemy aeroplanes. On 27th September he attacked fifteen Fokker biplanes that were harassing one of our bombing formations, driving down one in flames. He then engaged a second; in the combat the two machines collided, and the enemy aeroplane fell down completely out of control. Although his machine was badly damaged, Lieutenant Lawson successfully regained our lines."',525,'H.Q.'),
