 (31271,31274,'Unknown','TERRENCE RODNEY','LE ROUX','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'5 South African Infantry Battalion',1298,'1981-05-27','Killed in action, while on patrol from Etale base close to the Charlie pipeline. The 7-man patrol was following spoor when they were ambushed by a force of approximately 70 SWAPO/PLAN insurgents who opened fire on them with PKM and RPD machine-guns as well as 60mm mortars and RPG-7 Rocket launchers. Le Roux suffered two bullet wounds to the chest and one to the head that killed him instantly.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. R. F. Le Roux','South Africa',72,'PHALABORWA TOWN CEMETERY',1947,NULL,NULL,'746',NULL,'T R','75536508BG','22','Limpopo Province',1,'LG 8 February 1919 - "A pilot of courage and skill, bold in attack and gallant in action, who has accounted for five enemy aeroplanes. On 27th September he attacked fifteen Fokker biplanes that were harassing one of our bombing formations, driving down one in flames. He then engaged a second; in the combat the two machines collided, and the enemy aeroplane fell down completely out of control. Although his machine was badly damaged, Lieutenant Lawson successfully regained our lines."',179,'Army'),
