 (31279,31282,'Unknown','MARIUS JOHANN','LECUONA','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'2 Special Service Battalion',655,'1988-02-03','Died in Freak Accident, as crew commander of a Ratel 90, the command came to visgraad (take cover under trees) when enemy Migs were overhead. A branch from the tree caught the browning mounting which came loose and hit Marius in the head, killing him. Ops Hooper','Son of Mr. L. J. O. Lecouna','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'M J','84592641BG','19','Gauteng',1,'LG 8 February 1919 - "A pilot of courage and skill, bold in attack and gallant in action, who has accounted for five enemy aeroplanes. On 27th September he attacked fifteen Fokker biplanes that were harassing one of our bombing formations, driving down one in flames. He then engaged a second; in the combat the two machines collided, and the enemy aeroplane fell down completely out of control. Although his machine was badly damaged, Lieutenant Lawson successfully regained our lines."',179,'Army'),
