 (31758,31761,'Unknown','CECIL CHARLES','MCALISTER','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'14 South African Infantry Battalion',348,'1981-08-14','Killed in action, during a contact with PLAN insurgents, near Opuwa in the Kaokoveld. During an attack by PLAN on a Temp Base, he was killed by a Strim Rifle grenade while exiting his sleeping bag','Husband of Mrs. S. R. McAlister','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Panel 08',NULL,'C C','70459490BT','27','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 17 September 1917 pg. 9577 - serving with East Surrey Regiment - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty under heavy shell fire. He was instrumental in saving the lives of several NCOs and men of his company who had been buried in a tunnel by an enemy bombardment. He was severely wounded whilst engaged on this duty."',179,'Army'),
 (31759,31762,'Unknown','ALFRED DESMOND','MCCALLUM','Captain',115,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1987-09-13','Due to tactical circumstances, his troop got stuck in the mud of a shona near the Lomba River during a tank fight, and his Ratel 90 was destroyed at point blank by a T55 tank. 2Lt Alves, his crew as well as 32 Bn members such as Capt Mac McCallum was killed instantly. The tank round penetrated the Ratel through the side door, detonated in the main ammunition storage container and resulted in an explosion causing the vehicle to catch fire. (Operation Modular)','Son of James Frank William McCallum, of Vereeniging, Transvaal','South Africa',72,'VEREENIGING (JACOBSKOP) CEMETERY',2605,NULL,NULL,'No headstone',NULL,'A D','74316175PK','27','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 17 September 1917 pg. 9577 - serving with East Surrey Regiment - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty under heavy shell fire. He was instrumental in saving the lives of several NCOs and men of his company who had been buried in a tunnel by an enemy bombardment. He was severely wounded whilst engaged on this duty."',179,'Army'),
 (31760,31763,'Unknown','MICHAEL SEAN','MCCANN','Second Lieutenant',475,'South West African Territory Force',877,'101 Battalion, Romeo Mike Team',157,'1988-02-04','Killed in action, near Mupa in Southern Angola when their Casspir drove into an ambush and was struck by a Czechoslovakian RPG-75 Anti-Tank Rocket. The rocket struck the Browning Machine-gun mounting and exploded, spraying the inside of the vehicle with lethal shrapnel, killing them instantly','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'HOUT BAY (WEST) CEMETERY',1177,NULL,NULL,'No headstone',NULL,'M S','82463563BG','21','Western Cape',1,'LG Sup 17 September 1917 pg. 9577 - serving with East Surrey Regiment - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty under heavy shell fire. He was instrumental in saving the lives of several NCOs and men of his company who had been buried in a tunnel by an enemy bombardment. He was severely wounded whilst engaged on this duty."',179,'Army'),
