 (31762,31765,'Unknown','LUKE EDWARD PATRICK','MCCULLOCH','Lance Corporal',311,'Royal Irish Regiment',672,'Unknown',50,'2006-09-06','Killed in action, in Sangin, Helmand Province, he and other soldiers were sleeping out in the open because of not enough bunkers, and he came off sentry duty and was sitting where he slept and was eating when he was hit by shrapnel from a mortar.','Son of Gary Brandt and Elaine McCulloch-Brandt, and brother of Sebastian McCulloch-Brandt. From Cape Town, South Africa. Left South African when he was 14 years old and finished his schooling at the Grammar School in Corsham he also attended the Catholic school in Slough for a year before moving to Corsham','United Kingdom',90,'ARMED FORCES MEMORIAL AT THE NATIONAL ARBORETUM',89,NULL,NULL,'Cremated - Alternative Commemoration',NULL,'L E P','25136150','21','Staffordshire',1,'LG Sup 17 September 1917 pg. 9577 - serving with East Surrey Regiment - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty under heavy shell fire. He was instrumental in saving the lives of several NCOs and men of his company who had been buried in a tunnel by an enemy bombardment. He was severely wounded whilst engaged on this duty."',179,'Army'),
 (31763,31766,'Unknown','LESLIE JAMES','MCDONALD','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'40 Sqdn.',1162,'1958-08-23','Killed in aircraft accident, engine failure crashed near Germiston, in AT-6 Harvard #7193. Pilot bailed out but parachute failed to open.','Son of Mrs. McDonald, of Hospital Hill, Johannesburg. ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (BRAAMFONTEIN) CEMETERY',1219,'-26.19379','28.02763 ','Cremated at Braamfontein. Ashes were inserted in niche in columbarium',NULL,'L J','P1/41826','27','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 17 September 1917 pg. 9577 - serving with East Surrey Regiment - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty under heavy shell fire. He was instrumental in saving the lives of several NCOs and men of his company who had been buried in a tunnel by an enemy bombardment. He was severely wounded whilst engaged on this duty."',179,'Army'),
