 (32000,32003,'Unknown','KEVIN JAMES','MORROW','Rifleman',462,'REGIMENT',585,'Rand Light Infantry',2792,'1984-05-31','Died in Military Vehicle Accident, Rfn Morrow and a few other soldiers were tasked to act as a protection element for a Technical Service Corps crew sent out to recover a broken down Buffel vehicle. After the Buffel vehicle was located and hitched to the recovery vehicle, he took up a position on the back of the recovery vehicle. On the return journey to Ondangwa, the driver lost control of the vehicle, causing it to overturn Rfn Morrow still sitting on the back. He was killed instantly.','Husband of Mrs. H. Morrow. Father of Candice Clare Johnson, now of Perth, Western Australia. Morrow was from Malvern, Kwazulu Natal.','South Africa',72,'QUEENSBURGH CEMETERY',2083,NULL,NULL,'Cremated at Poole Crematorium, Dorset, Ashes taken to Zimbabwe',NULL,'K J','71391601BT','28','Kwazulu Natal',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=514791',179,'Army'),
 (32001,32004,'Unknown','HENRY GEORGE','MORTON','Air Corporal',43,'South African Air Force',775,'17 Sqdn.',441,'1966-04-21','Died in Aircraft Accident, at Terrace Bay, South West Africa, in Alouette III #65. They were allocated call sign "SAP 4" and tasked to assist the SAP Sgt Olivier whose vehicle was giving trouble while on patrol near the Cunene River. Together with Lt T Winterbach, SAP member Cst DJA Brand and two officials from the Consolidated Diamond Mines, PJ Holmes and D Bernhardt, they took off to look for Sgt Olivier. As the banked over the sea to turn northwards, the helicopter hit the sea and broke apart. There were no survivors and his body was not recovered','Son of Warrant Officer Morton. Commemoration plaque at Swakopmund Police Station','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - Panel 02',NULL,'H G','24031','22','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=514791',179,'Army'),
