 (32200,32203,'Unknown','DUDLEY','NEL','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'4 South African Infantry Battalion',1150,'1982-01-19','Killed in action. Nel was stationed at Etale, 18 km from the Angolan border. Assigned to an escort detail that was to protect a Water Works JCB that had the task of repairing the water pipeline between Charlie Tower at Engela hospital and Eenhana. On the way there the JCB got stuck in the mud on several occasions. Nel and his buddy (Reyneke), got off the armoured vehicle and stayed close to the JCB with the intention of assisting it through the mud whenever it got close to getting stuck. From this point on, the going was really good, until the JCB detonated a land mine with one of it&#39;s back wheels. They were both was killed instantly.','Son of Mrs. G. F. Nel, of Alberton.','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (BRAAMFONTEIN) CEMETERY',1219,'-26.19379','28.02763 ','Crem. Niche',NULL,'D','79395984BG','18','Gauteng',383,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98653',383,'attd. 53rd Bn. "A" Coy.'),
 (32201,32204,'Unknown','DUDLEY','NEL','LAM',307,'South African Air Force',775,'28 Sqdn.',871,'1961-02-10','Killed in aircraft accident, crashed near Bizana, in Douglas C-47 Dakota #6856','ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (OLD No.1) MILITARY CEMETERY',2491,'-25.80165','28.12721 ','Crem. Niche',NULL,'D H','79395984BG','19','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98653',383,'attd. 53rd Bn. "A" Coy.'),
 (32202,32205,'Unknown','DAVID JOHN','NEL','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Corps of Engineers',793,'1 Construction Regiment',70,'1982-08-19','Killed in action, landmine. Assigned to an escort detail that was to protect a Water Works JCB that had the task of repairing the water pipeline between Charlie Tower at Engela hospital and Eenhana. On the way there the JCB got stuck in the mud on several occasions. Nel and his buddy (Reyneke), got off the armoured vehicle and stayed close to the JCB with the intention of assisting it through the mud whenever it got close to getting stuck. From this point on, the going was really good, until the JCB detonated a land mine with one of its back wheels. Nel was killed instantly.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. J. D. Nel','South Africa',72,'GERMISTON (PRIMROSE) CEMETERY',936,'-26.19511','28.14623 ','Crem. Niche',NULL,'D J','80217755BG','18','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98653',383,'attd. 53rd Bn. "A" Coy.'),
