 (32393,32396,'Unknown','HENDRIK ALBERTUS','OOSTHUYSE','Sergeant',492,'South African Artillery',784,'10 Anti Aircraft Regiment',136,'1983-12-18','Killed in action, Ops Askari, ten members that were part of an Anti-Aircraft team deployed near Caiundu in Southern Angola were killed during a fierce fire-fight when their position was attacked by a numerically superior enemy force of more than 200 FAPLA troops. Sergeant Hendrik Albertus Oosthuyse volunteered to remain behind armed with a MAG machine-gun and due to his heroic actions, he delayed the enemy advance sufficiently to allow the remainder of the team to successfully evade capture','Husband of Mrs. M. C. Oosthuyse','South Africa',72,'BELLVILLE (STIKLAND) CEMETERY',214,NULL,NULL,'Military Stone',NULL,'H A','74217076PE','25','Western Cape',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor82.asp?t=517425',179,'Army'),
