 (32459,32462,'Unknown','DESMOND JOHN','PEKEUR','Petty Officer',403,'South African Navy',832,'SAS WING',3053,'1986-04-10','Died in Military Vehicle Accident,near Schmidtsdrift. He was part of a group who were engaged in locust extermination when the back tyre of his Landrover burst and the vehicle rolled.','Husband of Mrs. DM Pekeur of Kraaifontein','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'D J','74740671PC','31','Gauteng',541,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',541,'Navy'),
 (32460,32463,'Unknown','ABRAHAM LIEBERGH','PELSER','Corporal',166,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'7 South African Infantry Battalion',1529,'1977-03-08','Died in Freak Accident, some of the troops used to straighten the pins on their hand grenades to make them easier to extract and then hooked the grenades into their webbing via the grenade handle. Unfortunately, when Abraham took off his webbing after returning to Nkurukuru Base from a patrol, his thumb caught on the grenade pin and pulled it out. The armed M26 grenade fell onto the floor in the middle of the tent and without hesitation, he dived onto the grenade and absorbed the full force of the explosion that killed him instantly but saved the lives of all the other soldiers in the tent','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'A L','72430408BC','21','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',541,'Navy'),
 (32461,32464,'Unknown','GERHARDT','PENZHORN','Pupil Pilot',436,'South African Air Force',775,'7 South African Infantry Battalion',1529,'1938-03-18','Killed in an aircraft crash in Tiger Moth #ZS-AIP. The engine stalled while the plane was in an inverted position during low level aerobatics. The plane crashed one mile SE of the Randfontein Airfield while attempting to recover.','ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'KROONDAL LUTHERAN CHURCH CEMETERY, RUSTENBURG DISTRICT',2810,'-25 43.335','27 18.364 ','Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'G','P1/8138','24','North West Province',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',541,'Navy'),
