 (32470,32473,'Unknown','MARIUS','PETERSON','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'1 South African Infantry Battalion',114,'1982-04-15','Killed in action. Whilst on patrol the Lt sent out a section (1 Ratel) to follow a couple a tracks that the tracker had picked up. The Ratel hit an ambush just after 10am. By the time backup had formed up and went to their aid a group of soldiers had been killed.','Son of Mr. W. K. H. Peterson, of Bellville, Cape Town.','South Africa',72,'BELLVILLE (STIKLAND) CEMETERY',214,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'M','78491404BG','19','Western Cape',626,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
