 (32521,32524,'Unknown','WILLEM JOHANNES','PIETERSEN','Rifleman',462,'South African Commandos',791,'Boksburg Commando',1967,'1977-05-05','Died in Freak Accident, drowned. Part of a 4-man squad on O.P. duties on the Kavango River, on a piece of land that formed a peninsula. During the night the river rose, cutting that piece of land off from the river-edge. The river flowed very strongly and, in the squads&#39; attempts to get back, Pietersen drowned.','Son of Mr. W. J. Pietersen, of Boksburg.','South Africa',72,'BOKSBURG CEMETERY',295,'-26.21977','28.27423 ','Block C, Grave 2209',NULL,'W J','72512734KT','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',179,'Army'),
