 (32529,32532,'Unknown','MARK ANTHONY','PLATEEL','Lance Corporal',311,'MEDICAL T',471,'Grp 36 HQ',2194,'1981-08-28','Killed in action, out on a patrol with his unit in Angola, a mortar hit them. A group of 4 or 5 soldiers were in a circle and the mortar hit right in the middle, killing Mark instantly.','Son of Mr. A. L. Plateel. Attended York High School, George','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'M A','78419827BG','19','Gauteng',179,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',179,'Army'),
