 (32536,32539,'Unknown','AASVOEL','KUMALO','Chief Inspector',131,'Unknown Unit',951,'31 (Bushman) Battalion',1000,'1991-02-05','Died of heart attack, at Baragwanath Hospital. He became ill on 3 February while on duty and was hospitalised. He was attached to Witwatersrand Command HQ at the time.','Husband of Mrs. Sizakele Angel Kumalo, c/o Georgedale School, Georgedale Mission.','South Africa',72,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Reportedly buried in the Hammarsdale Cemetery, Natal.',NULL,'A','06416457HB','67','Unknown',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',179,'Army'),
