 (32544,32547,'Unknown','ERASMUS CHRISTOFFEL','POTGIETER','Corporal',166,'South African Air Force',775,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1975-10-21','Died in Shooting Incident, killed while playing "Russian Roulette" at a private house in Walvis Bay.','Son of Mr. P. A. C. Potgieter, of Virginia.','South Africa',72,'VIRGINIA CEMETERY',2635,'-28.11082','26.8493 ','Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'E C','72205859','19','Free State',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32545,32548,'Unknown','IZAK CORNELIUS','POTGIETER','Field Cornet',238,'South African Air Force',775,'42 Sqdn.',1186,'1964-12-07','Died in Aircraft Accident, near Coligny, in Cessna 185A #728. He was busy with a tactical exercise as part of "Exercise Musslebreak" and patrolling the Ventersdorp-Coligney Rd in a westerly direction. One mile past Bodenstein, he gained height and then crashed','Son of Mr. S. J. Du Toit Potgieter','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','Grave 460',NULL,'I C','PX/47750','23','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32546,32549,'Unknown','JOHAN DIEDERIK','POTGIETER','Brigadier',103,'FREE STATE COMMAND',334,'Officer Commanding 2 Mil Area, SWA',2695,'1976-01-04','Died in Aircraft Accident, shot down by own AAA, in Aerospatiale SA3330 Puma C #122. The OC 2 Mil Area, scheduled a visit to Battlegroup Chicken, near Mussende, Angola. Unfortunately the Puma was painted green, similar to the colour of the enemy planes and flew off course over an AA battery that had not been informed of the flight. Thinking the enemy were attacking, the AA shot the chopper down','Husband of Mrs. S. J. Potgieter, of Saldanha. ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'BETHAL CEMETERY',239,'-26.46273','29.47474 ','Grave 460',NULL,'J D','01169895PE','40','Mpumalanga',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32547,32550,'Unknown','JOHAN HENDRIK','POTGIETER','Rifleman',462,'South West African Territory Force',877,'Etosha Area Force Unit',2127,'1982-04-15','Killed in action, on patrol the Lt sent out a section (1 Ratel) to follow a couple a tracks that the tracker had picked up. The Ratel hit an ambush just after 10am. By the time backup had formed up and went to their aid a group of soldiers had been killed.','Husband of Mrs. R. Potgieter','Namibia',56,'TSUMEB CEMETERY',2539,'-19.24686','17.71971 ','Grave 460',NULL,'J H','67302257BG','30','Mpumalanga',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32548,32551,'Unknown','JOHANNES JACOBUS','POTGIETER','Private',429,'86 Technical Stores Depot',143,'Etosha Area Force Unit',2127,'1973-01-07','Died of sports injuries, during training, at Nyamandhlovu, Rhodesia. His death certificate was issued in Rhodesia.','Son of Mr. J. C. Potgieter, of Johannesburg. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr JRT Wood) ***May have been attached to 2nd Rhodesia Regiment','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (WEST PARK) CEMETERY',1224,'-26.15926','27.9943 ','DRM 13335',NULL,'J J','68897571N and/or PR89424','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32549,32552,'Unknown','JOHAN LOUIS','POTGIETER','Corporal',166,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'1 South African Infantry Battalion',114,'1981-11-04','Ops Daisy. Died in an act of heroism about two kilo&#39;s south of "Bravo Battalion&#39;s HQ" in the Chitequeta district, South-eastern Angola. By doing so he specifically saved the wounded Rfn. Boorsma&#39;s life (diving onto him) and by doing so, he indicated to his Lieutenant where SWAPO was firing from and therefore saving more lives. A small group of FAPLA/SWAPO snipers had pinned a Ratel platoon for at least 10-15 minutes and killed two more Unita soldiers (traveling with them) and wounded another three. Was recommended for the Honoris Crux for his bravery, but army headquarters refused the recommendation.','Son of Mrs. S. P. Potgieter, of Boksburg.','South Africa',72,'BOKSBURG CEMETERY',295,'-26.21977','28.27423 ','Sector 14',NULL,'J L','74503004BG','23','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32550,32553,'Unknown','KEVIN EVERITT','POTGIETER','Staff Sergeant',531,'1 Parachute Battalion',7,'1 South African Infantry Battalion',114,'1973-05-16','Died in Freak Accident, parachute accident at Tempe. Kevin had been given a steerable reserve chute by his father that he decided to test. To do this, he had to first discard his main chute before using the reserve chute. After discarding his main parachute, he deployed the reserve chute but it became entangled in the buckles of his main chute and wrapped itself around him, causing him to plunge to his death','Son of Frederik Evert and Esme Potgeiter. Husband of Mrs. June Lilian Potgieter','South Africa',72,'BLOEMFONTEIN AREA CEMETERY ?',283,NULL,NULL,'Cremated - Memorial plaque',NULL,'K E','05535174E','26','Free State',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',118,'Air Force'),
 (32551,32554,'Unknown','MICHIEL CASPARUS EKSTEEN','POTGIETER','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'2nd Armoured Car Regt.',897,'1975-08-13','Died in Shooting Incident, at Ruacana Airport. He was accidentally shot with a 7.62 MG while his convoy was parked and they were busy clearing and checking weapons.','Son of Johannes Marthinus and Wilhelmina Gertruida Potgieter, of Vrede','South Africa',72,'VREDE CEMETERY',2649,'-27.42927','29.16884 ','Cremated - Memorial plaque',NULL,'M C E','72354327N','18','Free State',21,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',21,'"D" Sqdn.'),
