 (32553,32556,'Unknown','RICHARD LAURENCE STANLEY','POWELL-JONES','Second Lieutenant',475,'South African Air Force',775,'Regiment De la Rey',2806,'1938-04-18','Died in Aircraft Accident, crash in Tiger Moth #ZS-AIP. The engine stalled while the plane was in an inverted position during low level aerobatics. The plane crashed one mile SE of the Randfontein Airfield while attempting to recover.','Son of Capt. Stanley W. and Viola Powell-Jones, of Rustenburg. Instructor Pilot for Witwatersrand Technical School of Aeronautics. ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG AREA CEMETERY ?',1226,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'R L S','P1/7285','23','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 3 March 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He has at all times set a splendid example of courage and determination"',21,'"D" Sqdn.'),
