 (32705,32708,'Unknown','JOHN ALLEN','ROBINSON','Captain',115,'South African Air Force',775,'19 Sqdn.',497,'1982-01-05','Killed in action, in Aerospatiale SA3330 Puma C #168. Puma crashed 15km North East of Namacunde, when an AK47 round damaged the tail rotor. The resulting fire damage caused the pilot to lose control and the aircraft crashed inverted.','Son of Francis Henry Robinson, also died in service. Brother of G. H. Robinson, of Johannesburg. ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Cremated - Ashes scattered at Cape Town',NULL,'J A','70535448PK','27','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98188',179,'Army'),
 (32706,32709,'Unknown','STANLEY JOHN DALY','ROBINSON','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force',635,'19 Sqdn.',497,'1939-01-30','Died in Aircraft Accident, Blenheim Mk.I L1476 of 64 Fighter Squadron RAF crashed on Sykes Moor, Derbyshire during a training flight from RAF Church Fenton','Son of Dr. Francis Harry Robinson (Old Shirburnian), Ophthalmic Surgeon, of P.O. Uitenhage, South Africa. Attended Park Town Preparatory School, Johannesburg, South Africa. Attended Sherborne School (Abbey House) September 1931-July 1936; School Prefect; 1st XI 1935, 1936 (captain); 1st XV 1933, 1934, 1935 (captain); 1st XI Hockey 1935; Gym Squad 1933-1934 (captain 1935-36); 1st Class Gym; Camp PT Squad 1935; PT Instructor with Badge; Trebles (1933-36); Captain of Swimming (1936); Captain of Boxing (1936); Sergeant in OTC. Acting Pilot Officer, Royal Air Force.','United Kingdom',90,'KIRKBY WHARFE (ST. JOHN THE BAPTIST) CHURCHYARD EXTENSION',1319,'53.86021','-1.23212 ','Pre War Grave in CWGC care',NULL,'S J D','70535448PK','21','Yorkshire',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=98188',179,'Army'),
