 (32728,32731,'Unknown','MICHAEL HOPE','RORKE','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'2 Sqdn.',657,'1951-05-15','Killed in action, in North American F-51 Mustang #330. Lt M.H. Rorke was one of three pilots preparing to take off from K-16 on their third mission of the day, their target being a well camouflaged supply dump near Singye. During his take of run, Lt Rorke&#39;s aircraft became airborne three quarters down the runway, but failed to climb higher than approximately 10 feet, and swung slowly towards a stranded B29 bomber at the end of the runway. As the Mustang&#39;s left wing began to drop, Lt Rorke jettisoned his napalm tanks, possibly in a last attempt to avoid disaster, but crashed into the B29 and the exploding napalm engulfed both aircraft.','ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Korea',73,'UNITED NATIONS PUSAN CEMETERY',2570,NULL,NULL,'Grave 1210',NULL,'M H','P1/33453','27','Western Cape',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=514240',179,'Army'),
