 (32828,32831,'Unknown','LESLEY ANDREW','SCHOLTZ','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'3 South African Infantry Battalion',987,'1980-04-08','While guarding a Water Works camp, 2 km North of Ombalantu, the detachment came under fire and he was severely wounded in the head during the exchange. He died later at 1 Mil Hospital.','Son of Mr. T. E. Scholtz, of Knysna.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'L A','76251438BG','20','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=91573',179,'Army'),
