 (32832,32835,'Unknown','GUSTAV CARL','SCHONBORN','Rifleman',462,'South African Commandos',791,'University OFS Commando',3175,'1983-12-21','Died in Military Vehicle Accident, military vehicle accidentally drove over him in very dusty conditions with poor visibility during anti-insurgent follow-up operations in Southern Angola','Son of Mr. and Mrs. G. C. Schonborn, of Upington.','South Africa',72,'UPINGTON (KEIDEBEES) CEMETERY',2574,NULL,NULL,'E1',NULL,'G C','77414357BT','22','Northern Cape',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=91573',179,'Army'),
 (32833,32836,'Unknown','ADAM JOHANNES HENDRIKUS','SCHONFELDT','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'SADF Horse & Dog Centre',3032,'1975-11-14','Killed in action, by enemy machine gun fire when their patrol walked into a PLAN ambush during a night-time follow-up operation tracking fresh insurgent spoor in the Eastern Caprivi','He was a member of the Tactical Platoon of the SADF Horse and Dog Centre, based at M&#39;pacha in the Caprivi during his death. His Tracker dog was Rinty no. W991. Both he and his dog were killed in a night time follow-up operation tracking fresh SWAPO tracks in the Eastern Caprivi and ending up in an ambush. His Platoon commander at the Dog School was Capt. GH Grobler, and his Instructor was Cpl J Rocher.','South Africa',72,'ZEERUST MUNICIPAL CEMETERY',2796,'-25.53738','26.07708 ','Grave 1128',NULL,'A J H','71205629BA','20','North West Province',402,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=91573',402,'attd. 6th South African Infantry'),
 (32834,32837,'Unknown','RINTY','SCHONFELDT','Dog',203,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'SADF Horse & Dog Centre',3032,'1975-11-14','Killed in action, by enemy machine gun fire when their patrol walked into a PLAN ambush during a night-time follow-up operation tracking fresh insurgent spoor in the Eastern Caprivi','He was a member of the Tactical Platoon of the SADF Horse and Dog Centre, based at M&#39;pacha in the Caprivi during his death. His Tracker dog full particulars are: Name - Rinty no.W991. Both handler and dog were killed in a night time follow-up operation tracking fresh SWAPO tracks in the Eastern Caprivi and ending up in an ambush. His Platoon commander at the Dog School was Capt. GH Grobler, and his Instructor was Cpl J Rocher.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'R','W991','20','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=91573',402,'attd. 6th South African Infantry'),
 (32835,32838,'Unknown','DERICK JOHN','SCHRONEN','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'4 South African Infantry Battalion',1150,'1983-12-31','Killed in Action during Ops Askari in Southern Angola while attached to 61 Mechanised Battalion Group when a Soviet 82mm High Explosive Mortar Bomb landed and exploded on the Roll-bar of their Buffel Troop Carrier, spraying the inside of the vehicle with lethal shrapnel, killing them instantly','Son of Mr. and Mrs. A. J. Schronen, of Bothasig, Cape Town.','South Africa',72,'CAPE TOWN (MAITLAND) CREMATORIUM',454,NULL,NULL,'Cremated. Ashes buried at Maitland Garden of Remembrance',NULL,'D J','81173254BG','18','Western Cape',626,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=91573',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
 (32836,32839,'Unknown','BRUCE EDWARD','SCHULTZ','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1980-02-05','Killed in action, in a contact with the enemy. Their Temporary Base near the Angolan Border (Sector 10) was attacked by SWAPO during the night.','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'KING WILLIAM&#39;S TOWN CEMETERY',1308,'-32.87536','27.39264 ','Cremated. Ashes buried at Maitland Garden of Remembrance',NULL,'B E','76457779BG','20','Eastern Cape',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=91573',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
