 (32838,32841,'Unknown','BAREND JACOBUS PHILLIPUS','SCHUTTE','Air Mechanic',46,'South African Air Force',775,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1965-06-10','Died in Shooting Incident, accidentally shot through the head with a .38 revolver by a comrade. They were part of the guard detail at Langebaanweg AFB on the 8 June 1965 and were in the off duty room where another member was playing with a firearm which went off and injured Schutte. He died 2 days later in hospital','Next of kin, P. Koch','South Africa',72,'PIET RETIEF STRYDKRAAL 477 IT FARM CEMETERY',2931,'-26.53683','30.56884 ','Block 7 Grave 126',NULL,'B J P','62187968','20','Mpumalanga',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
 (32839,32842,'Unknown','DEON','SCHUTTE','Lance Corporal',311,'GROUP 33',362,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1991-02-14','Died in Shooting Accident, shot while attempting to resolve a dispute as one soldier had taken another hostage.','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'SPRINGS CEMETERY',2337,'-26.24526','28.42538 ','Block 7 Grave 126',NULL,'D','86437498BG','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
 (32840,32843,'Unknown','JAN JURGENS ROETS','SCHUTTE','Trooper',581,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'1 Special Service Battalion',116,'1978-08-23','Killed in action, during the early hours of the morning when the bungalow in which they were sleeping at Katima Mulilo received a direct hit from a Soviet GRAD-P 122mm High Explosive Katyusha Rocket. SWAPO/PLAN insurgents operating from Zambia fired 20 x 122mm GRAD-P Katyusha Rockets into the town. 18 rockets exploded harmlessly in the veld, one struck a school in the Katima Mulilo Township and the other demolished the Bungalow in which the soldiers were sleeping','Son of Stefanus Johannes Bester Schutte and Johanna Susanna Maria Venter. He was unmarried. ("South Africa&#39;s Border War, 1966 - 1989" deur Willem Steenkamp bl. 80).','South Africa',72,'SPRINGS CEMETERY',2337,'-26.24526','28.42538 ','Block 7 Grave 126',NULL,'J J R','74429036BG','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
 (32841,32844,'Unknown','PIETER MARTHINUS','SCHUTTE','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'4 South African Infantry Battalion',1150,'1987-11-11','Killed in action, during an attack on the FAPLA 16 Bde, south of Chimbinga River, he was the driver of a Ratel 20 that engaged an enemy tank. While busy with this action, the Ratel was hit head on by a round from another tank, and knocked out. The gunner tried to help Schutte out of the vehicle but discovered that he had been killed instantly. Although seriously wounded, the gunner managed to exit the Ratel but died later of his wounds. Both he and the gunner were recommended for posthumous awards of the Honorus Crux.','Son of Mr. and Mrs. T. J. Schutte, of Lichtenburg.','South Africa',72,'LICHTENBURG (EAST) CEMETERY',1470,'-26.13988','26.15266 ','A11',NULL,'P M','83504696BG','20','North West Province',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
 (32842,32845,'Unknown','JEAN MARC','SCHUURMAN','Rifleman',462,'1 Parachute Battalion',7,'4 South African Infantry Battalion',1150,'1987-11-01','Died of wounds, received during Ops Firewood. The attack commenced at dawn and the SA forces only withdrew after dark on the same day. It was estimated that more than 300 Swapo fighters were killed during the battle. At the end of the day Cpl N S Olivier, L/Cpl R M Light, Rfn H N de Rose, Rfn D W van Rooyen and Rfn W F Ewels were killed in action. Several other members of D Coy was also wounded during the battle and Rfn J M Schuurman died on 1 November 1987 of his wounds. Capt P A Pienaar the 2IC of D Coy who was in charge of the two platoons was killed in West Africa almost 10 years later, on 29 October 1997.','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (WEST PARK) CEMETERY',1224,'-26.15926','27.9943 ','GEN B Grave 8853',NULL,'J M','83271031BG','20','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',626,'attd. 61 Mechanised Battalion Group'),
