 (32848,32851,'Unknown','THEODORE CHRISTIAN','SCOTT','Lieutenant',334,'South African Air Force',775,'2 Sqdn.',657,'1952-07-09','Killed in action, in North American F-51 Mustang #391. Lt T.C. Scott was the leader of a flight that were tasked to attack targets east of Kaesong. On arrival in the target area, Lt Scott experienced difficulties with his radio, and handed over the lead to his No.3, Lt Singleton. The mosquito controller warned them of the flak and handed them their target, after which they made their attacks individually, at a safe distance from each other. Lt Austin, flying in the No.4 position behind Lt Scott saw the latter&#39;s aircraft burst into flames and shed a few large pieces. The Mustang failed to recover from its dive, crashing into the ground.','ref. 85 years of SAAF','South Korea',73,'UNITED NATIONS PUSAN MEMORIAL',2571,NULL,NULL,'Panel 13',NULL,'T C','P1/28700','32','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',179,'Army'),
 (32849,32852,'Unknown','SYDNEY SHIELDS','SCULLY','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'South African Air Force',775,'35 Sqdn.',1043,'1963-08-08','Died in Aircraft Accident, in Stettynsberg mountains, in Avro Shackleton MR Mk 3 #1718','Husband of Mrs. D. E. Scully, of Wynberg, Cape Province. Attended Glenwood high school in Durban from 1932 - 1935.','South Africa',72,'CAPE TOWN (PLUMSTEAD) CEMETERY',463,'-34.02633','18.4764 ','Grave UJ. 147. - No headstone',NULL,'S S','P4895','45','Western Cape',1,'LG Sup 13 December 1945',179,'Army'),
