 (33009,33012,'Unknown','FREDERIK JOHANNES','SMITH','Private',429,'South African Medical Services',820,'85 Combat Flying School',1651,'1978-10-28','Died in Freak Accident, at Ogongo base, trying to rescue civilian workers who succumbed to methane gas in an underground tunnel.','Son of Mr. G. C. Smith, of Johannesburg.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'F J','75218362BG','19','Gauteng',1,'"At Ogongo Agricultural College in Ovamboland, a labourer went down into a sewage pit to clean it. His supervisor, Mr. Brown heard him fall into the water and climbed down to help him. Three Medical Service National Servicemen were in the area and tried to save them. None of them returned as all were overcome by fumes. The three, Ptes FJ Smith, JC Jooste and B van D van Papendorp were awarded Honoris Crux medals"',118,'Air Force'),
 (33010,33013,'Unknown','GEORGE DOUGLES','SMITH','Private',429,'South African Medical Corps',817,'85 Combat Flying School',1651,'1928-08-21','Died of tuberculosis and cirrhosis of the liver, at Roberts Heights Hospital.','Relation of Mr. J. M. Smith, of Johannesburg.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (OLD No.1) MILITARY CEMETERY',2491,'-25.80165','28.12721 ','Grave 879, Presbyterian  Section',NULL,'G D','1705','19','Gauteng',1,'"At Ogongo Agricultural College in Ovamboland, a labourer went down into a sewage pit to clean it. His supervisor, Mr. Brown heard him fall into the water and climbed down to help him. Three Medical Service National Servicemen were in the area and tried to save them. None of them returned as all were overcome by fumes. The three, Ptes FJ Smith, JC Jooste and B van D van Papendorp were awarded Honoris Crux medals"',118,'Air Force'),
