 (33026,33029,'Unknown','NICOLAAS WILLEM','SMUTS','Rifleman',462,'1 Parachute Battalion',7,'35 Sqdn.',1043,'1985-11-05','Killed in action, during ambush of SWAPO who had kidnapped Owambo children, about 15 km NNE of Etale','Son of Dr. and Mrs. J. Smuts, of George Road, Eldoraigne, Verwoerdburg. He had a sister and 2 brothers. Matriculated at the Voortrekkerhoogte High School.','South Africa',72,'CENTURION CEMETERY',499,NULL,NULL,'HA1',NULL,'N W','81267130BG','20','Gauteng',380,'"At Ogongo Agricultural College in Ovamboland, a labourer went down into a sewage pit to clean it. His supervisor, Mr. Brown heard him fall into the water and climbed down to help him. Three Medical Service National Servicemen were in the area and tried to save them. None of them returned as all were overcome by fumes. The three, Ptes FJ Smith, JC Jooste and B van D van Papendorp were awarded Honoris Crux medals"',380,'attd. 53 Battalion'),
 (33027,33030,'Unknown','WILLEM STEPHANUS','SMUTS','Trooper',581,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'1 Special Service Battalion',116,'1978-08-23','Killed in action, during the early hours of the morning when the bungalow in which they were sleeping at Katima Mulilo received a direct hit from a Soviet GRAD-P 122mm High Explosive Katyusha Rocket. SWAPO/PLAN insurgents operating from Zambia fired 20 x 122mm GRAD-P Katyusha Rockets into the town. 18 rockets exploded harmlessly in the veld, one struck a school in the Katima Mulilo Township and the other demolished the Bungalow in which the soldiers were sleeping','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (WEST PARK) CEMETERY',1224,'-26.15926','27.9943 ','Grave 560',NULL,'W S','75477661BG','19','Gauteng',1,'"At Ogongo Agricultural College in Ovamboland, a labourer went down into a sewage pit to clean it. His supervisor, Mr. Brown heard him fall into the water and climbed down to help him. Three Medical Service National Servicemen were in the area and tried to save them. None of them returned as all were overcome by fumes. The three, Ptes FJ Smith, JC Jooste and B van D van Papendorp were awarded Honoris Crux medals"',380,'attd. 53 Battalion'),
