 (33153,33157,'Unknown','NICOLAS ANDREW','STUBBS','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'Equestrian Centre',2121,'1987-02-19','Died in Military Vehicle Accident, at the Reitz Show Grounds. While attending a show to conduct a motorcycle display, he fell asleep next to the transport vehicle carrying the motorcycles. Later in the evening, when the vehicle was moved to a safer location he did not wake up when the vehicle was started, and was driven over.','Son of Mr. T. F. Stubbs, of Saxonwold, Johannesburg.','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'N A','83494971BG','40','Gauteng',1,'DFC LG 15 February 1946 pg. 962 - "In recognition of gallantry and devotion to duty in the execution of air operations"; MID LG Sup 1 January 1946 pg. 129',179,'Army'),
