 (33215,33219,'Unknown','IVAN LESLIE','TAYLOR','Private',429,'SA Army',704,'1 Signals Regiment',113,'1998-03-14','Shot at Stutterheim by a civilian person, while off duty.','Ref SANDF 1998 RoH','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'M','94856215','19','Gauteng',179,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=93750',179,'Army'),
 (33216,33220,'Unknown','RUPERT WILLIAM','TAYLOR','Lieutenant',334,'Military Intelligence',480,'1 Signals Regiment',113,'1922-03-10','Killed in action, during Rand Revolt, shot by Herbert Hull and David Lewis','Son of William Twentyman Taylor. In Samuel Alfred (Taffy) LONG&#39;s biographical entry in the New Dictionary of South African Biography, Vol. 1, it states that he was hanged on 17 November 1922, at the Central Prison in Pretoria, together with Herbert HULL and David LEWIS. Hull and Lewis were sentenced for the murder of Lt. Rupert William TAYLOR.','South Africa',72,'PRETORIA (REBECCA STREET) CEMETERY',2052,'-25.73953','28.1537 ','Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'R W','94856215','27','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 17 April 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He displayed great courage on several occasions in getting his men and mules through heavy shell fire. He set a splendid example to his men throughout under the most difficult circumstances."',179,'Army'),
 (33217,33221,'Unknown','RUPERT WILLIAM','TCHINGUAR','Lance Corporal',311,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1985-05-29','Died of Natural Causes','ref "Die Buffel Struikel" by LJ Bothma','Namibia',56,'KIMBO CEMETERY, BUFFALO',1304,NULL,NULL,'NEW SEC 74',NULL,'A C','79830352SP','27','Caprivi',179,'LG Sup 17 April 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He displayed great courage on several occasions in getting his men and mules through heavy shell fire. He set a splendid example to his men throughout under the most difficult circumstances."',179,'Army'),
 (33218,33222,'Unknown','RUPERT WILLIAM','TCHINONGO','Rifleman',462,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1977-08-02','Died in training, Hand Grenade Accident','ref "Die Buffel Struikel" by LJ Bothma','Namibia',56,'KIMBO CEMETERY, BUFFALO',1304,NULL,NULL,'OLD SEC 2',NULL,'A','76927912SP','27','Caprivi',179,'LG Sup 17 April 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He displayed great courage on several occasions in getting his men and mules through heavy shell fire. He set a splendid example to his men throughout under the most difficult circumstances."',179,'Army'),
 (33219,33223,'Unknown','WAITE','TCHIPANGO','Lance Corporal',311,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1987-09-13','Due to tactical circumstances, the troop got stuck in the mud of a shona near the Lomba River during a tank fight, and the Ratel 90 was destroyed at point blank by a T55 tank. The commander, 2Lt Alves, his crew as well as 32 Bn members were killed instantly. The tank round penetrated the Ratel through the side door, detonated in the main ammunition storage container and resulted in an explosion causing the vehicle to catch fire. (Operation Modular)','ref "Die Buffel Struikel" by LJ Bothma','Namibia',56,'KIMBO CEMETERY, BUFFALO',1304,NULL,NULL,'NEW SEC 161',NULL,'W','76928621SP','27','Caprivi',1,'LG Sup 17 April 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He displayed great courage on several occasions in getting his men and mules through heavy shell fire. He set a splendid example to his men throughout under the most difficult circumstances."',179,'Army'),
 (33220,33224,'Unknown','WAITE','TCHIZONDA','Rifleman',462,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1979-04-23','Killed in action, part of a group, from the Recce wing of 32Bn. They were tasked to do a Recce patrol close to Chana &#39;Enhombe&#39; (about 15 to 20 kms north of the cutline) to determine the extent of SWAPO activity in the area and if possible locate SWAPO Bases in order that 32Bn Companies could launch base attacks. They commenced their Recce on the late afternoon of 22 April 1979. Just after sunrise the following day, 23 April, the group was engaged by a much superior SWAPO force. In the ensuing firefight Tchizonda was wounded by small arms fire but was still able to be mobile. Unfortunately however, on one of the groups withdrawal maneuvers he was hit in the chest, at point blank range, by an RPG7. Due to the intense enemy fire his fellow Recce Members were not able to recover his body','No additional information known at this time','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered',NULL,'A M','78916272SP','27','Gauteng',1,'LG Sup 17 April 1917 - "For conspicuous gallantry and devotion to duty. He displayed great courage on several occasions in getting his men and mules through heavy shell fire. He set a splendid example to his men throughout under the most difficult circumstances."',179,'Army'),
