 (33373,33377,'Unknown','PETER','UZZELL','Rifleman',462,'GROUP 34',363,'Virginia Commando',3189,'1983-01-08','Died of wounds, burn wounds, at 1 Mil Hospital. Wounded in a landmine explosion on 6 January when their Buffel detonated a boosted anti-tank mine near the Okangwati Military Base, while on route to Sodeliet base. One of the mines used was an old British Mk 8 Anti-Tank Mine and the metal plug on top of this mine penetrated the V hull of the Buffel on the welded seam. This ignited the diesel tank and a box of white phosphorus grenades in the vehicle.','Son of Mr. J. J. Uzzell, of Glen Harmony, Virginia.','South Africa',72,'WELKOM CEMETERY',2694,NULL,NULL,'A29',NULL,'P','72241417KT','26','Free State',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',179,'Army'),
