 (33455,33459,'Unknown','JOHANNES ERASMUS','VAN DER MERWE','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'3 South African Infantry Battalion',987,'1980-12-03','Killed in action, escorting school children to Oshakati. On the return trip to Ondangwa, they were ambushed. Their Buffel was hit by an RPG round that passed through the vehicle without detonating, but mortally wounding Johannes (Rassie) van der Merwe and Christo van Zyl','Son of Mr. I. S. F. van der Merwe, of Kimberley.','South Africa',72,'STANFORD NEW CEMETERY',2382,NULL,NULL,'Row C,  Grave 1',NULL,'J E','76547991BG','19','Western Cape',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',179,'Army'),
 (33456,33460,'Unknown','JAMES JOHANNES','VAN DER MERWE','Conductor',158,'South African Service Corps',854,'Transport and Remounts',3156,'1923-04-15','Died of tuberculosis and nephritis, at Roberts Heights Hospital.','Husband of Mrs. van der Merwe, of Johannesburg','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (OLD No.1) MILITARY CEMETERY',2491,'-25.80165','28.12721 ','Grave 978',NULL,'J J','5504','19','Gauteng',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',179,'Army'),
 (33457,33461,'Unknown','JOHANNES LODEWIKUS','VAN DER MERWE','Rifleman',462,'GROUP 34',363,'Goudveld Kommando',2179,'1983-01-06','Killed in action. Buffel Troop Carrier detonated a boosted anti-tank mine near the Okangwati Military Base, while on route to Sodeliet base. One of the mines used was an old British Mk 8 Anti-Tank Mine and the metal plug on top of this mine penetrated the V hull of the Buffel on the welded seam. This ignited the diesel tank and a box of white phosphorus grenades in the vehicle.','Husband of Mrs. C. M. van der Merwe, of Odendaalsrus.','South Africa',72,'WELKOM CEMETERY',2694,NULL,NULL,'A30',NULL,'J L','71291868KT','27','Free State',6,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',6,'"A" Coy.'),
 (33458,33462,'Unknown','JACO PETRUS','VAN DER MERWE','Gunner',278,'South African Artillery',784,'10 Artillery Brigade',138,'1988-08-19','Missing, presumably drowned, after he went swimming in a river and disappeared. It is thought that he was taken by a crocodile, Ops 1 area. He has no known grave and remains unaccounted for','Son of Mr. and Mrs. J. D. Boshoff','South Africa',72,'VOLKSRUST CEMETERY',2644,'-27.36447','29.89216 ','Memorial stone - Body not recovered',NULL,'J P','84435338BG','19','Mpumalanga',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',6,'"A" Coy.'),
