 (33489,33493,'Unknown','JOHAN CHRISTIAAN','VAN DER WESTHUIZEN','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1980-10-15','He was involved in a private vehicle accident at Wolmeransstad on 10 Oct, while on a weekend pass. He suffered head injuries but died at 1 Mil Hospital 5 days later.','Son of Mr. J. C. van der Westhuizen, of Klerksdorp.','South Africa',72,'KLERKSDORP (NEW) CEMETERY',1337,NULL,NULL,'I AB 80',NULL,'J C','77390573','18','North West Province',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',622,'United Nations/African Union Mission in Darfur'),
 (33490,33494,'Unknown','JOHANNES DANIEL','VAN DER WESTHUIZEN','Rifleman',462,'1 Parachute Battalion',7,'6 South African Infantry Battalion',1421,'1981-03-28','Died of injuries, at Bloemfontein barracks. There were twin Brothers in the barracks and the one brother, who had picked up a "dud" 60mm High Explosive mortar bomb on the range, dropped the mortar bomb in the middle of a crowded bungalow after supper and the bomb exploded, mortally wounding the three. The other twin Brother lost his leg in the same incident and many other troops were wounded. The bungalow walls were also riddled with shrapnel. The twin brothers were not seen in the Unit lines again.','Son of Mr. F. A. S. van der Westhuizen, of Bloemfontein.','South Africa',72,'BLOEMFONTEIN (SOUTHPARK) CEMETERY',282,NULL,NULL,'I AB 80',NULL,'J D','77518702BG','19','Free State',1,'http://www.izkor.gov.il/izkor86.asp?t=95291',622,'United Nations/African Union Mission in Darfur'),
