 (33558,33562,'Unknown','BURGERT van DYK','VAN PAPENDORP','Private',429,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'3 South African Infantry Battalion',987,'1978-10-28','Died in Freak Accident, at Ogongo base, trying to rescue civilian workers who succumbed to methane gas in an underground tunnel.','Son of Mr. L. C. van Papendorp','South Africa',72,'BREDASDORP NEW CEMETERY',341,'-34.52419','20.04526 ','B1',NULL,'B v D','75381095BG','18','Western Cape',379,'"At Ogongo Agricultural College in Ovamboland, a labourer went down into a sewage pit to clean it. His supervisor, Mr. Brown heard him fall into the water and climbed down to help him. Three Medical Service National Servicemen were in the area and tried to save them. None of them returned as all were overcome by fumes. The three, Ptes FJ Smith, JC Jooste and B van D van Papendorp were awarded Honoris Crux medals"',379,'attd. 52nd Battalion'),
