 (33625,33629,'Unknown','JACOBUS CORNELIUS','VAN WYK','Lieutenant',334,'5th Reconnaissance Regiment',127,'8 South African Infantry Battalion',1628,'1979-05-23','Killed in action, at Shona Mutamanjamba in Southern Angola while carrying out reconnaissance mission to locate a suspected SWAPO/PLAN Base in the area. The three-man Team was tracked and ambushed by a numerically superior force of SWAPO/PLAN insurgents and in the ensuing fire-fight, two Team members were killed and the third member, although wounded, successfully evaded capture until the helicopter arrived to extract the Team. Upon hearing the approaching helicopter, the SWAPO/PLAN force broke contact and withdrew from the area','Awarded Honoris Crux for action 18 October 1975, with 1 Reconnaissance Regiment','South Africa',72,'KRUGERSDORP (STERKFONTEIN) CEMETERY',1379,'-26.06757','27.76241 ','Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'J C','67260869PE','27','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
 (33626,33630,'Unknown','JACOBUS JOHANNES CHRISTOFFEL','VAN WYK','Civilian',137,'Civilian',267,'8 South African Infantry Battalion',1628,'1922-03-16','Shot in the back for attempting to escape police custody, during Rand Revolt','Born Orange Free State','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (BRIXTON) CEMETERY',1220,'-26.19806','28.01538 ','D.R. Church Sec. Grave 1726. No headstone.',NULL,'J J C','67260869PE','49','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
 (33627,33631,'Unknown','LEON','VAN WYK','Captain',115,'1 Parachute Battalion',7,'8 South African Infantry Battalion',1628,'1982-05-02','Killed in action, east of Otavi during a contact with SWAPO/PLAN insurgents. A single SWAPO/PLAN insurgent was holding up in a shack on a farm. The shack was surrounded by a section of Paratroopers in the dark and after a heavy volume of fire had been brought to bear on the shack, Leon tried to enter it. However, the insurgent was still alive and fired at Leon with his AK-47 as he burst open the door. Leon was hit by several shots and severely wounded. He died shortly afterwards from his wounds. The insurgent escaped in the confusion','Next of kin, Mrs. E. van Wyk','South Africa',72,'BLOEMFONTEIN (HAMILTON) WAR CEMETERY',279,'-29.14836','26.20817 ','A2',NULL,'L','72481708PE','26','Free State',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
 (33628,33632,'Unknown','LEON FRANCOIS','VAN WYK','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'Regiment Molopo',2810,'1988-02-25','Killed in action, during a contact with enemy forces in Southern Angola, when his Olifant Tank was knocked out by a Soviet 130mm field gun','Husband of Mrs. C. van Wyk, of Nigel.','South Africa',72,'ROODEPOORT NEW CEMETERY',2192,NULL,NULL,'34820',NULL,'L F','73340051BT','30','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
 (33629,33633,'Unknown','MARIO','VAN WYK','Corporal',166,'South West African Territory Force',877,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1980-06-04','Killed in action, north of Mulemba (approximately 80km inside Angola) during first phase of Operation Sceptic, specifically area clearing and domination as well as establishment of tactical HQ.','Van Wyk was part of the same deployment as Joao, Braz and Van Der Walt who had been killed the previous day at Mutuanjamba. A group of SWAPO had clashed briefly with SADF units at Mulemba, and were withdrawing northwards. A rough impromptu stopper group was set-up and they were rewarded when SWAPO walked into them and a number were killed. Random SWAPO mortar fire killed Van Wyk moments later.','South Africa',72,'BOKSBURG CEMETERY',295,'-26.21977','28.27423 ','34820',NULL,'M','76305879BG','20','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
 (33630,33634,'Unknown','NICHOLAAS JOHANNES','VAN WYK','Able Bodied Seaman',24,'South African Navy',832,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1979-03-19','Died in a Motorcycle Accident, at Pretoria.','Son of Mrs. J. S. van Wyk, of Pretoria.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','34820',NULL,'N J','72235625','23','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
