 (33640,33644,'Unknown','CHRISTO','VAN ZYL','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'3 South African Infantry Battalion',987,'1980-12-03','Killed in action, escorting school children to Oshakati. On the return trip to Ondangwa, they were ambushed. Their Buffel was hit by an RPG round that passed through the vehicle without detonating, but mortally wounding Johannes (Rassie) van der Merwe and Christo van Zyl','Son of Mr. E. F. van Zyl, of Malvern, Johannesburg.','South Africa',72,'GERMISTON (PRIMROSE) CEMETERY',936,'-26.19511','28.14623 ','Buried with Rudolph Pollock; Petronella S.; Ernst F.; Hendrik Frederick and Willem van Zyl.',NULL,'C','77323103BG','19','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
