 (33755,33759,'Unknown','NICHOLAS JACOBUS','VISSER','Major',343,'5th Reconnaissance Regiment',127,'1 Recce Commando',103,'1975-10-29','Killed in aircraft accident, in Beechcraft Baron. The plane, known as "Dinky Toy" was supplied by UNITA and had been checked out by SAAF personnel at Rundu. It was busy with aerial observations for Battlegroup Foxbat in the Silva Porta area of Angola when it crashed, 6km north of Norton de Matos. The SADF investigation team could not determine the exact cause of the crash.','Husband of Mrs. J. M. Visser, of Oudtshoorn.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','Grave 855',NULL,'N J','01211440PE','37','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',179,'Army'),
 (33756,33760,'Unknown','WILLEM ROBERT','VISSER','Acting Pilot Officer',31,'Royal Air Force',635,'1 Recce Commando',103,'1956-05-18','Killed in aircraft accident, in Beechcraft Baron. The plane, known as "Dinky Toy" was supplied by UNITA and had been checked out by SAAF personnel at Rundu. It was busy with aerial observations for Battlegroup Foxbat in the Silva Porta area of Angola when it crashed, 6km north of Norton de Matos. The SADF investigation team could not determine the exact cause of the crash.','Of Ermelo, South Africa','Canada',14,'WINNIPEG (BROOKSIDE) CEMETERY',2748,'49.91653','-97.22103 ','Grave 4191',NULL,'W R','4170408','37','Manitoba',118,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',118,'Air Force'),
