 (33761,33765,'Unknown','GERT JACOBUS','VOGES','Staff Sergeant',531,'29 FIELD',70,'32 (Buffalo) Battalion',1013,'1977-03-29','Died from injuries sustained in a military vehicle accident which occurred on 29 Mar at the Otavi-Tsumeb crossroads, near Grootfontein. He was a passenger in the vehicle on the way to the airport.','Husband of Mrs. Dina S. C. Voges, of Maraisburg.','South Africa',72,'THABA TSHWANE (NEW) MILITARY CEMETERY',2490,'-25.78214','28.12179 ','Grave 930',NULL,'G J','54167291PE','39','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',118,'Air Force'),
 (33762,33766,'Unknown','STEVEN','VOLKERSZ','1st Lieutenant',11,'South African Air Force',775,'2 Sqdn.',657,'1980-10-10','Killed in action, shot down by SA-7 some 20 km SW of Mupa, in Atlas MB326KM Impala Mk II #1042. Volkerz ejected safely and waved to his wingman (Lt. Skinner) from the ground; however intercepted radio messages indicated that he was killed by SWAPO','Son of Mr. G. Volkersz, of Germiston','South Africa',72,'SADF WALL OF REMEMBRANCE, VOORTREKKER MONUMENT, PRETORIA',2234,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered',NULL,'S','74324500PM','23','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',118,'Air Force'),
 (33763,33767,'Unknown','GERHARD','VOLLGRAAFF','Lance Corporal',311,'South African Armoured Corps',779,'2 Special Service Battalion',655,'1975-11-23','Died of wounds, received in action during the Battle of Ebo. His armoured car was hit in the turret and he jumped out of the vehicle. A sniper shot him in the stomach and although he was taken to the hospital at Cela and was successfully operated on, he died later from complications.','Son of Mr. H. J. Vollgraaff, of Kanoneiland.','South Africa',72,'KANONEILAND (BLAAUWSKOP) CEMETERY',1242,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered',NULL,'G','72449325BC','19','Northern Cape',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',118,'Air Force'),
 (33764,33768,'Unknown','LEON','VOLSCHENK','Rifleman',462,'South African Infantry Corps',808,'4 South African Infantry Battalion',1150,'1988-07-08','Died of wounds, in 1 Military Hospital, from the effects of a gunshot wound in his abdomen received in a shooting accident at Oshivello on 30 June 1988. He was accidentally shot by an LMG during a fire and movement training exercise','Son of Mr. S. C. Volschenk, of Johannesburg.','South Africa',72,'JOHANNESBURG (WEST PARK) CEMETERY',1224,'-26.15926','27.9943 ','12858 GenM',NULL,'L','84501352','20','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',118,'Air Force'),
