 (33767,33771,'Unknown','UDO KNUD','VON SCHMETTAU','Sapper',469,'South African Corps of Engineers',793,'2 Field Engineer Regiment',624,'1975-12-10','Killed in action, during Op Savannah. His vehicle, in which he was transporting a wounded soldier, was hit by a mortar, killing him instantly. This was near Cela, in the Huambo Province, Angola.','Son of Mr. E. F. E. von Schmettau, of Walvis Bay, South West Africa','Namibia',56,'WALVIS BAY CEMETERY',2672,'-22.93101','14.522 ','Body not recovered',NULL,'U K','72304769BA','19','Gauteng',1,'He distinguished himself as part of Bravo Group during Op Savannah',118,'Air Force'),
