 (36136,36141,'Unknown','WILHEMNE','MILES','Inspector',291,'South African Police',840,'Mpumalanga',2616,'2001-07-05','Died on active service','Reg. # may be 468665-9. Dumisana Bomvana, 45, of Orlando West and Oscar Gift Mokgathedi were accused of a July 2001 robbery in which R190 000 was stolen from security guards at a pension paypoint at the Albertus Pop Centre in Extension Seven, Eldorado Park. Four policemen who were called to the scene chased the attackers. The robbers opened fire, killing Inspector Wilhemne Miles. Inspector Johnny Abdul died later in hospital.','South Africa',72,'SOUTH AFRICAN POLICE MEMORIAL, PRETORIA (UNION BUILDINGS)',2317,NULL,NULL,'Alternative Commemoration until grave found',NULL,'W','618110-4','27','Gauteng',548,'LG Sup 22 August 1918 as 133 Battery Sergeant Major 12th Citizen Battery',548,'Police'),
