 (38913,38919,'Unknown','PATRICK MICHAEL','BATE','Air Lieutenant',44,'Rhodesian Air Force',614,'7 Sqdn.',1530,'1979-09-26','Died in Aircraft Accident, in Alouette III # R5705 which struck power lines near Lake Alexander during Operation Thrasher. They were flying as decoys during an assault on Chimoio base in Mocambique.','ref. "Pride of Eagles" - History of the Rhodesian Air Force 1920 - 1980 by B. Salt','Zimbabwe',95,'CREMATED',592,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'P M','4291','47','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
 (38914,38920,'Unknown','DOUGLAS IAN BIGNALL','BATES','Sapper',469,'Rhodesian Corps of Engineers',621,'3 Squadron',989,'1976-06-15','Killed in action, in a vehicle ambush while clearing roads in the Honde Valley during Op Thresher, gun shot wound to head','Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CREMATORIUM',1063,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'D I B','PR73533','24','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
 (38915,38921,'Unknown','FRANK P','BATTAGLIA','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1978-03-06','Killed in action, at Kavalamanja, Zambia during Operatio Turmoil, by a ZIPRA machine gun nest.','He was an American citizen from Florida and New York City. He was a Vietnam veteran having served with the U.S. 173rd Airborne. One week after being casevaced wounded his platoon suffered a severe ambush. One week after tour of duty his other platoon suffered a severe ambush. Frank served a full contract with the Spanish Foreign Legion. He received a great honor there to carry the statue of the Blessed Virgin Mary in a huge religious feast day parade. Frank came to Rhodesia with his wife, and went to SAS training troop. His wife joined the Rhodesian Air Force and worked packing parachutes. Later Frank would always check the parachute packing number and had jumped with a chute packed by his wife a few times. Frank after SAS training joined 1 RLI 3 Cdo 14 Troop. He was an avid poker player and gave some young Rhodesian soldiers poker lessons while playing for matches. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood)','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'F P','728515','24','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',656,'3 Commando'),
 (38916,38922,'Unknown','PETER JOHN','BATTERSHILL','Junior Commandant',295,'Guard Force',372,'Internal Affairs',2474,'1979-03-27','Killed in action in a vehicle ambush between Mount Darwin and the BSAP Base at Dotito, during Op Hurricane. His vehicle was hit by a M90 bazooka which hit the windshield and killed him instantly.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'P J','728515','24','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',656,'3 Commando'),
