 (38918,38924,'Unknown','ARTHUR CHARLES','BEAMISH','Captain',115,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'5th Battalion',1377,'1978-11-02','Murdered by terrorists, on his farm in the Horseshoe Block while in between service in the 5RR.','His brother R W Beamish also died in service. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'A C','V2658','30','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',656,'3 Commando'),
 (38919,38925,'Unknown','RAYMOND W','BEAMISH','Sergeant',492,'Rhodesia Forces',605,'1st Field Regiment',543,'1979-07-20','Killed in action, by a gunshot wound received in the Grapple area while fighting against Pfumo re Vanhu.','His brother A C Beamish also died in service. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'R W','728094','30','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',656,'3 Commando'),
