 (38921,38927,'Unknown','GIDEON EDWARD','BECKING','Rifleman',462,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'4th Battalion',1256,'1979-04-25','Killed in action, vehicle hit a boosted mine in the Ops Thresher area. He was the owner of the Sabie Star holiday resort near Umtali and had previously been captured by ZANLA and later released in Mozambique, as he was South African citizen','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','South Africa',72,'CAROLINA CEMETERY',478,'-26.06797','30.10577 ','Cremated',NULL,'G E','76852','35','Mpumalanga',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',656,'3 Commando'),
 (38922,38928,'Unknown','GERALD WILLIAM ANDREW','BELL','Second Lieutenant',475,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'4th Battalion',1256,'1977-03-22','Killed in action, vehicle ambush in the Zambezi Valley, Op Hurricane. Gerry was returning from a call-up to Mana Pools via Rukomechi to take up his job with National Parks when they were ambushed by a group of ZIPRA terrorists. A single bullet entered the door-less land Rover striking him in the chest and resulting in his death. A natural leader and highly skilled in bush craft, this ranger with National Parks served his call ups with the RAR.','Son of Jess and Bill Bell. Brother to Lindsay. A Guinea Fowl School old boy. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'MASVINGO CEMETERY',1619,'-20.07684','30.84057 ','Cremated',NULL,'G W A','76852','23','Mpumalanga',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',656,'3 Commando'),
