 (38934,38940,'Unknown','HARRY ANTHONY','BERMAN','Private',429,'Rhodesian Defence Regiment',624,'1st Battalion',524,'1978-02-24','Killed in action, died from wounds received in an ambush.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'H A','104929','20','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',532,'INTAF'),
 (38935,38941,'Unknown','ANDREW ARTHUR','BERRINGTON','Sergeant',492,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'9th Battalion',1718,'1978-02-01','Killed in action, vehicle ambush as they were leaving Vila Salazar, Op Repulse, at the end of their call-up. The ambush was initiated with an RPG rocket that struck the cab, killing the driver, Rfn Colin Murray and Sgt Andrew Berrington, who took the brunt of the blast. Jose Alpium was shot in the chest as he was debussing, dying an hour later','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'A A','45362','20','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
