 (38937,38943,'Unknown','EMMANUEL','BETOMAN (BATEMAN)','Private',429,'Central Intelligence Organisation',997,'1 Psychological Operations Unit',2748,'1980-03-28','Died of renal failure','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'E','660988','41','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (38938,38944,'Unknown','MARTIN D&#39;ARCY','BETTS','Rifleman',462,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1977-12-13','Killed in action, during a Fire Force action at Nyamatombe Hill, in the Maramba Tribal Trust Land, during Operation Hurricane. They were trying to clear a cave of terrorists.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'M D','100055','41','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',646,'2 Commando'),
 (38939,38945,'Unknown','DANIEL','BEZUIDENHOUT','Private',429,'Rhodesia Defence Regiment',604,'1st Battalion',524,'1976-12-24','Died on active service','ref. Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'BULAWAYO (ATHLONE) CEMETERY',384,'-20.12167','28.59161 ','Cremated',NULL,'D','129386','18','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',646,'2 Commando'),
 (38940,38946,'Unknown','ERIAZERE','BHERE','Private',429,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'2nd Battalion',898,'1978-09-08','Died of wounds, gunshot wounds received in a contact, at Sengwe Tribal Trust Land, Op Repulse','ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'E','646343','18','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (38941,38947,'Unknown','ALBANY CHARLES','BICKLE','Second Lieutenant',475,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'1st Battalion',524,'1977-12-08','Died in Vehicle Accident, on the Bulawayo - Vic Falls road. He had popped in to see his father on their farm in Nyamandlovu and was hurrying back to rejoin the convoy','On Plumtree School Roll of Honour. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'A C','V3678','18','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (38942,38948,'Unknown','KEVIN HOWARD','BICKNELL','Sergeant',492,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'1 Independent Company',88,'1978-04-10','Died of wounds, gunshot wounds sustained in a shooting incident at the Essexvale Battle Camp, Op Tangent. Upon returning from R&R on that Monday, twenty members of this Company had drawn rifles and live ammunition for retraining purposes. They assembled at the end of a football field, where they stripped their weapons for cleaning prior to moving to the rifle range for firing practice. Once the group had stripped their FNs, a Pte Robert Nyamini Mapfumo suddenly cocked his rifle and opened fire on automatic at his fellow soldiers. As Mapfumo&#39;s 20 round magazine emptied, and before he could replace it with a fully charged one, Privates Mawonda and Zevezene overpowered and disarmed Mapfumo. Tragically though, four lay dead and four were seriously wounded. Cpl Stephen Randall of Bulawayo, L/Cpl Michael Wall of Que Que, Sgt Kevin Bicknell of Hartley and Pte John Tshuma of Bembesi had lost their lives. Sgt Vic Anderson, Cpl Malcolm Partridge, L/Cpl Rob Garitzio and Pte David Chiremba had been wounded. In spite of claiming insanity, Mapfumo was found guilty of murder in the High Court in Bulawayo and sentenced to death.','Intake 155 DRR. A Prince Edward School old boy. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'K H','113536','18','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',642,'3 Platoon'),
 (38943,38949,'Unknown','RICHARD LOUIS','BIEDERMAN','Sergeant',492,'Special Air Service',895,'"C" Sqdn.',22,'1977-12-05','Died in Shooting Incident, in an accidental shooting in Mocambique. SAS operators were on covert operations aimed at disrupting ZANLA and FRELIMO logistical lines when the accident, involving another SAS patrol, occurred. He was an American national.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'R L','726658','26','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',642,'3 Platoon'),
 (38944,38950,'Unknown','DAVID ANTHONY MICHAEL','BILLING','Corporal',166,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'8th Battalion',1664,'1976-02-14','Killed in action, gunshot wound, received on the Mukumbura Road, Mount Darwin, Op Hurricane.','Son of Des and Grace Billing. Father of Ronald and Gordon Billing. On St. George&#39;s College War Memorial, Harare, Zimbabwe. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'D A M','PR32274','34','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',642,'3 Platoon'),
