 (38974,38980,'Unknown','ANTHONY JOHN','BRADING','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1970-01-22','Killed in action, contact with ZAPU insurgents, Ntondongwe fly gate area, just north of the boundary of the Doma Safari area, Sipolilo district, in Op Birch. With a JOC established at Mangula, elements of 1 Commando followed spoor for three days, eventually making contact on the 21st. Early the following morning, contact was again made, and in an ensuing firefight, Tony was shot and killed. All three terrorist insurgents were killed','Born 1949 in Southern Rhodesia. Educated at Jameson High School. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated, ashes placed in brother&#39;s grave',NULL,'A J','4099','21','Harare (Salisbury)',635,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',635,'1 Commando'),
 (38975,38981,'Unknown','ANTHONY','BRADLEY','Corporal',166,'HQ',388,'Mashonaland',2580,'1977-01-06','Died in a Military Aircraft Accident, in Dakota #R7034 near the Lundi River. Hit an overhead wire after taking off from Buffalo Range on a para drop resupply mission.','Ref  &#39;Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr JRT Wood). Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated, ashes placed in brother&#39;s grave',NULL,'A','64232','21','Harare (Salisbury)',635,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
