 (38997,39003,'Unknown','JEREMY','BULL','Rank Unknown',443,'Rhodesian Air Force',614,'7 Sqdn.',1530,'1978-09-03','Died in the first Viscount crash, passenger on the plane shot down in the Urungwe district. Most of the survivors were murdered by ZIPRA terrorists, Jeremy and his newly-wed bride, Karen (nee Leach), were returning from a week&#39;s honeymoon in the Kariba resort. They were both killed on impact with the ground. A memorial service was held for them in the Gwelo Baptist Church, the same church where they were married only two weeks earlier','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'J','648330','22','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',665,'2 Troop'),
