 (39021,39027,'Unknown','ROBERT NORMAN JAMES','CARRUTHERS','District Officer',200,'Internal Affairs',407,'3 Independent Company',973,'1978-11-28','Killed in action, in the Mount Darwin district, vehicle ambush in the Chiswiti area. Return fire from the vehicle resulted in two terrorists being killed','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood)','Zimbabwe',95,'GWERU CEMETERY',1033,'-19.45085','29.80413 ','Block 39, Section A, Tier K, Grave 17',NULL,'R N J','114666','23','Gweru (Gwelo)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (39022,39028,'Unknown','RAYMOND VIVIAN JAMES','CARRUTHERS','Lieutenant',334,'Southern Rhodesian Air Force',890,'3 Independent Company',973,'1952-12-14','Died in Military Aircraft Accident, when Auster J5 # SR 53 struck a cable across the Hunyani river, south of Salisbury.','ref. "Pride of Eagles" - History of the Rhodesian Air Force 1920 - 1980 by B Salt','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE AREA CEMETERY',2874,NULL,NULL,'Block 39, Section A, Tier K, Grave 17',NULL,'R V J','114666','25','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (39023,39029,'Unknown','DAVID ASTON','CARSHALTON','Trooper',581,'Grey Scouts',351,'B Trp',1940,'1976-08-27','Killed in action, in a contact in the  Chiredzi area, Op Repulse,  gun shot wound to head. While tracking about 70 terrorists, they were ambushed and he was killed in the initial firefight.','Ref  &#39;Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr JRT Wood). Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'CHIPINGE CEMETERY',529,NULL,NULL,'Block 39, Section A, Tier K, Grave 17',NULL,'D A','PR66139','26','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
 (39024,39030,'Unknown','GARY RONALD','CARTER','Flight Sergeant',257,'Rhodesian Air Force',614,'7 Sqdn.',1530,'1979-09-26','Died in Aircraft Accident, in Alouette III # R5705 which struck power lines near Lake Alexander during Operation Thrasher. They were flying as decoys during an assault on Chimoio base in Mocambique.','ref. "Pride of Eagles" - History of the Rhodesian Air Force 1920 - 1980 by B. Salt. Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'BULAWAYO (WEST PARK) CREMATORIUM',388,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'G R','6479','26','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
