 (39028,39034,'Unknown','PETER JOHN','CASWELL','Temp Captain',569,'Rhodesian Army Education Corps',617,'1st Battalion',524,'1978-12-01','Died in a vehicle accident, collision with a train on the Birchenough Bridge road, on the outskirts of Fort Victoria. He was flung from the vehicle and broke his neck.','Ref  &#39;Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr JRT Wood). Amendments from Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'P J','781187','20','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
 (39029,39035,'Unknown','CELESTINO','BAROPAYI','Private',429,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'1st Battalion',524,'1975-08-31','Killed in action, gunshot wound, in the Umfurudzi Wild Life Area, Shamva, Op Hurricane.','ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'C','645270','27','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',22,'"E" Coy.'),
 (39030,39036,'Unknown','ROBERT HUGH','CERFE','Corporal',166,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'3 Independent Company',973,'1978-03-18','Killed in action, operating from the old police camp in Nyamaropa, Op Thrasher, a stick of four encountered a very large group of CTs. In the ensuing engagement, and in spite of Cpl Cerfe&#39;s desperate pleas for help over the radio, the stick was overrun and only the MAG gunner, having run out of ammunition, managed to escape, returning to base a couple of days later. Cpl Rob Cerfe and Privates Elson Makonde and Jacob Nkomo were all killed','A Gifford High School old boy. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'R H','106161','27','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',22,'"E" Coy.'),
 (39031,39037,'Unknown','ANDREW','CHAIT','Sergeant',492,'Special Air Service',895,'"C" Sqdn.',22,'1977-03-24','Killed in action, in an attack on Chioco in Tete Province, Mocambique. Shot while preparing to throw a grenade at a machine gun position.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'A','XR5153','27','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',22,'"E" Coy.'),
 (39032,39038,'Unknown','EMMANUEL','CHAKA','Private',429,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'1st Battalion',524,'1976-06-13','Killed in action, in Operation Hurricane, gun shot wound. From Terence Murphy RhAF chopper pilot "I was flying a G-car in a Fire Force. 15 insurgents had been reported and we went to find them. They found me! We were circling a specific area while the Fire Force commanders sorted out a plan, and, as I flew over some rocks the aircraft came under intense small arms fire and was hit a number of times. At least we now knew where they were! Unfortunately a soldier of 1 Bn RAR sitting next to me was badly   wounded. We stripped him of his machine gun and ammunition, landed the remaining troops in the contact area, and sped off to the medical facility at base some minutes flying away. Alas, Private Emmanuel Chaka was found to be dead on arrival. The aircraft had sustained several hits and the engineers wanted to patch up the aircraft there and then, but, displaying a brave front not reflecting how I felt inside - we refueled and immediately went back to the action. I was glad to find it was just about over when I rejoined!"','ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated',NULL,'E','646317','19','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',22,'"E" Coy.'),
