 (39140,39146,'Unknown','GEORGE WILLIAM','CLARKE','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'Support Commando, 1st Battalion',3125,'1977-05-15','Killed in a contact near Rogogo Airfield, between Mrewa and Inyanga. He died of his wounds while being casavaced by helicopter to Mtoko.','George was from California and quite Californian in style and manner always smiling. He was a Vietnam veteran having served in the U.S. Marine Corps. George was in the battle of Hue city. George was in RLI Intake 156. Ref  &#39;Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr JRT Wood). Ref Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981, by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'African Section',NULL,'G W','728197','28','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
