 (39149,39155,'Unknown','AIDEN JAMES','COLMAN','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1979-09-06','Killed in action, shot down in Mozambique (at Mapai). Believed to have been carrying explosives to be used in Operation Uric and hit by a RPG7 or AAA., in Aerospatiale SA3330 Puma C #164. Also killed was the SAAF aircrew and 14 Rhodesian soldiers.','Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Mozambique',54,'Buried at the crash site near Mapai (Rail), Mozambique by the local population',401,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'A J','730092','22','Ohio',646,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',635,'1 Commando'),
