 (39169,39175,'Unknown','GARY CAETANO','CROUCH','Corporal',166,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'9th Battalion',1718,'1977-03-07','Killed in action, by a landmine in the Rutenga area, Op Repulse.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated at Warren Hills',NULL,'G C','PR45902','19','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',639,'Mortar Troop'),
 (39170,39176,'Unknown','JEREMY MARK','CROW','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1979-09-06','Killed in action, shot down in Mozambique (at Mapai). Believed to have been carrying explosives to be used in Operation Uric and hit by a RPG7 or AAA., in Aerospatiale SA3330 Puma C #164. Also killed was the SAAF aircrew and 14 Rhodesian soldiers.','No additional information known at this time','Mozambique',54,'Buried at the crash site near Mapai (Rail), Mozambique by the local population',401,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'J M','123929','19','Bulawayo',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',635,'1 Commando'),
