 (39173,39179,'Unknown','BRIAN NOEL','CUTMORE','Sergeant',492,'Rhodesian Air Force',614,'7 Sqdn.',1530,'1979-01-02','Killed in action, Air Operations in Alouette III #R5170 which had a mid-air collision with #R5701 near Selukwe, during Operation Grapple','ref. "Pride of Eagles" - History of the Rhodesian Air Force 1920 - 1980 by B. Salt. Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Post War grave in CWGC care',NULL,'B N','111580','63','Free State',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',532,'INTAF'),
 (39174,39180,'Unknown','FRANCISCO DUARTE','DA COSTA','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1976-11-15','Died of wounds, gunshot wound in a contact, Battle of Hill 31, Msasa Tribal Trust Lands, Mutasa, Op Thrasher. He was shot by a lone terrorist running away from the sweep-line. He was casevaced to Ruda and then Umtali.','Recently arrived from Portugal. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Portugal',65,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Post War grave in CWGC care',NULL,'F D','728075','31','Free State',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',643,'3 Commando, 11 Troop'),
 (39175,39181,'Unknown','PERCIVAL WILLIAM','JACOBSON','Trooper',581,'Special Air Service',895,'1st Battalion',524,'1961-06-12','Died in Military Vehicle Accident. Percy and his unit were travelling back from manoeuvres in the Brecon Beacons when their troop carrier rolled over.  Several of the other men had injuries, but Percy the most serious, he sustained a fractured skull. He was taken to Atkinson Morley Hospital (specialists in brain injury) in Wimbledon, and 24 hours later he died.','Son of Max Jacobson and Ima Violet Heberle. Brother of Ernest and Charmain in South Africa. Not on Armed Forces Memorial. Arrived from Durban, South Africa on Carnarvon Castle 29 January 1960. A professional engineer by trade and earned his degree at Witwatersrand University.','United Kingdom',90,'WIMBLEDON (GAP ROAD) CEMETERY',2898,NULL,NULL,'Post War grave in CWGC care',NULL,'P W','2382909','27','Surrey',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',643,'3 Commando, 11 Troop'),
 (39176,39182,'Unknown','NICOLAU ANTONIO','DA SILVA-CHALHEIROS','Rifleman',462,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'1st Battalion',524,'1976-05-17','Died of wounds, gunshot wounds, in a vehicle ambush on the Ft Victoria / Beit Bridge road, Nuanetsi District. da Silva was driving the lead vehicle in a 5-vehicle convoy when they came under heavy rocket, machine gun and rifle fire. His vehicle took most of the hits, killing B.J. Edwards and wounding da Silva. da Silva refused help from his platoon commander stationed next to him, and continued to drive out of the ambush zone.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CEMETERY',1062,NULL,NULL,'Post War grave in CWGC care',NULL,'N A','PR91132','22','Harare (Salisbury)',6,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',6,'"A" Coy.'),
