 (39202,39208,'Unknown','BARRY MAURICE','DENNIS','Private',429,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'1st Battalion',524,'1967-07-03','Died on active service','Dennis would most certainly not be his surname, but his first name. His surname is unknown. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated at Warren Hills',NULL,'B M','R44158','51','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',179,'Army'),
 (39203,39209,'Unknown','ANDRE','DENNISON','Major',343,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'2nd Battalion',898,'1979-06-03','Died in Friendly Fire Incident, Dennison and others were in the pub of the Zimbabwe Ruins Hotel when it came under CT attack. He reacted with two others from RAR and two from BSAP. One of the policemen heard a noise in front of him and opened fire, hitting Dennison','ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated at Warren Hills',NULL,'A','781030','51','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'MLM Awarded 23 September 1977; BCR Awarded 9 February 1979 - "He was awarded the BCR, as a result of his actions in a contact in October 1978. Despite having a shattered femur and bleeding heavily, he refused to be casevaced and continued to direct the fight. His bravery and dedication was far beyond the normal call of duty"; MFC (Ops) Awarded 31 March 1978 - "For dragging a wounded comrade, under heavy fire, out of a cave where a CT had established himself"',6,'"A" Coy.'),
