 (39253,39259,'Unknown','ANDREW JAMESON','DU TOIT','Second Lieutenant',475,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'3 Independent Company',973,'1979-12-27','Died of wounds, bullet wound in a contact in the Inyanga area, Op Thrasher. Various sticks had been deployed in the commercial wattle plantations in the area. Gus&#39; stick had gone into a plantation workers&#39; compound when they came under mortar and small arms fire from the nearby forest. As Gus was running across the edge of the forest in a clearing that carried electricity pylons, he was fatally wounded. He died during the helicopter casevac flight to hospital','Intake 163. A Prince Edward School old boy. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Non CWGC grave in CWGC care - date of death is buried date',NULL,'A J','V5047','24','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'Awarded for 15 November 1976 in the battle of "Hill 31" in the Honde Valley against a gang of 40 terrorists of which 32 were accounted for',635,'1 Commando'),
