 (39575,39581,'Unknown','CHRISTOPHER FRANCIS','LANG','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1979-06-04','Killed in action, at Chivinge in the Tete Province, Mocambique during Operation Chamber. This was an attack on the Frelimo / ZANLA base on the Luia River. They were met by fierce resistance from Frelimo troops, and during the attack, Lang, Lance Corporal Frans Nel and Corporal Peter "Doc" Rice were shot and killed.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Crem. Niche',NULL,'C F','728892','20','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',635,'1 Commando'),
