 (39707,39713,'Unknown','DAVID CARL','TAYLOR','Pilot Officer',414,'Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve',638,'139 Sqdn.',332,'1941-11-23','Died of injuries, received in aircraft accident, Blenheim Z7275 crashed during training on 22/11/41, died next day of his injuries.','Son of Lewis Taylor, of Johannesburg, South Africa. A talented violinist, he won an overseas scholarship at the Royal Academy of Music. In 1939, he is listed as a Professor of Music living in Banstead. The Royal Academy of Music still present the David Carl Taylor award. A.R.A.M. Professor, Royal Academy of Music, London. Of South Africa. ***Jewish','United Kingdom',90,'NORWICH CEMETERY',1831,NULL,NULL,'Sec. 54. Grave 147.',NULL,'D C','102613','31','Norfolk',1,'Awarded 25 March 1977 - "Success in a fire force action in April 1976 was attributed to his initiative, personal courage and leadership qualities"',15,'"C" Coy.'),
