 (40066,40072,'Unknown','COLIN GRAHAM','NEASHAM','Trooper',581,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1979-09-06','Killed in action, shot down in Mozambique (at Mapai). Believed to have been carrying explosives to be used in Operation Uric and hit by a RPG7 or AAA., in Aerospatiale SA3330 Puma C #164. Also killed was the SAAF aircrew and 14 Rhodesian soldiers.','No additional information known at this time','Mozambique',54,'Buried at the crash site near Mapai (Rail), Mozambique by the local population',401,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'C G','123027','26','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'Medal awarded 18 April 1978',635,'1 Commando'),
 (40067,40073,'Unknown','JOHN','VAN EYSSEN','Private',429,'Cape Corps',251,'1st',515,'1921-07-16','Died of pulmonary tuberculosis and heart failure','Son of Mrs. C. A. van Eyssen, of O&#39;Kiep, Namaqualand','South Africa',72,'CAPE TOWN (PLUMSTEAD) CEMETERY',463,'-34.02633','18.4764 ','Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'J','608','26','Western Cape',1,'***Accepted by CWGC for War Grave Status & burial site under investigation',635,'1 Commando'),
