 (40069,40075,'Unknown','EWART FRANCOIS','NEL','Lance Corporal',311,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1979-06-04','Killed in action, at Chivinge in the Tete Province, Mocambique during Operation Chamber. This was an attack on the Frelimo / ZANLA base on the Luia River. They were met by fierce resistance from Frelimo troops, and during the attack, Lang, Lance Corporal Frans Nel and Corporal Peter "Doc" Rice were shot and killed.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'E F','726466','26','Western Cape',1,'***Accepted by CWGC for War Grave Status & burial site under investigation',635,'1 Commando'),
 (40070,40076,'Unknown','FRANS JACOBUS','NEL','Trooper',581,'Special Air Service',895,'"C" Sqdn.',22,'1977-11-23','Killed in action. Shot in the head while advancing in a sweep line against ZANLA at Chimoio during Operation Dingo.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'KAROI MAIN CEMETERY',1252,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'F J','727434','20','Western Cape',1,'***Accepted by CWGC for War Grave Status & burial site under investigation',635,'1 Commando'),
 (40071,40077,'Unknown','JAN ANDRIES','NEL','Warrant Officer Class II',595,'Selous Scouts',760,'4 Troop',1154,'1976-06-26','Killed in action, in a contact, gunshot wound while trying to clear a double storey house at Mapai, during Operation Long John','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CREMATORIUM',1063,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'J A','724447','30','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'Medal awarded 17 December 1976',635,'1 Commando'),
 (40072,40078,'Unknown','PIETER JACOBUS STEPHANUS','NEL','Sergeant',492,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'6 Independent Company',1411,'1979-06-16','Died in Freak Accident, while trying to disarm an RPG rocket for a souvenir, in the barracks at Inyanga, Op Thrasher','ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'MUTARE CEMETERY',1740,'-18.97303','32.64875 ','Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'P J S','119582','21','Manicaland Province',1,'Medal awarded 17 December 1976',635,'1 Commando'),
