 (40074,40080,'Unknown','ROBERT GEORGE','NELSON','Senior Aircraftsman',484,'Rhodesian Air Force',614,'7 Sqdn.',1530,'1977-05-18','Killed in action, air ops in Alouette III #R3042. Aircraft was hit by groundfire during Operation Grapple in the Gokwe Area and caught alight. Although the pilot managed to land the chopper, Nelson apparently jumped from the aircraft before it landed and died on impact.','ref. "Pride of Eagles" - History of the Rhodesian Air Force 1920 - 1980 by B. Salt. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'R G','6526','21','Manicaland Province',1,'Medal awarded 17 December 1976',118,'Air Force'),
