 (40202,40208,'Unknown','DANIEL','COTTLE-GREEN','Second Lieutenant',475,'London Regiment',441,'22nd Bn.',756,'1917-02-25','Killed in action, bullet to the head, during action across the Tigris. Having only joined his unit the day before.','Son of Robert Cottle-Green, of 20 Kinver Road, Sydenham, ex-chairman of the Pretoria Club, South Africa. Born Pretoria, South Africa. His brother Robert Cottle-Green also died in service. He is commemorated on his brother&#39;s headstone in France.','Iraq',36,'BASRA MEMORIAL',163,'30.41163','47.54582 ','Panel 41.',NULL,'D','103738','21','Harare (Salisbury)',646,'Awarded while Sgt. 31 March 1978 -  "He displayed initiative and bravery of the highest order. He personally accounted for 14 CT kills and 8 captures, including high ranking commanders". He was also recommended for Rhodesia&#39;s highest award, the Grand Cross of Valour.',457,'attd. Machine Gun Corps (Infantry)'),
