 (40205,40211,'Unknown','NEVILLE ALAISTER','POWELL','Major',343,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1979-02-12','Killed in action, as a passenger on the second Viscount civilian airliner shot down by ZIPRA terrorists using a SAM 7.','Major N.A. "Spike" Powell MBE WB WKhm(G) was 3 Commando&#39;s 2 IC during Operation Cauldron in 1968. Major Powell&#39;s last appointment was Officer Commanding RLI Base Group. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated. Memorial stone in the Athlone Cemetery, Bulawayo',NULL,'N A','780573','24','Bulawayo',1,'Awarded while Sgt. 31 March 1978 -  "He displayed initiative and bravery of the highest order. He personally accounted for 14 CT kills and 8 captures, including high ranking commanders". He was also recommended for Rhodesia&#39;s highest award, the Grand Cross of Valour.',457,'attd. Machine Gun Corps (Infantry)'),
