 (40366,40372,'Unknown','KENNITH RICHARD','SMITH','Lance Corporal',311,'Special Air Service',895,'"C" Sqdn.',22,'1974-06-08','Died of wounds, received in a landmine explosion near Chimoio, Mozambique. Lost his leg and died of complications (fatty embolism in bloodstream) in Salisbury Central Hospital','From Australia. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'K R','6335','23','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',659,'1st Troop'),
 (40367,40373,'Unknown','MALCOM H','SMITH','Corporal',166,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'1st Battalion',524,'1977-03-11','Killed in action, in a contact in the North East Operational Area, near St Barbara&#39;s Mission, enemy group was moving in the opposite direction on the same path system (probably going back to Mozambique via Honde Valley), when they bumped into one another. A burst of automatc fire at close range caught Malcom in the face killing him instantly. The man behind him, Petrus Botha, was hit in the throat and died','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - crash site coordinates are: S22 06&#39; 48.2" E31 39&#39; 12.1"',NULL,'M H','PR63399','23','Harare (Salisbury)',1,'***Not yet accepted for War Grave Status by CWGC, need service file',15,'"C" Coy.'),
