 (40396,40402,'Unknown','GARY DOUGLAS','SUMMERS','Rifleman',462,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'1 Independent Company',88,'1977-06-01','Accidental death, in the Binga district, Op Tangent. Gary had been acting as a radio relay on Mt Tundazi in the Siabuwa TTL, Binga District, Op Tangent, across the valley from the BSAP base. It was reported that a fire had started by accident, and whilst trying to put out the fire, Gary slipped and fell over the edge.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered - Location of crash site Mozambique S18 30 19.5 E33 00 16.3',NULL,'G D','PR11028','28','Bulawayo',1,'LG Sup 2 June 1962 - "Her Majesty',612,'Signal Sect.'),
