 (40468,40474,'Unknown','ARTHUR STOCQUELL','TOPHAM','Sergeant',492,'Rhodesian Armoured Car Regiment',615,'"A" Sqdn.',9,'1978-11-07','Killed in action, in a landmine blast near Chipinga, Op Thrasher. He was sitting in the turret of a Ferret Scout Car, busy with checking deserted farms in the area.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Buried in Mrewa',NULL,'A S','73548','25','Unknown',1,'Awarded 13 October 1978 - "He was involved in 35 contacts in which 170 CTs were killed. This included 29 parachute deployments. In a contact on 27 June 1978, under very heavy fire, he went to the rescue of his wounded machine gunner. He accounted for 2 CTs, but in the follow up he was fatally shot".',179,'Army'),
