 (40470,40476,'Unknown','LOVEMORE','TOTOHWIYO','Private',429,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'2nd Battalion',898,'1978-12-29','Died on active service','ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Buried in Mrewa',NULL,'L','660798','19','Bulawayo',1,'Awarded 13 October 1978 - "He was involved in 35 contacts in which 170 CTs were killed. This included 29 parachute deployments. In a contact on 27 June 1978, under very heavy fire, he went to the rescue of his wounded machine gunner. He accounted for 2 CTs, but in the follow up he was fatally shot".',179,'Army'),
 (40471,40477,'Unknown','ALBERT KNIGHT','TOURLE','Lieutenant',334,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'2 Independent Company',636,'1972-04-09','Died in Animal Attack, attacked by a lion at Bumi, Kariba, whilst camped on the shores of Lake Kariba. A lioness appeared out of the darkness and attacked, biting him in the neck. The lioness disappeared into the dark but, before the men could grab their weapons, the lioness returned for another attack, before retreating again into the night. Died later from his injuries but, his comrades did manage to get him to a doctor before he died','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Buried in Mrewa',NULL,'A K','780768','32','Bulawayo',1,'His BCR citation states that it was for gallantry and leadership in action. Despite a faulty radio in a contact, he still managed to direct his troops, accounting for 6 CTs himself. He showed complete disregard for his own safety under conditions of extreme danger',179,'Army'),
 (40472,40478,'Unknown','RONALD JOHN','TRAVERS','Corporal',166,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1977-12-18','Killed in action, in the Mangwende Tribal Trust Lands, Lomagundi District, Op Hurricane. They were busy clearing caves in the area when he received fatal gunshot wounds from a RPD.','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Buried in Mrewa',NULL,'R J','725838','32','Bulawayo',1,'His BCR citation states that it was for gallantry and leadership in action. Despite a faulty radio in a contact, he still managed to direct his troops, accounting for 6 CTs himself. He showed complete disregard for his own safety under conditions of extreme danger',646,'2 Commando'),
