 (40476,40482,'Unknown','THOMAS ARTHUR CHARLES','TRODDYN','Sapper',469,'Rhodesian Corps of Engineers',621,'7 Squadron',1533,'1980-02-20','Killed in action, landmine explosion while busy clearing mines near the Nyamasanzdura River.','Born in Wales. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','United Kingdom',90,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'Cremated. His ashes were returned to Wales.',NULL,'T A C','728901','32','Unknown',1,'For actions or awarded 4 September 1979',6,'"A" Coy.'),
