 (40551,40557,'Unknown','GODFREY JAMES GLANVILLE','WEBBER','Second Lieutenant',475,'Rhodesian African Rifles',613,'1st Battalion',524,'1977-09-07','Killed in action, ambush in the Gwanda area, Op Tangent. Webber and four trackers followed the spoor of terrorists for four days after they had abducted a fellow RAR soldier. They had entered a village where they were ambushed','An Umtali Boys High School old boy. ref. "Rhodesian African Rifles Roll of Honour" by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'UNKNOWN CEMETERY',2572,NULL,NULL,'RCB section, grave 1767',NULL,'G J G','781165','23','Bulawayo',1,'***Submitted for War Grave Status to CWGC, awaiting acceptance',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (40552,40558,'Unknown','BARRY CHRISTOPHER','WEINMANN','Flight Lieutenant',253,'Rhodesian Air Force',614,'4 Sqdn.',1151,'1974-04-14','Killed in action, air operations in Trojan #R3427, in Mozambique. Shot down by anti-aircraft fire, north of Cabora Bassa.','Son of John Francis Freeley and Freda Freeley (nee Welensky). Born Isle of Man, United Kingdom. Adopted by Hans and Eva Weinmann on 7 July 1950 and his name changed to Barry Christopher Weinmann. Husband of Ellie Weinmann (later remarried to Peter Woolcock). Father to Anita Dunsdon, of Durban and Leanne Brayshaw, of Vietnam. ***Email from daughter Anita 3 March 2017. ref. "Pride of Eagles" - History of the Rhodesian Air Force 1920 - 1980 by B. Salt. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'GWERU CEMETERY',1033,'-19.45085','29.80413 ','RCB section, grave 1767',NULL,'B C','4173','28','Gweru (Gwelo)',1,'***Submitted for War Grave Status to CWGC, awaiting acceptance',15,'"C" Coy.'),
