 (40562,40568,'Unknown','DEON McALASTAIR','WHITE','Rifleman',462,'Rhodesia Regiment',610,'10th Battalion',195,'1976-10-30','Died of wounds, received in action on the 28th Oct, gunshot wound to the head. He killed six of the enemy in this contact while drawing enemy fire away from the rest of his section','ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CREMATORIUM',1063,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered. Possibly buried at the crash site.',NULL,'D M','PR99392','20','Harare (Salisbury)',15,'***Submitted for War Grave Status to CWGC, awaiting acceptance',15,'"C" Coy.'),
 (40563,40569,'Unknown','PETER CYRIL O&#39;BRIEN','WHITE','Temporary Sergeant',571,'Rhodesian Light Infantry',627,'1st Battalion',524,'1976-02-28','Killed in action, gunshot wound in a contact at Chibara Hills, Mt Darwin, Op Hurricane.','Sgt. Peter White was engaged to RWS Dawn Losper (nee Doughty) and was tragically killed 6 weeks before their scheduled wedding. ref. "Rhodesian Roll of Honour" by P. Geldenhuys (Roll compiled by Dr. J. R. T. Wood). Amendments from "Rhodesian Combined Forces Roll of Honour 1966-1981", by Adrian Haggett and Gerry van Tonder.','Zimbabwe',95,'HARARE (WARREN HILLS) CREMATORIUM',1063,NULL,NULL,'Body not recovered. Possibly buried at the crash site.',NULL,'P C O','725494','24','Harare (Salisbury)',650,'Earned his BCR for tracking a gang of terrorist 12 Kilometres and accounting for 6 of them. His BCR citation states he showed outstanding qualities of leadership, tactical skills, tracking ability and personal bravery',650,'1 Commando, 2 Troop'),
